ALCHEMY_BASE_ALCHEMY_TRAINING:
### Alchemy Training
When you learn Alchemy, gain proficiency with alchemist’s supplies.
If you already have proficiency with alchemist’s supplies, choose one Mortal Realm Alchemy talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent.
You also gain the following base abilities:
Alchemy Check;
Pill Forging;
Field Formula;
Reagent Stock.

ASH_TAL_CREMATION_PRISON:
#### Cremation Prison - Unique Ash Talent
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Range: 90 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 6 CP
Choose one creature.
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save:
Restrained;
cannot take Reactions;
cannot gain Temporary HP;
healing received is halved;
take 2d8 Fire damage and 2d8 Necrotic damage at the start of each turn;
repeat the saving throw at the end of each turn, ending the effect on a success.
Successful Save: Take 2d8 Fire or Necrotic damage and cannot gain Temporary HP until the start of its next turn.

BEASTMASTERY_BASE_BEASTMASTERY_TRAINING:
#### Beastmastery Training
When you learn Beastmastery:
gain proficiency in Wisdom (Animal Handling);
if already proficient, choose one Beastmastery talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
choose one Beastmastery Package: Rider or Tamer. You may later gain the other Package through Extra Beastmastery Package.
Beastmastery Packages

BLACKSMITH_BASE_BLACKSMITH_TRAINING:
### Blacksmith Training
When you learn Blacksmith:
gain Smith’s Tools proficiency or one alternate artisan’s tool proficiency as described above;
gain the Read the Flaw ability;
gain the Set the Workpiece ability;
gain the Hammer the Mark ability;
choose one Mortal Realm Blacksmith talent for which you meet the prerequisites.

BLACKSMITH_BASE_READ_THE_FLAW:
### Read the Flaw
Action Type: Multi-Mode
Timing Detail: Action or 1 minute
Split Review Decision: single_combat_action_plus_procedure_variant
Recommended Factory Realization: procedures=ONE_MINUTE_EXAMINATION
Range: Touch or reach
Target: One legal workpiece
Cost: None
Study one workpiece.
Make an Intelligence check using Smith’s Tools against a DC set by the GM. If the workpiece is part of a creature’s equipment, the DC is normally the creature’s Armor Class or your Blacksmith Save DC, whichever is higher.
On a success, learn two of the following:
whether the object is damaged;
whether the object is nonmagical, magical, or artifact-level;
whether the object is poorly made, ordinary, fine, masterwork, spiritual, or anomalous;
one material used in the object;
whether the object has a hidden flaw;
whether the object has been repaired before;
whether the object is under an active magical or sphere effect;
whether the object is suitable for a Blacksmith talent you know;
what kind of tool, furnace, or material would help improve it;
whether the object is resisting your work.
If you spend 1 minute instead of an Action, also place 1 Forge Mark on the workpiece on a successful check.
You may use Read the Flaw without a check on a nonmagical object you own, made, or have worked on for at least 10 minutes.

BLOOD_BASE_BLOODSENSE:
#### Bloodsense
When you learn the Blood sphere, you gain Bloodsense.
You sense exposed blood, fresh wounds, and meaningful living circulation within 60 feet.
You know:
the direction of Bloodied creatures;
whether a visible creature is injured;
whether blood was spilled nearby within the last hour;
whether a corpse likely died from blood loss;
whether an obvious Blood Sample belongs to the same creature as another sample you have already studied. Bloodsense does not automatically reveal Invisible creatures unless blood has been freshly spilled or another talent says otherwise.

BRUTE_BASE_IMPACT_COLLISION:
#### Impact Collision
Some Brute talents cause an Impact Collision.
An Impact Collision occurs when forced movement would carry a creature into:
a wall;
a solid object;
another creature;
a Barrier;
another obstacle that cannot be crossed.
Unless a talent says otherwise:
the moving creature stops in the nearest legal space;
collision damage is Bludgeoning damage;
a creature may collide only once during one shove sequence;
an unattended object takes the same collision damage when appropriate;
artifacts, Formation cores, and Realm-defining structures may resist or require a separate check.

DISEASE_BASE_DIAGNOSE_THE_SICKNESS:
#### Diagnose the Sickness
Action Type: Action
Range: Touch, or 30 feet if you can clearly perceive the target
Target: One creature, corpse, object, patch of terrain, sample, wound, room, or obvious contamination source
Duration: Instantaneous
Cost: None
You read the signs of disease and hostile biological or spiritual patterns.
You learn whether Disease is present and one of the following facts:
whether the infection is ordinary, magical, spiritual, alchemical, demonic, or unknown;
whether the target carries any of your Contagion Tokens;
whether the target is Sickened;
whether the infection appears contagious in the current scene;
whether the condition is worsening;
whether ordinary medicine might help;
whether quarantine is recommended;
whether the target is an active carrier, passive carrier, or merely contaminated.
If you spend 1 CP when using Diagnose the Sickness, learn three facts instead of one.
Diagnose the Sickness does not automatically reveal the exact creator, exact cure, hidden Secret techniques, full disease history, every carrier nearby, or the safest treatment plan.

DREAMS_BASE_DREAM_SEED:
#### Dream Seed
A Dream Seed is a symbolic impression planted in one creature’s subconscious.
A Dream Seed is not a visible mark.
It does not provide tracking, exact-square knowledge, or automatic detection.
Unless a talent says otherwise:
a Dream Seed on an awake unwilling creature lasts until the start of your next turn;
a Dream Seed on a willing or sleeping creature lasts for 1 hour;
a creature may bear only one of your Dream Seeds at a time;
a Dream Seed allows you to use Seed talents on that creature;
a Dream Seed ends if a talent consumes it. A sleeping creature does not automatically wake when a Dream Seed is planted.

FORMATIONS_BASE_FORMATION_TRAINING:
#### FORMATION TRAINING
When you gain the Formations sphere, gain proficiency with one of the following if you do not already have it:
Arcana;
Investigation;
Religion;
Survival;
Calligrapher’s Supplies;
Cartographer’s Tools;
Mason’s Tools;
Tinker’s Tools.
You also gain a basic formation kit worth 50 gp.
Choose one Basic Pattern from the Basic Pattern list. You know that pattern.

GLASS_BASE_FAULTLINE_MARKS:
#### Faultline Marks
A Faultline Mark is the moment when pressure reveals where a line wants to break.
You can have a number of Faultline Marks active at one time equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
When you would create a Faultline Mark beyond this limit, choose one existing mark to end.
A Faultline Mark lasts until the end of your next turn unless a talent says otherwise.
You may place a Faultline Mark when one of the following happens:
your Faultline Strike hits;
your Glass Shard hits;
a creature damages your tempered Glass Surface;
a creature attacks you while your body, armor, or shield is your tempered Glass Surface;
a creature attacks through, across, or against a Glass Surface you created or tempered;
a creature willingly moves across Shattered Glass Terrain you created;
a creature touches, breaks, or relies on a Glass Surface you control;
a talent explicitly places a Faultline Mark.

HARVESTING_GATHERING_BASE_HARVEST_LOTS_A:
### Harvest Lots
A Harvest Lot is a sealed, usable portion of raw material.
Examples include:
a bundle of medicinal herbs;
a spirit fruit;
bark curls from a sacred tree;
sealed dew from moon grass;
a fungus cap harvested at the correct hour;
powdered mineral scraped from a vein;
venom in a waxed ampoule;
beast gall, horn, claw, hide, bone, scale, silk, shell, or blood;
a low-grade beast core;
a jar of spirit soil;
resin, incense wood, or aromatic root;
petals, seeds, pollen, or bitter leaves.
A Lot must come from a source that exists in the scene, downtime, market, sect field, wilderness route, or strategic project. This sphere does not create Lots from nothing.

HARVESTING_GATHERING_BASE_READ_THE_SIGN:
### Read the Sign
Action Type: Multi-Mode
Timing Detail: Search or Study action, or 10 minutes of field examination
Split Review Decision: single_combat_action_plus_procedure_variant
Recommended Factory Realization: procedures=TEN_MINUTE_FIELD_EXAMINATION
Range: 60 feet for obvious signs; 1 mile during wilderness survey; special talents may extend this
You examine plants, soil, tracks, insects, wind, dew, beast leavings, mineral seams, spirit pressure, local taboos, and terrain memory.
Make a Gathering Check. The GM sets the DC by rarity, concealment, danger, and how much time you spend.
On a success, learn up to three facts:
whether useful materials are present;
approximate rarity;
whether the material is ripe, immature, spoiled, cursed, diseased, guarded, trapped, or spiritually unstable;
the safest obvious method of harvest;
whether the source can survive a careful harvest;
whether the material is compatible with Alchemy, Medicine, Crafting, Beast Taming, Formations, Talismans, or another system;
one obvious environmental danger connected to the harvest.
On a failure, you learn only one incomplete fact. On a failure by 5 or more, the GM may give a misleading impression, reveal the source to a guardian, or cause the source to begin spoiling.

HARVESTING_GATHERING_BASE_TRAINING_AND_T:
### Training and Tools
When you learn this sphere, gain proficiency with one of the following:
herbalism kit;
Nature;
Survival;
Medicine;
land vehicles;
an appropriate artisan’s tool such as woodcarver’s tools, mason’s tools, or cartographer’s tools.
If you already have the chosen proficiency, choose one Mortal Realm Harvesting and Gathering talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent.
You also gain a basic gatherer’s kit if starting equipment is being assigned by class or background. A gatherer’s kit includes a small sickle, pruning knife, digging hook, cord, waxed paper, cloth wraps, small jars, simple gloves, and a field ledger.

IMBUEMENT_BASE_READ_THE_VESSEL:
#### Read the Vessel
Action Type: Multi-Mode
Timing Detail: Study action or 1 minute of examination
Split Review Decision: single_combat_action_plus_procedure_variant
Recommended Factory Realization: procedures=ONE_MINUTE_EXAMINATION
Range: 30 feet, or touch for hidden internal properties
Target: One creature, object, weapon, armor, tool, construct, or special vessel
Cost: None
You study a Vessel’s surface properties and qi-response. Make an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma check using Arcana, Insight, Investigation, Medicine, or an appropriate tool proficiency against a DC set by the GM, usually 10 for mundane objects, 15 for active equipment, or the target’s Cultivation Save DC for supernatural vessels.
On a success, learn two of the following:
whether the Vessel is currently affected by a Mandate;
one property the Vessel can receive safely;
one property the Vessel resists;
whether the Vessel is mundane, magical, spiritually awakened, construct-like, soul-bound, or artifact-grade;
whether an item has a suppressed or active magical bonus;
whether a creature has an active body, mind, speed, weight, sense, speech, or resistance enhancement;
whether the Vessel would suffer backlash if imbued carelessly.
Read the Vessel does not reveal a full stat block, secret technique, owner identity, command word, hidden curse, or artifact history unless the GM decides the check is exceptional.

JESTER_BASE_JESTER_TRAINING:
### Jester Training
When you learn Jester:
gain proficiency in Charisma (Performance), Charisma (Deception), or Dexterity (Acrobatics);
if already proficient in all three, choose one Jester talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
choose one Mortal Realm Punchline talent for which you meet the prerequisites.

POISON_BASE_APPRAISE_THE_VENOM:
#### Appraise the Venom
Action Type: Action
Range: Touch, or 30 feet if you can clearly perceive the target
Target: One creature, corpse, object, wound, food, drink, weapon, sample, patch of terrain, or visible contamination source
Duration: Instantaneous
Cost: None
You read toxic traces, venom patterns, corrosion, and poisonous residue.
You learn whether poison is present and one of the following facts:
whether the poison is ordinary, alchemical, spiritual, demonic, plant-based, beast-based, mineral, corrosive, or unknown;
whether the target is Poisoned;
whether the target carries any of your Dose Marks;
whether the target has Toxin Burden;
whether the target suffers an Ingrained Toxin;
whether the poison appears immediately dangerous, delayed, or long-term;
whether an ordinary antidote might help;
whether the poison can be safely handled in the current scene;
whether the poison appears connected to Alchemy, Disease, Blood, Flowers, Death, or another sphere.
When you use Appraise the Venom on a poison, a poisoned target, or a sample, you may create an Antidote Profile for it.
If you spend 1 CP when using Appraise the Venom, learn three facts instead of one.
Appraise the Venom does not automatically reveal exact formulas, hidden creators, secret techniques, rare antidote recipes, or the full history of a toxin.

PRESSURE_POINTS_BASE_PRESSURE_POINTS_TRA:
### Pressure Points Training
When you learn Pressure Points:
gain proficiency in Wisdom (Medicine) or Dexterity (Sleight of Hand);
if already proficient in both, choose one Pressure Points talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
learn Precision Contact, Touch the Point, Numbing Point, and Reading Touch;
choose one additional Mortal Realm Point talent for which you meet the prerequisites.

PRESSURE_POINTS_BASE_READING_TOUCH:
### Reading Touch - Diagnostic
Trigger: You hit a creature with Precision Contact
Cost: None
Instead of applying a Point or Seal, read the body’s immediate response.
Choose one fact to learn:
whether the target is Bloodied;
whether the target is Poisoned, Paralyzed, Stunned, Unconscious, or suffering Exhaustion;
whether the target’s movement, speech, grip, sight, or breath is currently impaired;
whether the target currently benefits from a visible, audible, or physically expressed body-enhancing cultivation effect;
which of Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution appears most vulnerable to pressure-point disruption.
Reading Touch does not reveal a complete stat block, hidden identity, class features, Path, Realm, secret technique, or invisible effect.

PROTECTION_BASE_WARD:
#### Ward
A Ward is a temporary protected area.
Unless a talent says otherwise:
a Ward is centered within range;
a Ward remains where it was created;
a Ward uses Concentration unless made Persistent;
you may reduce its size when creating it;
you may maintain only one Ward at a time. Ward talents replace Barrier Ward unless the talent explicitly modifies Barrier Ward.

PUPPETRY_BASE_PUPPET_INITIATION:
### Puppet Initiation
When you learn Puppetry:
gain proficiency with Woodcarver’s Tools, Weaver’s Tools, Smith’s Tools, Tinker’s Tools, Calligrapher’s Supplies, or Sleight of Hand;
if already proficient with your chosen option, choose one Puppetry talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
create or designate one basic puppet vessel during a long rest;
learn Raise the Vessel, Puppet Strike, and the basic Tension Responses.

RADIANCE_TAL_HEAVEN_OPENING_JUDGMENT:
##### Heaven-Opening Judgment
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Range: 300-foot line, 10 feet wide
Cost: 12 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Release a colossal beam of pure Radiance.
Creatures inside make Dexterity saving throws.
Failed Save: Take 12d10 Radiant damage, become Dawnmarked until the end of your next turn, and cannot regain HP until the start of your next turn.
Successful Save: Take half damage and become Dawnmarked until the start of your next turn.
The beam ignores:
Half Cover;
Three-Quarters Cover;
ordinary concealment;
ordinary Darkness;
non-Legendary magical Darkness;
one ordinary Radiant Resistance;
up to 5 feet of ordinary wood, packed earth, or unworked stone.
Structures and unattended objects take double damage.
Heaven-Opening Judgment does not ignore Total Cover created by Legendary, Secret, artifact, Formation, or Realm-defining defenses unless a separate contest permits it.

RETRIBUTION_BASE_MARTIAL_FOCUS:
### Martial Focus
Retribution uses Martial Focus.
you may hold one Martial Focus at a time;
some talents expend Martial Focus;
expending Martial Focus is not an Action;
you cannot expend Martial Focus if you do not currently hold it;
if a talent says you regain Martial Focus, regain it only if it is currently absent.
Martial Focus represents breath, posture, attention, and the moment in which observation becomes certainty.

SECT_STEWARDSHIP_BASE_ACCEPTING_A_DUTY:
### Accepting a Duty
Once per Long Rest, you may declare a Duty.
A Duty is a clear non-combat obligation such as:
tend the lower herb terraces;
copy the new outer gate roster;
carry a sealed letter to the west courtyard;
arrange food for visiting disciples;
inspect the dormitory spirit lamps;
find why medicine stores are short;
escort a group of new outer disciples to orientation;
prepare the Mission Hall notices;
help a farmer settle a sect tithe dispute;
keep records for a gathering expedition.
While pursuing your Duty, you may spend Merit Dice on any non-combat ability check that directly advances it, even if the check is not tied to your chosen Sect Role.
When you complete the Duty, choose one reward with GM approval:
regain one spent Merit Die;
improve your Standing for one scene;
gain a minor favor from someone involved;
learn one useful rumor;
secure food, shelter, or basic supplies for yourself and up to five companions;
gain Advantage on one later Sect Check related to the same hall, person, or problem.
Completing a Duty should create a record, witness, favor, or obligation. The GM may deny the reward if no one knows, cares, or can verify that the duty was performed.

SECT_STEWARDSHIP_BASE_LEARNING_SECT_STEW:
### Learning Sect Stewardship
When you learn Sect Stewardship, choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma as your Sect Stewardship key ability.
Choose Intelligence if your stewardship is based on records, law, administration, scheduling, scripture catalogues, and logistics.
Choose Wisdom if your stewardship is based on reading people, judging duties, teaching juniors, noticing waste, and understanding sect customs.
Choose Charisma if your stewardship is based on face, introductions, mediation, patronage, public speech, and social leverage.
You gain proficiency in one of the following skills or tools:
History;
Insight;
Investigation;
Persuasion;
Religion;
Calligrapher’s Supplies;
Cook’s Utensils;
Herbalism Kit;
a tool appropriate to your sect duty, with GM approval.
If you already have proficiency in the chosen skill or tool, gain a flat +2 bonus to checks with it when the check directly concerns sect life, records, duties, ledgers, halls, missions, etiquette, or institutional logistics.

SECT_STEWARDSHIP_BASE_PETITIONING_THE_HA:
### Petitioning the Hall
As a non-combat Action during a scene, or during downtime, you may spend one Merit Die to petition an appropriate hall, superior, clerk, family, steward, or local authority for ordinary support.
Roll the Merit Die.
On a 1-2, you receive only the minimum help that your Standing demands.
On a 3-4, you receive useful help without extra trouble.
On a 5 or higher, if your Merit Die is large enough to roll that result, the support is unusually timely, discreet, generous, or well-matched.
Common petitions include:
a meal and safe sleeping space;
a clean set of robes or work clothes;
mundane tools for a duty;
permission to enter a public hall;
a basic map of the sect grounds;
an introduction to a clerk, senior, farmer, guard, or apprentice;
access to public notices;
use of a common room, kitchen, stable, outer library desk, or messenger channel;
temporary storage for ordinary goods;
a written receipt or witness statement.
Petitioning cannot obtain rare treasures, secret manuals, combat allies, high-ranking interventions, expensive materials, forbidden access, or anything the institution would not plausibly grant.

SECT_STEWARDSHIP_BASE_TAKING_A_PLACE:
### Taking a Place
When you finish a Long Rest, choose one Sect Role that reflects your current duty.
A role is not a class, job, or permanent rank. It is what you are currently known to be doing.
Common roles include:
Field Hand;
Kitchen Worker;
Messenger;
Dormitory Senior;
Archive Runner;
Medicine Hall Assistant;
Mission Board Reader;
Patrol Clerk;
Guest Attendant;
Stable Hand;
Furnace Cleaner;
Spirit Field Steward;
Lecture Scribe;
Dispute Witness;
Storehouse Aide;
Outer Gate Watcher;
Junior Instructor.
When a non-combat ability check directly relates to your chosen role, you may spend one Merit Die and add it to the check.
Examples:
A Field Hand adds Merit to notice spoiled seed, judge irrigation schedules, or organize harvest labor.
A Kitchen Worker adds Merit to feed a dormitory, identify ration theft, or use the kitchen gossip network.
A Lecture Scribe adds Merit to remember an elder’s teaching or copy a clean set of notes.
A Storehouse Aide adds Merit to find a legal substitute supply or detect forged requisitions.

SMOKE_BASE_SMOKE_TRACE:
#### Smoke Trace
A Smoke Trace is the residue left when a creature or effect passes through your smoke.
You can have a number of Smoke Traces active at one time equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
When you would create a Smoke Trace beyond this limit, choose one existing trace to end.
A Smoke Trace lasts until the end of your next turn unless a talent says otherwise.
Once per round, you may place a Smoke Trace on a creature, object, or 5-foot space when one of the following happens inside your Smoke Veil or through a line of sight that passes through your Smoke Veil:
a creature moves at least 5 feet;
a creature makes an attack roll;
a creature takes the Magic action, spends CP, uses a spell slot, or activates an explicitly supernatural technique;
a creature breathes, speaks, shouts, sings, or uses a breath weapon;
Fire damage is dealt;
an object burns, breaks, opens, closes, or is carried through the smoke;
a creature successfully Hides or becomes Invisible.
A creature does not need to know it has a Smoke Trace, but soot, scent, spiritual residue, or a faint smoke-thread may be visible to magical senses or close inspection.

TALISMANS_BASE_READ_THE_SCRIPT:
#### Read the Script
Action Type: Action
Range: 30 feet
Target: one visible talisman, seal, inscription, ward tag, formula page, or written Qi mark
Make an Intelligence check using Arcana, Investigation, Calligrapher’s Supplies, or another relevant proficiency.
On a success, learn one:
formula family;
approximate rank;
activation method;
whether it is cracked, unstable, reusable, or permanent;
whether it is connected to a Formation, corpse, spirit, door, object, or creature;
whether it is safe to touch.
Success by 5 or more reveals an additional fact.
Read the Script does not reveal secret formulae, hidden command words, full project schematics, or the identity of the crafter unless the evidence is present.

TAL_AIR_WIND_SENSE:
#### Wind-Sense - Breath
You learn to read disturbances in air.
You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice:
moving creatures that displace air within 30 feet;
hidden creatures that are not behind Total Cover and are moving within 30 feet;
incoming arrows, darts, needles, thrown weapons, or similar projectiles;
gas, smoke, or pressure changes;
whether a sealed door has air moving beneath or around it.
Wind-Sense does not reveal creatures that do not move, creatures behind airtight barriers, or creatures concealed by superior stealth, illusion, or Void techniques without an opposed check.

TAL_ALCHEMY_SMOKE_OF_RETURNING_BREATH:
### Smoke of Returning Breath - Medicine
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
When you use Medicinal Smoke, the target may also choose one:
end the Deafened condition;
end the Blinded condition if caused by smoke, powder, poison, or alchemical irritation;
stand from Prone without spending movement;
gain Advantage on the next Constitution saving throw it makes before the start of your next turn.

TAL_ATHLETICS_BODY_BEYOND_DISTANCE:
#### Body Beyond Distance
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Duration: 1 hour
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Enter a sustained travel state.
For the duration:
multiply overland travel pace by 10;
ignore ordinary exhaustion from travel;
traverse cliffs, rivers, forests, and broken terrain without slowing;
carry one willing creature of your size or smaller without reducing pace;
continue moving across ordinary water and vertical surfaces. Body Beyond Distance ends early if you enter combat, become Incapacitated, or stop moving for more than 1 minute.

TAL_ATHLETICS_COURT_OF_TEN_THOUSAND_STEP:
#### Court of Ten Thousand Steps - Martial Domain “The court did not contain roads. The cultivator made roads by stepping.”
Prerequisite: CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short rest
For the duration:
increase all movement Speeds by 20 feet;
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
stand from Prone without spending movement;
move through allied spaces normally;
climb ordinary surfaces without a check;
once per turn after moving at least 20 feet, regain Martial Focus;
once per turn when a hostile creature misses you, move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks. Court of Ten Thousand Steps ends early if you become Incapacitated.

TAL_ATHLETICS_FLASH_STEP:
#### Flash Step - Motion
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When you take the Dash Action, expend Martial Focus.
Teleport into your final destination without passing through intervening spaces.
The destination:
must be visible;
must be legal and unoccupied;
must be within the distance you could move through the Dash;
cannot cross a Dimensional Lock;
cannot cross a sealed boundary. Flash Step is cultivated motion approaching spatial transcendence.
It does not grant general Space-sphere control.

TAL_ATHLETICS_FLOWING_PURSUIT:
#### Flowing Pursuit - Motion
Prerequisite: CL 7+
When you move at least 20 feet toward one creature during your turn, choose one:
ignore Opportunity Attacks from that creature;
gain +2 AC against that creature until the start of your next turn;
add 5 feet to one jump during the movement;
move through one allied creature’s space without treating it as difficult terrain.

TAL_ATHLETICS_HEAVEN_TREADING_BODY:
#### Heaven-Treading Body
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Your cultivated motion no longer requires ordinary support.
Gain:
Fly Speed equal to land Speed;
Hover;
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
move across water, fragile surfaces, falling debris, and open air as though they were stable terrain;
reduce falling damage to 0. Heaven-Treading Body is visible as impossible physical mastery, pressure ripples, brief footholds, or another appropriate expression.

TAL_ATHLETICS_MERIDIAN_THREADING_DASH:
#### Meridian-Threading Dash - Focus
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When Coordinated Movement restores Martial Focus, choose one:
move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
stand from Prone without spending movement;
end one ordinary Grappled effect affecting you;
gain Advantage on your next Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check before the end of your next turn.

TAL_ATHLETICS_ONE_BREATH_TEN_THOUSAND_ST:
#### One Breath, Ten Thousand Steps
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Until the end of your turn
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Until the end of your turn:
take Dash as part of this Bonus Action;
take Dash again without spending an Action;
ignore Opportunity Attacks;
move through hostile spaces as though they were difficult terrain;
move across walls, water, air, and fragile surfaces;
each time you move at least 20 feet, regain Martial Focus;
apply any number of known Motion talents during the turn, but apply each Motion talent only once;
make one weapon attack or unarmed strike at any point during the movement. This technique does not allow movement through sealed barriers or Dimensional Locks.

TAL_ATHLETICS_STRONG_LUNGS:
#### Strong Lungs - Technique
Gain:
Advantage on saving throws against inhalation effects and suffocation;
Advantage on Constitution saving throws against exhaustion from forced march;
multiply normal breath-holding duration by your Proficiency Bonus.

TAL_ATHLETICS_SURE_GRIP:
#### Sure Grip - Technique Gain:
Advantage on Athletics checks made to climb or prevent falling;
as a Reaction, make an Athletics check to catch yourself or one creature within natural reach while falling;
never drop held objects merely because you become Frightened, Stunned, or Unconscious;
Grapples you maintain do not automatically end merely because you become Incapacitated.

TAL_ATHLETICS_TERRAIN_GLIDE:
#### Terrain Glide - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Shark Swim, CL 10+
Swim through soil, snow, loose earth, and sand as though they were water.
This counts as difficult terrain.
Terrain Glide does not grant:
sight through soil;
breath through soil;
movement through worked stone;
movement through metal;
movement through sealed barriers.

TAL_ATHLETICS_THE_STEP_TAKEN_BEFORE_INTE:
#### The Step Taken Before Intention
“The enemy decided to strike. The cultivator had already stepped beyond the meaning of the attack.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Flash Step, Heaven-Treading Body, hidden movement scripture
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You are targeted by an attack, trapped by an area effect, or would fail a Dexterity saving throw
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per week
Move up to your Speed.
This movement:
occurs before the triggering effect resolves;
does not provoke Opportunity Attacks;
may cross air, walls, water, hostile spaces, and fragile surfaces;
may use Flash Step once during the movement without spending additional Focus;
cannot cross sealed barriers or Dimensional Locks. After movement:
if you are outside the triggering attack’s reach, line, or area, the effect misses you;
otherwise, gain Advantage on the triggering Dexterity saving throw or impose Disadvantage on the triggering attack roll. Until the end of your next turn:
hold Martial Focus even after expending it;
increase all movement Speeds by 30 feet;
ignore ordinary Restrained and Grappled effects caused by physical contact.

TAL_AXES_MOUNTAIN_FELLING_AXE_BODY:
### Mountain-Felling Axe Body - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+, Hewing Intent
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 3 CP or 3 Stamina
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You become the weight behind the edge.
For the duration:
- your reach with axe weapons increases by 5 feet;
- your Bite limit increases by 2;
- once on each of your turns, when you hit with Hewing Strike, you may choose two Hewing riders instead of one;
- when you consume Bite, add your Proficiency Bonus to the damage or to one forced movement distance caused by that talent;
- you have Advantage on saving throws against being pushed, pulled, knocked Prone, disarmed, or frightened by non-Secret effects;
- your axe attacks against objects, barriers, and constructs ignore Resistance to nonmagical weapon damage and reduce Damage Thresholds by your Proficiency Bonus for that attack only.
This form does not let you cut through Domains, mountains, armies, or major formations without the appropriate talent or contest.

TAL_AXES_ROOT_HEWING_PASSAGE:
### Root-Hewing Passage - Woodcutter, Split
Prerequisite: CL 10+, Work-Axe Eye
You can open a path through living or dead material.
As an Action, spend 2 CP, 2 Stamina, or expend Martial Focus to hew a 10-foot-wide passage through one of the following within reach or within 10 feet:
- dense roots;
- brambles;
- wooden barricades;
- mundane undergrowth;
- bone thickets;
- waxy growths;
- rope tangles;
- non-Secret plant restraints;
- non-Secret physical webbing or net fields.
If the obstruction is mundane, the passage opens automatically if an axe could reasonably cut it. If it is cultivated, make an Axes Check against the effect's save DC. On success, open the passage until the start of your next turn. On success by 5 or more, open it for 1 minute.

TAL_AXES_WORK_AXE_EYE:
### Work-Axe Eye - Woodcutter, Utility
You can quickly read grain, knots, hinge points, rot, swollen wood, rope strain, barricade lashings, and weak structural joins.
You have Advantage on checks to:
- cut or break wooden objects;
- identify the weakest point of a door, cart, bridge, scaffold, barricade, tree, root mass, or palisade;
- estimate whether an axe can cut through an object before reinforcements arrive;
- harvest usable timber, resin, bark, stakes, or splints during travel.
When you deal damage to an unattended wooden object with an axe, add your Proficiency Bonus to the damage.

TAL_BARRAGE_BATTLEFIELD_SCAVENGER:
#### Battlefield Scavenger - Arsenal
When recovering non-firearm ammunition after combat, recover three-quarters of spent ammunition instead of half.
Draw one thrown weapon or piece of ammunition from:
the environment;
a corpse;
an unattended object;
a willing creature;
a living creature within reach. Draw it as part of the same Action used to attack with it.
##### Extracting from an Unwilling Creature
The creature makes a Dexterity saving throw.
Failed Save: Extract any number of embedded thrown weapons or ammunition pieces up to the amount present. The creature takes 1d4 Slashing damage per extracted piece.
Successful Save: The attempted attack Action is wasted because the ammunition was not secured.
If you possess an appropriate Scoundrel talent, apply one compatible Trick to the extraction.

TAL_BARRAGE_CASCADING_BARRAGE:
#### Cascading Barrage - Blitz
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When one Barrage attack reduces a creature to 0 HP or scores a critical hit, make one additional ranged weapon attack against a different legal target within range.
This additional attack:
is part of the Barrage;
does not require an Action;
does not add a positive ability modifier to damage unless Hammering Shots applies;
cannot trigger Cascading Barrage again.

TAL_BARRAGE_CEASELESS_AMMUNITION:
#### Ceaseless Ammunition - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When carrying at least 10 pieces of one nonmagical ammunition type, fire as many pieces of that ammunition as required without reducing the tracked amount during combat.
After combat:
do not retrieve more ammunition than you began with;
end with the same quantity you had when combat began. This is a cultivated supernatural effect.
Ceaseless Ammunition does not reproduce:
magical ammunition;
artifacts;
poisons;
consumable talismans;
explosive projectiles;
rare alchemical payloads.

TAL_BARRAGE_INTERCEPTING_SHOT:
#### Intercepting Shot
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A visible ranged weapon attack passes within 30 feet
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Make a ranged weapon attack against the incoming projectile.
If your attack roll equals or exceeds the triggering attack roll, choose one:
negate the attack;
reduce its damage by your weapon damage roll plus Proficiency Bonus;
redirect the attack into one legal unoccupied space within 10 feet of its original target. Intercepting Shot does not normally stop:
huge siege projectiles;
area effects;
beams;
intangible supernatural effects;
attacks with no physical projectile.

TAL_BARRAGE_MARTIAL_FOCUS:
#### Martial Focus
Barrage uses Martial Focus.
Unless a broader martial-sphere rule later replaces this wording:
you may hold one Martial Focus at a time;
some talents expend Martial Focus;
expending Martial Focus is not an Action;
you cannot expend Martial Focus if you do not currently hold it;
if a talent says you regain Martial Focus, you regain it only if it is currently absent. Base Sphere Ability

TAL_BARRAGE_MIXED_BARRAGE:
#### Mixed Barrage - Blitz
Replace the Bonus Action ranged attack from your Barrage with one:
melee weapon attack;
unarmed strike;
Shove attempt. Mixed Barrage supports hybrid styles such as:
thrown knife into close strike;
arrow into spear thrust;
dart into shoulder check;
sling stone into kick.

TAL_BARRAGE_MOBILE_BARRAGE:
#### Mobile Barrage - Blitz
Move up to 10 feet between your primary attack and your Bonus Action attack.
This movement:
does not provoke Opportunity Attacks from a creature hit by your primary attack;
must use a legal route;
does not increase your total movement for the turn.

TAL_BARRAGE_NEEDLE_RAIN_BURST:
#### Needle-Rain Burst - Volley
Prerequisite: CL 7+
Action Type: Action
Range: Weapon range
Area: 10-foot-radius sphere
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Spend five pieces of ammunition or five thrown weapons.
Creatures inside make Dexterity saving throws.
Failed Save: Take damage equal to two weapon damage dice plus your ability modifier.
Successful Save: Take half damage.
Needle-Rain Burst may use:
arrows;
bolts;
darts;
needles;
knives;
stones;
other appropriate projectiles.

TAL_BARRAGE_QUICK_DRAW_ARSENAL:
#### Quick-Draw Arsenal - Arsenal
Once per turn, draw one:
thrown weapon;
piece of ammunition;
quiver;
case;
sling stone;
needle bundle;
comparable projectile container without spending an Action.
You may stow one appropriate ranged or thrown weapon at the same time.

TAL_BARRAGE_REDIRECTION:
#### Redirection - Blitz Forgo the Bonus Action attack from your Barrage.
Choose one other weapon attack made as part of the Barrage.
Redirect its course once by up to 90 degrees.
This may:
strike around a corner;
bypass ordinary cover;
shoot through an opening;
exploit a reflective surface;
attack from an unexpected angle. Redirection requires a physically plausible route unless combined with another sphere or Forged Technique.

TAL_BARRAGE_SOVEREIGN_ARSENAL_INCARNATIO:
#### Sovereign Arsenal Incarnation
“The cultivator drew one weapon. The battlefield supplied the rest.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
For the duration:
create spiritual copies of ordinary nonmagical ammunition or thrown weapons you currently carry;
Barrage Bonus Action attacks add your ability modifier to damage;
Barrage may apply two different Blitz talents instead of one;
regain Martial Focus once per turn when one Barrage attack hits;
increase ranged and thrown weapon range by 60 feet;
ordinary projectiles return or reform at the end of your turn;
ignore Half and Three-Quarters Cover;
make ranged Opportunity Attacks against hostile creatures willingly moving more than 10 feet within normal range. Sovereign Arsenal Incarnation does not reproduce:
artifacts;
magical ammunition;
rare poisons;
explosive payloads;
talismans;
unique weapons.

TAL_BARRAGE_SPLITTING_RHYTHM:
#### Splitting Rhythm - Focus
Prerequisite: CL 7+
When Blitz Focus restores Martial Focus, choose one:
move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
draw or stow one weapon;
gain +2 AC against one ranged attack before the start of your next turn;
add your Proficiency Bonus to the next damage roll made with a thrown or ranged weapon before the end of your next turn.

TAL_BARRAGE_STAIR_SHOT:
#### Stair Shot - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Action
Requirement: Ammunition suitable for embedding into a surface
Spend 10 pieces of ammunition to create a temporary stair, bridge, or ledge of projectiles along a mostly vertical surface.
The structure:
extends up to 5 feet x CL;
may travel horizontally, upward, or downward;
cannot rise or descend more steeply than 45 degrees;
requires a wall, cliff, structure, large creature, or comparable surface;
supports ordinary movement at the GM’s discretion. Expend Martial Focus to create the structure as a Reaction, such as when catching a falling creature or building an emergency platform.
Stair Shot normally requires arrows, bolts, or comparable ammunition.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_BROAD_SKILLS:
#### Broad Skills - Tamer
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Tame may affect a non-humanoid creature with permanent Intelligence 4 or lower.
You have Disadvantage on the Animal Handling check if the creature is not a Beast.
Broad Skills may include suitable:
Monstrosities;
spirit beasts;
demon beasts;
giant insects;
unusual animals;
magical beasts. Broad Skills does not allow ordinary Tame to enslave a sapient creature.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_COURT_OF_FANG_AND_REIN:
#### Court of Fang and Rein - Martial Domain
“The beasts did not become soldiers. The soldiers finally learned to move like a pack.”
Prerequisite: CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short rest
For the duration:
##### You and Beast Allies
gain +10 feet Speed;
gain Advantage on checks against being shoved or moved;
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain created by natural terrain;
use the highest Passive Perception among allies within 60 feet;
move through allied spaces normally.
##### Once Per Turn After one Beast Ally hits, choose one different Beast Ally within 30 feet.
It may:
move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
take Help as a Reaction;
gain Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Court of Fang and Rein ends early if you become Incapacitated.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_MOUNTED_MANEUVERS:
#### Mounted Maneuvers - Rider
Your mount may take:
Dash;
Disengage;
Dodge;
Attack, but only to Shove. When you Shove while mounted, use the mount’s Strength modifier instead of your own.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_ONE_RIDER_ONE_BEAST:
#### One Rider, One Beast
Prerequisite: Rider Package, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You and one willing mount enter perfect battle rhythm.
For the duration:
use the higher Speed between you and the mount for both participants;
both gain +2 AC;
both gain Advantage on Dexterity saving throws;
both ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
neither provokes Opportunity Attacks from movement;
once per turn after either participant hits, the other may move 10 feet or make one Shove as a Reaction. You and the mount remain separate creatures with separate Actions and Reactions.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_PACK_ENCIRCLEMENT:
#### Pack Encirclement - Tamer, Pack
Prerequisite: Pack Attack, CL 10+
When at least two Beast Allies threaten one creature:
that creature cannot Disengage from those Beast Allies;
the first Beast Ally hitting it each round reduces its Speed by 10 feet until the start of its next turn;
when it attacks one Beast Ally, another Beast Ally within reach may move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_SHARED_SADDLE_RHYTHM:
#### Shared Saddle Rhythm - Rider, Focus
Prerequisite: CL 7+
When your mount takes Dash, Disengage, or Dodge while you ride it, choose one:
regain Martial Focus;
move 5 feet after the mount’s movement without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
grant the mount Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Use Shared Saddle Rhythm once per round.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_SOVEREIGN_PACK_MIND:
#### Sovereign Pack Mind
Prerequisite: Tamer Package, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
For the duration, communicate with Beast Allies within 1 mile through:
intent;
emotion;
simple images;
prey direction;
danger;
formation changes. Once per round when one Beast Ally within 120 feet makes an attack roll, saving throw, or ability check, grant:
+Proficiency Bonus
to the roll after seeing the result but before knowing the outcome.
Sovereign Pack Mind does not erase individuality.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_TRAMPLING_LINE:
#### Trampling Line - Rider
Prerequisite: Run Down, CL 7+
When your mount succeeds on Overrun, choose one:
push the target 10 feet;
knock the target Prone;
deal Bludgeoning damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
allow the mount to move 10 additional feet. Use Trampling Line once per turn.

TAL_BEASTMASTERY_WILD_SPEAKER:
#### Wild Speaker - Tamer
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Speak with ordinary Beasts.
This grants communication, not automatic friendship.
A Beast’s answers reflect:
intelligence;
temperament;
memory;
priorities;
fear;
hunger;
loyalty. At CL 10+, communicate with spirit beasts and demon beasts when they share a meaningful language of instinct, emotion, or spirit.

TAL_BERSERKER_ATAVISM:
#### Atavism - Adrenaline, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 7+
While active, when a supernatural effect cares about creature type, choose to count as:
your normal creature type; or
Beast.
Use whichever is more favorable.
Atavism does not grant:
beast anatomy;
Beast-sphere talents;
transformation;
senses;
natural weapons;
Beast Nature.

TAL_BERSERKER_BATTER:
#### Batter
A Batter is a Special Attack made with:
a melee weapon;
an unarmed strike;
a natural weapon;
a thrown weapon.
On a hit that deals damage, the target becomes Battered until the end of your next turn.
A Battered creature has no automatic penalty by itself.
Exertion talents exploit the opening created by Batter.

TAL_BERSERKER_BELL_RINGER:
#### Bell-Ringer - Exertion
When Batter deals damage, the target has Disadvantage until the start of your next turn on:
Intelligence saving throws;
Intelligence checks;
Concentration saving throws, including one caused by the Batter attack.

TAL_BERSERKER_COURT_OF_THE_UNBROKEN_WARP:
#### Court of the Unbroken Warpath - Martial Domain
“The battlefield did not become smaller. The warrior simply stopped recognizing obstacles as reasons to stop.”
Prerequisite: CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short rest
For the duration:
activate one Adrenaline talent without taking the normal -2 AC penalty;
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
gain Resistance to forced movement;
deal double damage to unattended objects and temporary Barriers;
after reducing a creature to 0 HP or critically hitting, move 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks;
once per turn when Batter hits a Battered target, regain Martial Focus.
Court of the Unbroken Warpath ends early if you become Incapacitated.

TAL_BERSERKER_CULTIVATION_SUNDER:
#### Cultivation Sunder - Exertion, Ruin
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When Batter deals damage, attempt to break one ongoing supernatural effect affecting:
the target;
an area you struck;
a Barrier you struck.
Choose one effect you can perceive.
If you cannot identify an effect, target the weakest eligible effect.
Compare Batter damage to:
10 + effect rank
For ordinary fifth-edition spells, use spell level as effect rank. For an effect without a listed rank, the GM assigns a rank from 0 to 9 using the closest spell-level equivalent.
Damage Meets DC: Suppress the effect for rounds equal to your Proficiency Bonus.Damage Exceeds DC by 5+: Dispel the effect.
Cultivation Sunder does not automatically dispel:
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
artifacts;
Formation cores;
Realm-defining transformations.
Those require a contested Cultivation Check or a specific rule.

TAL_BERSERKER_DEATHLESS:
#### Deathless
Gain:
Advantage on death saving throws;
when determining death from massive damage, treat maximum HP as three times its actual value;
if Stable at 0 HP, regain 1 HP after 1d4 minutes instead of 1d4 hours.

TAL_BERSERKER_DREADNOUGHT:
#### Dreadnought - Adrenaline
While active, gain Advantage on checks and saving throws made to resist or end:
Grappled;
Paralyzed;
Petrified;
Prone;
Restrained;
Stunned.

TAL_BERSERKER_HEAVEN_SHAKING_BATTER:
#### Heaven-Shaking Batter - Exertion, Ruin
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When Batter deals damage, choose one:
push the target 15 feet;
knock the target Prone;
deal additional Force damage equal to 2d8;
damage one unattended object or Barrier adjacent to the target for the same Batter damage;
create a 10-foot-radius patch of difficult terrain centered on the target.
If the target was already Battered, choose two different effects instead of one.

TAL_BERSERKER_JUGGERNAUT:
#### Juggernaut - Adrenaline
While active:
ignore difficult terrain;
your Speed cannot be reduced below its normal value by ordinary effects;
effects that reduce Speed to 0 still function if they explicitly immobilize, Grapple, Restrain, or seal movement.

TAL_BERSERKER_RUINOUS_TREAD:
#### Ruinous Tread - Ruin
Prerequisite: Shatter Earth, CL 5+
When leaving a space through ordinary movement, choose to break that ground.
The space becomes difficult terrain until cleared as an Action or repaired appropriately.
Ruinous Tread normally affects:
stone;
packed earth;
wood;
softer surfaces.
It does not automatically destroy:
metal floors;
Formation cores;
artifacts;
Realm-defining terrain.

TAL_BERSERKER_UNYIELDING_ADVANCE:
#### Unyielding Advance - Adrenaline
Prerequisite: CL 10+
While active:
cannot be moved unwillingly unless the source succeeds on a Strength check against your Berserker Save DC;
when a hostile creature enters your reach, move 5 feet toward it without provoking opportunity attacks;
when you take damage, gain Advantage on your next Strength (Athletics) check before the start of your next turn.

TAL_BERSERKER_WAR_GOD_INCARNATION:
#### War-God Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign engine of battle.
For the duration:
gain Resistance to all damage except Psychic;
activate two Adrenaline talents at once;
ignore the AC penalty from one active Adrenaline talent;
increase reach by 5 feet;
Batter damage gains +2d10;
when Batter hits, the target counts as already Battered for that attack’s Exertion;
once per turn after taking damage, move 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks;
when you reduce a creature to 0 HP, regain Martial Focus.

TAL_BRUTE_BATTLEFIELD_BOWLING:
#### Battlefield Bowling - Collision
Prerequisite: Dominoes, CL 7+
When Dominoes triggers, attempt the free shove against each creature in a contiguous line until one shove fails.
Each additional shove:
knocks Prone only;
cannot apply Brutal Shove damage;
cannot apply Manhandle talents;
cannot trigger Hammer unless the creature was already being moved by the original shove.

TAL_BRUTE_COURT_OF_THE_MOVING_MOUNTAIN:
#### Court of the Moving Mountain - Martial Domain
“The mountain did not chase its enemies. It merely decided that every direction led downhill.”
Prerequisite: CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short rest
For the duration:
gain Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks;
count as one size larger for Shove, Grapple, and Overrun;
reduce forced movement affecting you by 10 feet;
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain created by rubble, debris, and broken ground;
when Brutal Shove succeeds, move the target 5 additional feet;
once per turn when a creature collides with terrain or another creature, regain Martial Focus.
Court of the Moving Mountain ends early if you become Incapacitated.

TAL_BRUTE_CRUSHING_COLLISION:
#### Crushing Collision - Collision
Prerequisite: Hammer, CL 5+
When Hammer creates an Impact Collision, choose one:
the shoved creature makes a Constitution save or becomes Dazed until the start of its next turn;
the secondary creature makes a Strength save or falls Prone;
increase collision damage by your Proficiency Bonus;
break one ordinary unsecured object involved in the collision.
Dazed: This is a Brute-specific state, not a core 2024 condition. A Dazed creature cannot take Reactions and has Disadvantage on its next attack roll before the state ends.

TAL_BRUTE_FORTRESS_LINE_BREAKER:
#### Fortress-Line Breaker - Unique Brute Talent
Prerequisite: Living Battering Ram, CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Move up to your Speed in a straight or gently curving line.
During this movement:
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
attempt Overrun against each hostile creature in your path;
apply Brutal Shove to each successful Overrun;
apply one Manhandle talent to one successful Overrun;
deal double damage to unattended mundane objects in your path.
Stop if one Overrun fails or a barrier cannot be crossed.

TAL_BRUTE_GET_OVER_HERE:
#### Get Over Here
When you control one end of a tether attached to a creature, make shove attempts against it as though it were within reach.
Examples:
net;
lasso;
rope;
chain;
whip;
grappling hook;
tether technique.
On a success, move the target toward you instead of away.
When using Shove Aside, movement must still bring the target at least diagonally closer.
Apply Manhandle talents normally, but talents requiring natural reach function only if the target ends within natural reach.

TAL_BRUTE_MERIDIAN_LEVER_REVERSAL:
#### Meridian-Lever Reversal - Focus
Prerequisite: Shift Weight, CL 10+
When Shift Weight triggers, choose one:
shove the creature before resolving its missed attack’s remaining effects;
move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks after the shove;
redirect the creature into one adjacent legal space;
apply one Manhandle talent to the reaction shove by expending Martial Focus again.
You cannot expend Martial Focus twice unless you regained it before the second expenditure.

TAL_BRUTE_MIGHTY_HURL:
#### Mighty Hurl - Manhandle
Prerequisite: Throw, CL 7+
When using Throw:
increase additional movement from 10 feet to 20 feet;
move the target vertically, horizontally, or diagonally;
if the target falls, resolve falling damage normally;
if the target collides, Hammer applies if known.

TAL_BRUTE_MOUNTAIN_SWING_THROW:
#### Mountain-Swing Throw - Manhandle, Collision
Prerequisite: Mighty Hurl, CL 10+
When using Throw, choose one additional benefit:
increase forced movement by 20 feet;
throw one creature up to two sizes larger than you if you first succeed on the shove;
choose one 10-foot line the target passes through; creatures inside make Dexterity saves or fall Prone;
when the target collides, increase collision damage by 2d8.

TAL_BRUTE_MUSCULAR_SURGE:
#### Muscular Surge
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: Self
Target: Self
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: None
Requirement: You are not Exhausted.
Psych yourself into a larger expression of strength.
For the duration:
add your Proficiency Bonus to your Strength score only when determining carrying capacity;
add your Proficiency Bonus to your running long-jump distance;
count as one size larger when determining which creatures you may Shove or Grapple.
Immediately before you make one of the following Strength checks, you may end Muscular Surge without taking an action. You must choose before rolling. If you end it this way, you have Advantage on that check:
climb;
swim;
jump;
break a door;
break bonds;
overturn an object;
perform a comparable feat of strength approved by the GM.
This Advantage does not apply to an attack roll or a contested check.
When Muscular Surge ends for any reason, you gain one temporary level of Exhaustion for 10 minutes. That temporary level ends when the 10 minutes expire and does not remove any other Exhaustion you possess. You cannot activate Muscular Surge while you have any level of Exhaustion.

TAL_BRUTE_PERPETUAL_MOTION:
#### Perpetual Motion - Manhandle
Immediately make one additional shove against the same target.
This additional shove:
deals Brutal Shove damage normally;
cannot apply a Manhandle talent;
cannot trigger Perpetual Motion again.

TAL_BRUTE_ROOTED_STANCE:
#### Rooted Stance
Prerequisite: CL 7+
While holding Martial Focus:
gain Advantage on checks and saving throws against forced movement;
reduce forced movement affecting you by 5 feet;
count as one size larger when resisting Shove and Overrun.

TAL_BRUTE_SOVEREIGN_WEIGHT_INCARNATION:
#### Sovereign Weight Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become an incarnation of impossible leverage.
For the duration:
count as two sizes larger for Shove, Grapple, Overrun, carrying capacity, and Brute talents;
gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage;
gain Advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws;
Brutal Shove damage becomes 2d8 + Strength modifier;
once per turn when you successfully shove, move the target 10 additional feet;
Hammer collision damage gains +2d8;
ignore ordinary forced movement unless you choose to move.

TAL_BRUTE_TERRAIN_TRASHER:
#### Terrain Trasher - Terrain
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Grab a solid surface within reach and attempt to destroy it.
The surface must be:
a wall;
door;
floor;
barrier section;
comparable solid structure.
It cannot be:
loose dirt;
liquid;
iron or harder material without a specific enabling feature;
an artifact;
a Formation core;
a Realm-defining structure.
Make:
DC 10 Strength check
Success: Tear out a section approximately your own size.
Against a surface thicker than 1 foot, destroy only 1 foot of thickness per use.

TAL_BRUTE_THE_HAND_THAT_REPOSITIONED_HEA:
#### The Hand That Repositioned Heaven
“Heaven declared the mountain immovable. The cultivator placed one palm against it and asked whether Heaven intended to defend that opinion personally.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Court of the Moving Mountain, hidden mountain-moving scripture
Action Type: Action
Range: Reach or 30 feet against a tethered target
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature, unattended object, temporary Barrier, or ordinary structure section.
##### Creature
Make one Brutal Shove with Advantage.
On a success:
ignore ordinary size limits;
move the target up to 100 feet in one legal direction;
apply up to three Manhandle talents you know;
treat any collision as Hammer with +6d10 collision damage;
the target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Become Stunned until the end of your next turn.
Successful Save: Cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.
##### Object, Barrier, or Structure
Make a Strength check against a GM-set DC.
On a success, choose one:
tear open a major breach;
shift the object up to 30 feet;
collapse one ordinary section;
turn the object into rubble;
force open one sealed mundane passage.
The Hand That Repositioned Heaven does not automatically move or destroy:
artifacts;
Formation cores;
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
Realm-defining structures.
Those may still be contested or meaningfully damaged according to the GM.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_BLOODLESS_DEVOU:
#### Bloodless Devouring - Hunger
When you deal damage to a creature below half its maximum HP, you may spend 1 Devoured Essence.
Choose one:
regain HP equal to Proficiency Bonus + your Daemonic key ability modifier;
regain 1 CP or 1 Stamina;
gain Temporary HP equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus;
reduce Corruption by 1 if the creature was a demonic creature, undead, fiend, possessing entity, or active inner demon manifestation.
Use Bloodless Devouring once per turn.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_BORROW_THE_MONS:
#### Borrow the Monster’s Shape - Mutant
When you gain Devoured Essence from a beast, monstrosity, fiend, demon, aberration, or demonic beast, choose one minor trait you observed.
Until your next Long Rest, while Demon Seed is active, you may manifest one borrowed trait:
climbing claws, granting Climb Speed equal to half Speed;
swimming lungs, granting Swim Speed equal to half Speed;
hardened hide, granting +1 AC while unarmored or lightly armored;
night eyes, granting Darkvision 60 feet or +30 feet to existing Darkvision;
venom glands, adding Poison damage equal to Proficiency Bonus once per turn;
horns or fangs, increasing Unarmed Strike damage die by one step, to a maximum of d10.
You may hold only one borrowed trait at Mortal Realm.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_CONSUME_FEAR_RE:
#### Consume Fear, Refine Command - Tyrant
Prerequisite: Dread Appetite, CL 5+
When a creature fails a saving throw against your Dread Appetite, gain 1 Devoured Essence.
If the creature was already Frightened, you may choose one additional effect:
it cannot willingly move closer to one ally of your choice until the end of its next turn;
it drops one held mundane object if it fails a Strength saving throw;
it cannot take Reactions until the end of your next turn;
you move up to 10 feet toward it without provoking opportunity attacks from it.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_DAEMONIC_AUGMEN:
#### Daemonic Augment
Action Type: Special Trigger
Timing Detail: No Action, once per turn
Cost: 1 CP, 1 Stamina, or 1 Devoured Essence
Trigger: You use a sphere talent, weapon attack, Unarmed Strike, or Cultivation Attack that deals damage, imposes a condition, moves a creature, creates a zone, or forces a saving throw.
Twist the technique with daemonic hunger. Choose one:
add Proficiency Bonus to one damage roll;
impose Disadvantage on one Concentration saving throw caused by the triggering effect;
if the triggering effect moves a creature, increase the movement by 5 feet;
if the triggering effect creates Difficult Terrain, one creature that fails a save also cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn;
if the triggering effect deals Necrotic, Psychic, Fire, Poison, Acid, Force, or weapon damage, ignore ordinary Resistance to one of those damage types for that instance;
mark one damaged creature until the start of your next turn. The first time you damage the marked creature before the mark ends, gain 1 Devoured Essence.
Daemonic Augment may modify non-Daemonic sphere talents, but only once per turn. This is one of the main reasons the sphere is forbidden.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_DEMON_EMPEROR_I:
#### Demon Emperor Incarnation
Prerequisite: Inner Demon Incarnation, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP or 15 Devoured Essence
Use Limit: Once per Long Rest
You become the visible sovereign of your inner demon court.
For the duration:
gain Fly Speed 60 feet and Hover;
gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, Necrotic, Psychic, and Poison damage;
gain Advantage on saving throws against Frightened, Charmed, Poisoned, Grappled, Restrained, and Stunned;
Daemonic Augment costs no resource once per turn;
your first Daemonic talent each turn costs 2 fewer CP or Devoured Essence, minimum 0;
once per turn when you reduce a creature to 0 HP, regain 3 CP or 3 Stamina;
Demon Sovereign Aura is active without Concentration, using a 60-foot radius;
ordinary creatures of lower Realm that start their turn inside the aura must make a Wisdom saving throw or become Frightened until the start of their next turn.
When the incarnation ends, gain 2 Corruption.
If Corruption would exceed 10, the excess becomes Demonic Debt. The GM may spend Demonic Debt later to introduce tribulation distortion, inner demon trials, sect investigation, possession pressure, or enemies drawn by your scent.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_INNER_DEMON_INC:
#### Inner Demon Incarnation - Seed, Mutant
Prerequisite: Second Furnace Demon Heart, CL 10+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 8 CP or 8 Devoured Essence
Use Limit: Once per Long Rest
Let the demon seed partially incarnate.
For the duration:
Demon Seed is active and does not require its normal cost;
gain Fly Speed equal to walking Speed, but no Hover;
gain Resistance to Necrotic and Psychic damage;
your Daemonic Augment may be used twice per turn, but not on the same roll or effect;
when you gain Devoured Essence, gain one additional Devoured Essence, once per round;
your weapon attacks, Unarmed Strikes, and Cultivation Attacks count as magical;
you emit obvious daemonic signs.
When the incarnation ends, gain 1 Corruption.
If you ended the incarnation with 0 Devoured Essence, gain 1 additional Corruption.

TAL_DAEMONIC_CULTIVATION_SECOND_FURNACE_:
#### Second Furnace Demon Heart - Seed
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Your demon seed becomes a second furnace.
While Demon Seed is active:
increase your maximum Devoured Essence by Proficiency Bonus;
once per turn when you spend Devoured Essence, gain Temporary HP equal to Proficiency Bonus;
when you Overdraw, reduce the additional Corruption Save DC by 2;
if you start your turn with 0 CP or 0 Stamina, you may gain 1 Corruption to gain 1 Devoured Essence.

TAL_DEATH_BLACK_PROCESSION_ROAD:
#### Black Procession Road - Corpse, Ghost
Prerequisite: Deathly Passage, CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Range: 1 mile
Duration: 1 minuteConcentration: Required
Cost: 10 CP
You open a road between grave-signs.
Choose two locations within range that each contain at least one of the following:
corpse;
grave marker;
Ghost Lantern;
Death servant you control;
preserved remains;
battlefield death-site;
Mausoleum of Quiet Souls;
active Death Domain.
For the duration, you and willing creatures you designate may move from one point to the other by spending 10 feet of movement while adjacent to either point.
Hostile creatures cannot use the road unless you permit them. If a hostile Death, Space, Shadow, or Spirit effect contests the road, resolve with an opposed Cultivation Check.
The road cannot enter a sealed Barrier, consecrated prohibition, imperial tomb seal, or stronger ward unless overcome.

TAL_DEATH_DEATHLY_PASSAGE:
#### Deathly Passage - Corpse, Ghost
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 60 feet
Cost: 2 CP
You step through the nearest available grave-path.
Teleport to an unoccupied space you can see or sense within 5 feet of one of the following within range:
a corpse;
an undead creature;
a dying creature at 0 HP;
your Ghost Lantern;
a Death servant you control;
a grave marker, funerary tablet, or burial object bearing your Death mark.
You cannot pass through a sealed Barrier, consecrated boundary, or effect that blocks teleportation unless your Death cultivation overcomes it.

TAL_DEATH_DEATH_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
#### Death-Sovereign Incarnation - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Court of the Ninth Grave, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minuteConcentration: Not required
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You assume a sovereign deathly manifestation: a crown of funerary fire, a robe of ash, a halo of black tablets, a skeletal mandala, a procession of ancestor lamps, or a silent judge’s mask.
For the duration:
you gain Fly Speed 40 feet and Hover;
you gain Immunity to Necrotic damage;
you gain Resistance to Psychic damage and nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage;
Grave Sense range becomes 1 mile;
Withering Hand deals 6d10 Necrotic damage instead of its normal damage;
you may command Death servants you control within 1 mile, provided a grave Qi route, Ghost Lantern, corpse line, ancestral token, or Death Domain connects you;
once during each of your turns, you may use Withering Hand without using an Action;
when an enemy within 20 feet starts its turn, it makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failure, it takes 4d8 Necrotic damage and cannot regain HP until the start of its next turn. On a success, it takes half damage.
A creature takes damage from this aura only once per turn.

TAL_DEATH_GRAVE_SENSE:
#### Grave Sense
Action Type: Special Trigger
Timing Detail: No action; you may focus as an Action for more detail
Range: 30 feet
Cost: None
You can sense strong nearby death-signs.
You can detect the presence and direction, but not exact identity, of the following within range:
corpses;
undead;
dying creatures at 0 HP;
ghosts or lingering death echoes;
grave Qi;
recent violent death;
active Death sphere effects.
As an Action, you may focus on one death-sign you can sense and learn one of the following:
whether it is corpse, undead, ghost, dying creature, grave Qi, or active Death effect;
whether the death was recent or old;
whether a corpse has been preserved, desecrated, animated, or protected by a rite;
whether an undead creature appears bound, feral, willing, commanded, or self-willed;
whether a possession or soul-binding effect is present, if it is visible to Death Sense.
Grave Sense does not automatically reveal hidden creatures, invisible creatures, a complete stat block, the target’s Path, the target’s Realm, or private memories.
At CL 10, the range becomes 60 feet. At CL 15, the range becomes 120 feet.

TAL_DEATH_LAST_BREATH_WITNESS:
#### Last Breath Witness - Ghost, Rite
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A creature you can perceive within 30 feet drops to 0 HP or dies
Cost: 1 CP
You catch the final breath before it scatters.
Choose one:
learn the direction of the creature’s strongest killer, if that killer is within 1 mile;
learn one image, word, or emotion from the creature’s final moment;
prevent the corpse from rising as ordinary undead for 24 hours;
allow the dying creature to speak one brief sentence if it is not instantly destroyed;
gain Advantage on your next Death talent used on that corpse within 1 hour.
This talent does not compel truth, bind the soul, or preserve life.

TAL_DEATH_LEGION_OF_THE_RESTLESS_DEAD:
#### Legion of the Restless Dead - Corpse, Command, Forbidden
Prerequisite: Grave Formation, CL 15+
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 1 hour
Range: Battlefield, graveyard, ossuary, tomb complex, or mass-death site
Duration: 24 hours
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
You gather a strategic force of lesser dead.
The legion can do one of the following at strategic scale:
guard a tomb, city gate, road, valley, or battlefield;
dig, carry, build, or perform mass labor;
delay an enemy army;
assault a fortified position;
evacuate supplies or bodies;
patrol a region;
hold a ritual perimeter;
fight as a terrifying but temporary military force.
During an ordinary encounter, represent the legion with up to two Grave Formations. These formations count against your Death Control Limit only while in the encounter. Outside the encounter, the legion is a narrative-scale asset subject to terrain, morale of the living, rites, counter-necromancy, and available remains.
If the legion is made from unwilling dead, stolen corpses, or bound souls, this is one of the clearest forbidden expressions of Death.

TAL_DEATH_MAUSOLEUM_OF_QUIET_SOULS:
#### Mausoleum of Quiet Souls - Rite, Ghost
Prerequisite: Funerary Preservation, CL 15+
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 30 days
Cost: 15 CP and rare funerary materials worth at least 25,000 gp
You create a permanent funerary sanctuary, tomb-court, ancestor hall, ghost hospital, or silent mausoleum.
A Mausoleum of Quiet Souls may provide the following benefits within its boundaries:
preserve corpses indefinitely;
protect souls from ordinary possession, binding, and soul theft;
prevent ordinary undead from rising naturally;
provide a home for willing ancestor spirits;
grant Advantage on checks made to investigate death, conduct exorcism, or preserve remains;
support Death, Spirit Awakening, Formations, Radiance, Protection, and Karma projects;
suppress Forbidden Death talents unless the intruder overcomes your Cultivation Save DC;
allow you to use Speak with the Departed on properly interred dead without disturbing the corpse.
You may maintain a number of Mausoleums equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

TAL_DREAM_COURT_HALF_WAKING_MOON:
#### Court of the Half-Waking Moon - Dreams Domain
“The enemy remained awake. That was the first illusion.”
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 7 CP
The battlefield becomes a shared half-waking dream.
##### You and Allies
gain Advantage on saving throws against Charmed, Frightened, and Dream Sleep;
gain Resistance to Psychic damage;
may communicate through brief symbolic impressions;
may move through allied spaces;
gain Advantage on checks made to recognize Illusions and mental influence.
##### Enemies When an enemy starts its turn inside, it makes a Wisdom saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
become Drowsy until the start of its next turn;
take 2d8 Psychic damage;
have Disadvantage on its next attack roll;
have Disadvantage on its next saving throw against a Dreams talent;
reduce Speed by 20 feet until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.

TAL_DRUNKEN_STYLE_BENT_REED_RECOVERY:
### Bent-Reed Recovery - Sway
When you are knocked Prone, pushed, pulled, or moved against your will, you may use your Reaction to bend with the force.
Choose one:
reduce the forced movement by 10 feet;
move an additional 5 feet in the same general direction and do not fall Prone;
fall Prone but regain Martial Focus if you did not already have it.

TAL_DRUNKEN_STYLE_COLLAPSE_INTO_VICTORY:
### Collapse Into Victory - Counter
Prerequisite: CL 11+
When a creature hits you with a melee attack while it is Off-Rhythm from you, you may expend Martial Focus as a Reaction.
The attack still hits, but you reduce the damage by 2d10 + your Proficiency Bonus.
Then choose one:
the attacker falls Prone;
the attacker cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn;
you move up to 15 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from the attacker;
you make one Unarmed Strike using the Damage option against the attacker.

TAL_DRUNKEN_STYLE_EMPTY_CUP_STANCE:
### Empty Cup Stance - Sway
While you are holding Martial Focus and not wearing heavy armor, you gain the following benefits:
standing from Prone costs only 5 feet of movement;
squeezing does not impose Disadvantage on your Drunken Style attack rolls;
creatures Off-Rhythm from you do not gain Advantage on attacks against you from you being Prone unless they are within 5 feet of you;
when you take the Dodge action, you may use Reeling Step as part of the same Action.

TAL_DRUNKEN_STYLE_HEAVEN_TRIPS_OVER_YOU:
### Heaven Trips Over You - Chaos-Step
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Area: 60-foot Emanation from you
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Choose a number of hostile creatures in the area up to your Proficiency Bonus. Each chosen creature must make a Wisdom saving throw.
Failed Save: The creature becomes Off-Rhythm from you until the end of your next turn and suffers two effects of your choice:
falls Prone;
cannot take Reactions until the end of your next turn;
has Disadvantage on attack rolls until the start of your next turn;
moves up to 15 feet in a legal direction you choose;
cannot benefit from Advantage on attack rolls until the start of your next turn;
provokes no Opportunity Attacks from you or your allies when moved by this talent.
Successful Save: The creature becomes Off-Rhythm from you and cannot take Opportunity Attacks until the start of your next turn.

TAL_DRUNKEN_STYLE_NO_BEAT_REPEATS:
### No Beat Repeats - Rhythm
Prerequisite: CL 11+
Once per turn when you apply Off-Rhythm to a creature that was already Off-Rhythm from you, choose one:
extend the Off-Rhythm duration until the end of your next turn;
move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from that creature;
gain Advantage on the next Drunken Style attack you make against that creature before the end of your turn;
cause that creature to lose the benefits of Advantage on the next attack roll it makes before the start of your next turn.

TAL_DRUNKEN_STYLE_PALM_OF_THE_MISSING_BE:
### Palm of the Missing Beat - Rhythm
When you hit an Off-Rhythm creature with Broken-Rhythm Strike, expend Martial Focus.
The target must make a Wisdom saving throw.
Failed Save: Until the start of your next turn, the target loses one of the following, your choice:
its Reaction;
its Bonus Action on its next turn;
the ability to benefit from Advantage on attack rolls;
the ability to make Opportunity Attacks.
Successful Save: The target cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of your next turn.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_AMBIDEXTERITY:
#### Ambidexterity
When you make the extra attack of the Light property as a Bonus Action, you may expend Martial Focus to make that attack as part of the Attack action instead.
You may use Ambidexterity only once per turn.
Ambidexterity:
changes the action timing of the Light-property extra attack;
does not create an additional attack;
does not grant an additional Bonus Action;
does not move an extra attack granted only by the Dual Wielder feat;
does not stack with Nick to create another Light-property extra attack.
If Nick already moves your Light-property extra attack into the Attack action, you do not need to expend Martial Focus to do so.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_ASYNCHRONOUS_SWING:
#### Asynchronous Swing - Rhythm
While holding Martial Focus, when you make attacks with both weapons from your Qualifying Pair during your turn, choose:
the normal weapon damage die of either weapon; and
one damage type normally dealt by either weapon.
Until the end of the current turn, both weapons use the chosen normal weapon damage die and chosen damage type for their weapon attacks.
Asynchronous Swing does not copy:
Weapon Mastery properties;
weapon properties;
Reach;
magic-item bonuses;
extra damage dice;
curses;
attunement benefits;
effects that trigger only from one named weapon.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_COMBO_MANEUVERS:
#### Combo Maneuvers - Pair
When you would make your Paired Strike, replace it with one Unarmed Strike used only for its Grapple or Shove option.
Use the ordinary 5.5e rules for that Unarmed Strike.
In particular:
a Shove does not require a free hand;
a Grapple requires a free hand;
Combo Maneuvers does not allow a weapon to maintain a Grapple;
you may use Dual Draw or another legal rule to unequip a weapon before attempting the Grapple.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_DUAL_DRAW:
##### Dual Draw
Whenever you would equip or unequip one weapon as part of the Attack action or another rule, you may equip or unequip two one-handed weapons instead.
Equipping includes drawing or picking up a weapon. Unequipping includes sheathing, stowing, or dropping a weapon.
Dual Draw does not:
allow you to interact with unrelated objects;
reload a weapon;
activate a magic item;
exceed the number of hands you actually possess;
change whether a weapon is one-handed or Two-Handed.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_DUAL_OPPORTUNITY:
#### Dual Opportunity - Guard
Trigger: You make an Opportunity Attack while wielding a Qualifying Pair.
Use Limit: Once per round.
Make one melee weapon attack with each weapon from your Qualifying Pair instead of making one attack.
These attacks:
use the same Reaction that triggered the Opportunity Attack;
are Opportunity Attacks;
do not count as Paired Strikes;
cannot receive Pair talents unless another feature explicitly allows it.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_FOLLOWING_STRIKE:
#### Following Strike - Pair
When you make your Paired Strike, make one additional attack with your Answering Weapon as part of the same Bonus Action, or as part of the same Attack action if your Paired Strike was moved into that action by Ambidexterity or Nick.
Following Strike has the following restrictions:
use it only once per turn;
the original Paired Strike and the additional attack must target different creatures;
at least one attack you made with your Lead Weapon as part of the Attack action must target a third creature;
do not add a positive ability modifier to the additional attack’s damage unless another rule explicitly permits it;
the additional attack is not itself a Paired Strike;
you cannot apply another Pair talent to the additional attack.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_GREATER_BLADES:
#### Greater Blades - Rhythm
For the limited purpose of determining whether you can make the Light property’s extra attack and use Dual Wielding sphere features, you may treat a one-handed melee weapon that lacks the Two-Handed property as though it had the Light property.
Greater Blades does not:
add the Light property to the weapon for any unrelated feature;
add or change a Weapon Mastery property;
allow a Two-Handed weapon to qualify;
allow a weapon used in two hands to qualify;
grant proficiency with the weapon.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_MIXED_DEFENSE:
#### Mixed Defense - Guard
You may use a mixed weapon pair consisting of:
one one-handed melee weapon in one hand; and
one one-handed Ranged weapon or one melee weapon with the Thrown property in the other hand.
While wielding that mixed pair:
you do not have Disadvantage on ranged attacks with the paired Ranged or Thrown weapon solely because a hostile creature is within 5 feet of you;
the paired Ranged or Thrown weapon counts as a melee weapon for Balanced Defense and other Dual Wielding sphere requirements;
this does not cause the weapon to gain the Light property.
When you use a Ranged weapon from the mixed pair to make a melee attack:
treat it as an improvised melee weapon;
it deals 1d4 Bludgeoning damage on a hit;
add your Proficiency Bonus to the attack roll only if you are proficient with improvised weapons;
it has Reach for that melee attack and for Opportunity Attacks made with it.
A melee weapon with the Thrown property continues to use its ordinary melee profile and gains Reach while you wield it as part of a mixed pair.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_TANDEM_OFFENSIVE:
#### Tandem Offensive - Rhythm
While holding Martial Focus, when an attack made with your Lead Weapon as part of the Attack action hits a creature, compare the numeric magic-item bonuses to attack and damage rolls granted by your two wielded weapons.
Until the start of your next turn, your Answering Weapon may use the higher of those two numeric bonuses.
Tandem Offensive copies only a numeric magic-item bonus to attack and damage rolls. It does not copy:
Weapon Mastery properties;
weapon properties;
damage dice;
extra damage dice;
activated abilities;
charges;
curses;
attunement benefits;
sentience;
a named weapon’s unique effects.

TAL_DUAL_WIELDING_TWIN_WEAPON_TRAINING:
#### Twin-Weapon Training
When you learn the Dual Wielding sphere, gain Balanced Defense and Dual Draw.
##### Balanced Defense
While wielding a Qualifying Pair, gain a +1 bonus to AC.
For stacking purposes, treat this bonus as a Shield bonus:
you do not gain this bonus while wielding a Shield;
if another feature says its AC benefit does not stack with a Shield, it does not stack with Balanced Defense;
Balanced Defense does not count as wielding a Shield for any other purpose;
Balanced Defense does not grant Shield training or satisfy a prerequisite that requires a Shield.
An Unarmed Strike or natural weapon does not qualify unless a specific rule explicitly allows it.
##### Dual Draw
Whenever you would equip or unequip one weapon as part of the Attack action or another rule, you may equip or unequip two one-handed weapons instead.
Equipping includes drawing or picking up a weapon. Unequipping includes sheathing, stowing, or dropping a weapon.
Dual Draw does not:
allow you to interact with unrelated objects;
reload a weapon;
activate a magic item;
exceed the number of hands you actually possess;
change whether a weapon is one-handed or Two-Handed.

TAL_EARTH_MOUNTAIN_ROOT_BODY:
### Mountain-Root Body - Body, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Your body can carry Earth as a living foundation.
While you are touching a solid surface:
you count as three contiguous Foundation Spaces for your own Earth features;
you can be used as a legal origin point for Humble Wall, Earthbind Line, Sink the Wheel-Rut, and similar non-Projected Earth features;
you gain Resistance to damage from falling and from being crushed by earth, stone, or nonmagical rubble;
when you take the Dodge action, you may give one creature that misses you before the start of your next turn one Burden Mark.

TAL_EARTH_SINKING_FOOT_REBUKE:
### Sinking Foot Rebuke - Earth Response, Burden
When you spend a Burden Mark with Anchor Step or Drag Down, choose one additional effect:
the target cannot take the Dash action until the end of the current turn;
the target has Disadvantage on the next Dexterity saving throw it makes before the start of your next turn;
if the target is Prone, it must spend an additional 5 feet of movement to stand before the end of the current turn.

TAL_EARTH_TREMOR_COURT_HEARING:
### Tremor Court Hearing - Burden, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Tremor-Listening Palm, CL 10+
While touching a solid or earthen surface, use an Action to listen through a number of connected Foundation Spaces you created.
Until the start of your next turn, you know the location of creatures touching those spaces, and you can tell whether each creature is:
moving quickly;
standing still;
Prone;
carrying a heavy load;
burrowing;
flying but within 5 feet of the surface;
concentrating on a spell, sphere talent, or supernatural technique that produces physical vibration.
This does not reveal private thoughts, exact identity, or illusions that do not interact with weight or contact.

TAL_EARTH_VALLEY_THAT_RECEIVES_THE_ARMY:
### Valley that Receives the Army
Prerequisite: Court of Bearing Ground, CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Area: 120-foot-radius sphere centered on a point on the ground you can see, subject to Path restrictions
Duration: Concentration, up to 10 minutes
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Choose one battlefield, road, valley, courtyard, cave, gate approach, or similar area.
For the duration:
all nonmagical difficult terrain in the area becomes normal terrain for creatures you choose;
all normal ground in the area becomes difficult terrain for hostile creatures;
hostile creatures that Dash, fly upward from a surface, teleport out of the area, or force movement on another creature gain one Burden Mark;
when a hostile creature with a Burden Mark starts its turn in the area, choose whether it makes a Strength saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
Speed becomes 0 until the end of its turn;
it falls Prone;
it cannot take the Dash or Disengage action until the end of its turn;
one willing creature in the area gains Temporary HP equal to 2 x your Proficiency Bonus.
Successful Save: Its Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its turn.
This effect does not collapse buildings, bury armies, or create permanent terrain unless the GM frames it as a strategic project.

TAL_EARTH_WEIGHT_SEAL_STRIKE:
### Weight-Seal Strike - Burden
When you hit a creature with Weight-Seeking Clod or a melee attack while you are touching the same surface as the target, choose one:
reduce the target’s Speed by 5 feet until the start of your next turn;
the target cannot take the Jump action or benefit from a running jump until the start of your next turn;
the target has Disadvantage on the next check it makes to Shove or Grapple before the start of your next turn.
This effect is in addition to any Burden Mark you place.

TAL_FENCING_BIND_WEAPON:
##### Bind Weapon - Guard
When you win a Disarm attempt, you may bind the target’s object to your weapon instead of causing the target to drop it.
You may also bind a hand, natural weapon, or comparable attacking limb as though it were a held object.
While the bind lasts:
the target has the Grappled condition;
the bound object or limb cannot be used to make attacks;
you must remain within the reach of the weapon or Unarmed Strike used to establish the bind;
you cannot use the weapon or limb maintaining the bind to make attacks;
the bind ends if you become Incapacitated, release it at any time with no Action required, or move beyond the permitted reach.
If an object is bound, the target may release that object at any time with no Action required, ending the bind. Otherwise, the target may use its Action to make a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your Cultivation Save DC, ending the bind on a success.
Bind Weapon is a special form of Grapple. It does not require a free hand unless the weapon or Unarmed Strike used to establish the bind requires one.

TAL_FENCING_FOOTWORK:
##### Footwork - Footwork
Cost: Expend Martial Focus.
Move up to 10 feet. This movement:
requires no Action or Reaction;
may occur even when it is not your turn;
does not provoke Opportunity Attacks;
must end in a legal unoccupied space you can reach.
You may use Footwork after an attack is declared against you but before its attack roll is made. If you do, the triggering attack roll has Disadvantage. If your movement makes you an illegal target for the triggering attack, the attack misses instead.
You may also use Footwork after an effect that allows a Dexterity saving throw includes you as a target but before you make the saving throw. If your movement does not remove you from the effect, you have Advantage on the Dexterity saving throw.

TAL_FENCING_VACUUM_CUT:
##### Vacuum Cut - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Piercing Needle sphere, CL 5+
When you take the Attack action and make a melee weapon attack during the same turn that you draw or otherwise equip the weapon used for that attack, you may expend Martial Focus to extend that attack’s reach to 30 feet.
Vacuum Cut:
changes the reach of that single melee weapon attack;
does not turn the attack into a ranged attack;
does not allow the attack to pass through Total Cover;
does not automatically allow the attack to target a creature you cannot perceive;
may receive an Exploit if it otherwise satisfies the Exploit rules.

TAL_FLOWING_RIVER_BORROWED_MOMENTUM:
### Borrowed Momentum - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Once per turn when a creature is moved by one of your Flowing River talents, choose one:
move yourself 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from that creature;
grant one ally within 30 feet a 5-foot movement that does not provoke Opportunity Attacks from that creature;
add your Proficiency Bonus to the next damage roll you make against that creature before the end of your next turn;
reduce the creature’s Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn.

TAL_FLOWING_RIVER_NO_CENTER_UNDER_HEAVEN:
### No Center Under Heaven - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Your body becomes a moving answer with no fixed center.
For the duration:
melee attack rolls against you have Disadvantage unless you are Incapacitated;
you may use Flowing Response without spending your Reaction once per round;
when Flowing Response succeeds, move up to half your Speed instead of 5 feet;
this movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks from any creature whose attack, Grapple, Shove, or forced movement you avoided this round;
when you move through a hostile creature’s space using River Crossing Step, that creature must make a Dexterity saving throw or fall Prone.

TAL_FLOWING_RIVER_RIVER_BREAKS_THE_CHARG:
### River Breaks the Charge - Response
Prerequisite: CL 10+
You may use Flowing Response when a creature you can see willingly moves at least 20 feet in a straight or mostly direct line toward you and enters a space within your reach.
When you do, the creature makes a Dexterity saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
the creature falls Prone;
its movement ends immediately;
you move the creature 10 feet to one legal space adjacent to you;
you move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from the triggering creature.
Successful Save: The creature’s Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of the current turn.

TAL_FLOWING_RIVER_SOFT_BODY_HARD_FLOOR:
### Soft Body, Hard Floor - Response
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When a creature within reach fails a saving throw against one of your Response talents, choose one:
the creature cannot stand from Prone until the start of its next turn;
the creature’s Speed becomes 0 until the start of its next turn;
the creature cannot take the Dash Action until the start of its next turn.

TAL_FORCE_IMMOVABLE_ANCHOR:
### Immovable Anchor - Anchor Talent
A willing creature within 5 feet of yourself or one of your Pressure Anchors gains:
Advantage on saving throws and contested checks made to resist forced movement;
Advantage on saving throws and contested checks made to avoid falling Prone;
Advantage on checks made to resist a Shove or Overrun attempt.
A creature benefits from only one of your Immovable Anchors at a time.

TAL_FORCE_PRESSURE_STEP:
### Pressure Step - Unique Force Talent
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: Self
Cost: 1 CP
Release pressure beneath or behind your body.
Move up to 10 feet through a legal route.
This movement:
does not provoke opportunity attacks;
may move horizontally or vertically;
ignores nonmagical difficult terrain;
cannot pass through solid objects;
is not teleportation.
If you end this movement without support, you fall normally.

TAL_FORCE_WORLD_BRACING_INCARNATION:
### World-Bracing Incarnation
“The mountain did not lend the cultivator its strength. The cultivator reminded the mountain how to stand.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign answer to physical pressure.
Gain:
+3 AC;
Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, and Force damage;
Advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws against forced movement, falling Prone, collision, and physically traveling area effects;
use Counterpressure once per round without spending CP;
use Pressure Step once per turn without spending CP;
increase Impact damage to 6d10 Force or Bludgeoning damage;
increase the push caused by Impact by 10 feet;
increase the HP of Barriers you create by 5 x Proficiency Bonus.
World-Bracing Incarnation does not grant flight, teleportation, or immunity to nonphysical effects.

TAL_GLASS_CLEAN_BREAK:
### Clean Break
When you reduce a Glass Surface, fragile object, mirror, window, crystal, or mundane glass item to 0 HP, choose one:
create Shattered Glass Terrain in one 5-foot square adjacent to it;
place a Faultline Mark on one creature within 5 feet of it;
move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from one creature that saw it break.

TAL_GLASS_HELD_PANE_METHOD:
### Held-Pane Method
When you temper a shield, weapon, fan, staff, sleeve-weight, bracelet, ring, bowl, or other held object, it can serve as a Glass Surface for your Refraction Responses.
While holding the tempered object:
you may place a Faultline Mark on a creature that misses you with a melee attack;
you may use Turn the Angle on yourself even if the marked creature is not adjacent to another Glass Surface;
if the object is a shield, its transparent edge may provide the same Cover it normally would without blocking line of sight.

TAL_GLASS_INCARNATION_OF_THE_TRANSPARENT:
### Incarnation of the Transparent Fault
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 6 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Your body, breath, meridians, and immediate surroundings become a single transparent faultline.
For the duration:
your body is always a tempered Glass Surface;
you may maintain two additional tempered Glass Surfaces beyond your normal limit;
when a hostile creature within 30 feet hits you or an ally, place a Faultline Mark on it;
once per round, use one Refraction Response without spending a Reaction;
when you spend a Faultline Mark, choose one creature within 30 feet. That creature either gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus or takes Slashing damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
you have Resistance to Slashing and Piercing damage;
you cannot be Blinded while you are conscious.
This Incarnation does not automatically create free-floating panes. A Body Refiner remains a living pane unless another feature permits projection.

TAL_GLASS_PALACE_LENS_ARRAY:
### Palace Lens Array - Projected
Prerequisite: Raised Pane Scripture, CL 10+
When you create projected Glass Panes, you may arrange them as lenses rather than barriers.
Choose one lens benefit when you create them:
allies looking through the lenses ignore Half Cover from nonmagical objects;
hostile creatures attacking through the lenses take a -2 penalty on the first attack roll each turn;
a creature that teleports into or out of a space adjacent to a lens gains a Faultline Mark;
invisible creatures adjacent to a lens leave visible distortions until the start of your next turn.
A Body Refining cultivator may learn this talent only with external-projection permission.

TAL_GUARDIAN_ADAMANT_GUARDIAN_INCARNATIO:
### Adamant Guardian Incarnation
“The gate did not hold because it was made of stone. It held because I stood there.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Transform into a perfected defensive incarnation.
For the duration:
gain +4 AC;
gain Resistance to all damage except Psychic and Force damage;
gain Immunity to Prone;
become immune to forced movement unless you willingly allow it;
increase your melee reach by 5 feet;
gain one additional Reaction each round; this explicitly overrides the ordinary one-Reaction limit;
still use only one Reaction for any single trigger.
#### Shelter the Weak
At the start of each of your turns, choose a number of allies within 20 feet up to your Proficiency Bonus.
Until the start of your next turn, each chosen ally gains Resistance to the first instance of damage it takes.

TAL_GUARDIAN_BODYGUARD:
### Bodyguard — Rescue Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Interpose improves:
its range increases to 20 feet;
you may move up to 20 feet when using it;
gain Resistance to the triggering attack’s damage until that attack resolves.

TAL_GUARDIAN_COLD_IRON_CALL:
### Cold Iron Call — Resilience Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you would be affected by a supernatural effect that does not merely deal damage, you may reserve space in your Held Harm Pool equal to:
5 × the originator’s Proficiency Bonus
If the source has no listed Proficiency Bonus, use the Proficiency Bonus appropriate to its Challenge Rating or Cultivation Level. If neither is available, the GM assigns a reasonable value.
If you reserve the required space, delay the non-damaging portion of that effect until the end of your next turn.
The reserved space follows the same rules as Durable.
Cold Iron Call does not automatically delay:
damage;
an entire area of effect;
an effect already active before you were targeted;
a Domain;
a Secret Inheritance;
a major narrative calamity;
an effect the GM determines cannot meaningfully be carried inside one body.
A suitable removal effect may remove the delayed supernatural effect before it resolves.

TAL_GUARDIAN_DURABLE:
### Durable — Resilience Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you fail a saving throw against one of the following, you may reserve 10 points of empty space in your Held Harm Pool:
disease;
one level of Exhaustion;
poison;
Blinded;
Charmed;
Deafened;
Frightened;
Paralyzed;
Petrified;
Poisoned;
Restrained;
Stunned;
Unconscious.
If you reserve the required space, delay the effect until the end of your next turn.
The reserved space:
counts against your Held Harm maximum;
cannot be filled by damage;
cannot be cleared through healing;
is released when the delayed effect resolves or is removed.
An effect that would ordinarily remove the delayed condition may remove it from Durable before it resolves.
You may voluntarily release one Durable effect without spending an Action. It applies immediately.
Durable delays one effect, not the entire ability that caused it. Damage and other consequences resolve normally.

TAL_GUARDIAN_GUARDIAN_S_FOCUS:
### Guardian’s Focus — Focus Talent
Use Limit: Once per round
When one of the following occurs, regain Martial Focus if it is currently absent:
a creature Challenged by you is reduced to 0 HP;
you hit with a Patrol attack;
you successfully use Interpose;
you succeed on a Grapple or Shove attempt while Patrol is active.

TAL_GUARDIAN_INDOMITABLE:
### Indomitable — Resilience Talent
Prerequisite: CL 7+
Trigger: You are reduced to 0 HP
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Do not fall Unconscious from HP loss until the end of your next turn.
During that time:
you act normally;
you do not make death saving throws;
you may receive healing;
damage still affects you normally;
Held Harm still resolves normally.
If you remain at 0 HP when the effect ends, fall Unconscious and resume the ordinary rules for death saving throws.

TAL_ILLUSION_MINOR_ILLUSION:
#### Minor Illusion
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Area: One 5-foot cube
Duration: 10 minutes
Cost: NoneConcentration: Not required
Tags: Image, Figment
You create a minor illusion inside the area. Choose one of the following options:
a Small or smaller image;
a brief repeating sound;
a smell;
a simple apparent temperature change;
a simple texture that can fool casual inspection;
a superficial spiritual impression;
two minor sensory details that fit the same small scene, such as footsteps and a shadow, a whispered voice and the scent of smoke, or a bloody handprint and the smell of blood.
As a Bonus Action on your turn, you may move the illusion up to 5 feet within range or change one minor sensory detail.
Minor Illusion cannot deal damage, apply a condition, create Cover, block movement, block line of effect, maintain a complex conversation, convincingly mimic a detailed combatant, hide a large area, or create a perfect copy of a unique person or spiritual signature.
A creature can Study the illusion as described in this sphere’s rules.

TAL_IRON_FIST_BELL_RINGING_BODY_SHOT:
##### Bell-Ringing Body Shot - Meridian
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you hit an Opened creature with an Unarmed Strike, choose one:
the target has Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks until the start of your next turn;
the target cannot take the Dash action until the end of its next turn;
the target’s next attack roll before the end of its next turn deals reduced damage equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus.

TAL_IRON_FIST_BELL_TOWER_BODY:
##### Bell-Tower Body - Guard, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Body Conditioning, CL 10+
While holding Martial Focus and not wearing Heavy armor:
reduce Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage from nonmagical attacks by your Proficiency Bonus;
gain Advantage on saving throws against being knocked Prone;
when a creature hits you with an Unarmed Strike, natural weapon, or nonmagical melee weapon, it takes Bludgeoning damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

TAL_IRON_FIST_BREATH_EXTENDED_STRIKE:
##### Breath-Extended Strike - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
While holding Martial Focus, your Unarmed Strike reach increases by 5 feet.
When you expend Martial Focus before making an Unarmed Strike, your reach for that strike becomes 30 feet.
A Breath-Extended Strike may appear as:
compressed fist Qi;
a palm imprint crossing the air;
a whip-crack kick of force;
a dragon-shaped exhalation;
a visible ripple from your stance through the ground.
This is still an Unarmed Strike. It does not allow general telekinesis, object manipulation, grappling through walls, or sustained remote force.

TAL_IRON_FIST_DRAGON_STEP_CLINCH:
##### Dragon-Step Clinch - Form
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When a creature fails the saving throw against your Unarmed Strike’s Grapple option, you may maintain the grapple with a leg hook, shoulder pressure, elbow clamp, or body clinch instead of a free hand.
A body clinch follows these rules:
you may maintain only one body clinch at a time;
you cannot maintain a body clinch while Restrained, Prone, or Incapacitated;
your Speed is reduced by 10 feet while maintaining it;
the target has Advantage on checks made to escape unless it was Opened when the grapple began;
you may end the clinch at any time without spending an Action.
Dragon-Step Clinch supports knees, elbows, and close-body forms without replacing the Wrestling sphere.

TAL_IRON_FIST_EIGHT_GATE_DIAGNOSIS:
##### Eight-Gate Diagnosis - Meridian
Prerequisite: Medicine of the Closed Gate, CL 10+
As an Action, study one creature within 30 feet that you can perceive.
Make a Wisdom (Medicine), Intelligence (Investigation), or Cultivation Check against the creature’s Cultivation Save DC.
Success: Learn two of the following:
whether it is Bloodied;
whether it has Resistance to Bludgeoning, Force, or nonmagical physical damage;
whether it has immunity to Prone, Grappled, Stunned, or forced movement;
whether it is maintaining an ongoing bodily or martial enhancement;
which saving throw among Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution appears weakest.
Until the end of your next turn, your first Unarmed Strike against that creature has Advantage.

TAL_IRON_FIST_HAMMER_AND_ANVIL_RHYTHM:
##### Hammer-and-Anvil Rhythm - Sequence
Once per turn, when you hit the same creature with two or more Unarmed Strikes during your turn, choose one:
apply Open the Gate again to that creature;
extend the creature’s Opening until the end of your next turn;
regain Martial Focus if it is absent.

TAL_IRON_FIST_IRON_FIST_TRAINING:
##### Iron Fist Training
When you learn Iron Fist:
gain proficiency in Strength (Athletics), Dexterity (Acrobatics), or Wisdom (Medicine);
if already proficient in all three, choose one Iron Fist talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
choose Strength or Dexterity as your Iron Fist ability;
gain the Iron Fist Die;
choose one Mortal Realm Form talent for which you meet the prerequisites.

TAL_IRON_FIST_IRON_MERIDIAN_BODY:
##### Iron Meridian Body - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Your Iron Fist techniques become openly supernatural.
Gain the following benefits:
your Unarmed Strikes count as magical cultivation attacks for overcoming Resistance and Immunity;
your Unarmed Strikes may deal Bludgeoning or Force damage, chosen when you hit;
you may strike incorporeal creatures normally with Unarmed Strikes;
when you use an Unarmed Strike to damage an unattended object, add your Proficiency Bonus to the damage.
Iron Meridian Body does not allow you to strike through Total Cover or attack creatures on another plane.

TAL_IRON_FIST_MERCIFUL_HAND:
##### Merciful Hand - Unique Iron Fist Talent
When your Unarmed Strike would reduce a creature to 0 HP, you may leave it at 1 HP and choose one:
knock it Prone;
Grapple it if you have a free hand and it is a legal target;
prevent it from taking Reactions until the end of its next turn;
immediately move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from it.
When you use Merciful Hand, regain Martial Focus if absent.

TAL_IRON_FIST_SOVEREIGN_IRON_BODY_INCARN:
##### Sovereign Iron-Body Incarnation
“The master did not raise a hand. Every bone in the room remembered how to be struck.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign incarnation of cultivated martial form.
For the duration:
gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, and Force damage;
your Unarmed Strike reach increases by 10 feet;
your Breath-Extended Strike range becomes 60 feet when you expend Martial Focus;
your Unarmed Strikes ignore Resistance to Bludgeoning and Force damage;
once per turn when you hit with an Unarmed Strike, apply one additional Form talent you know;
once per round when a hostile creature misses you with a melee attack, make one Unarmed Strike against it without spending your Reaction;
when you Open a creature, learn whether Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution is its weakest saving throw;
regain Martial Focus when you reduce a creature to 0 HP or cause a creature to fail a saving throw against one of your Iron Fist talents.
Sovereign Iron-Body Incarnation ends early if you become Incapacitated.

TAL_IRON_FIST_WORLD_TEMPERING_BODY:
##### World-Tempering Body
Prerequisite: Bell-Tower Body, CL 15+
While holding Martial Focus:
you cannot be knocked Prone unless the source succeeds on a Strength check or Cultivation Check against your Iron Fist Save DC;
reduce forced movement affecting you by 15 feet;
when you take damage from a melee attack, gain Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus after the damage resolves;
your Unarmed Strikes can damage objects as though made with adamantine for the purpose of ignoring ordinary object Damage Thresholds.

TAL_KARMA_RECORD_THE_DEED:
#### Record the Deed
Action Type: Reaction
Range: 60 feet
Cost: None
Use Limit: Once per round
Trigger: You Witness a Cause created by a creature within range
Place one Karmic Imprint on the creature responsible for the Cause.
Debt. Place one Debt Imprint when the creature does one of the following:
deals meaningful damage to another creature;
inflicts a harmful condition;
breaks a clear oath;
betrays a willing ally;
steals something of real value;
commands a minion to perform a harmful act;
performs another harmful act approved by the GM.
Grace. Place one Grace Imprint when the creature does one of the following:
restores Hit Points to another creature;
prevents meaningful damage;
removes a harmful condition;
protects another creature at personal risk;
keeps a difficult oath;
repays a meaningful debt;
performs another selfless act approved by the GM.
A single action normally creates only one Imprint. If more than one creature is responsible, the GM determines who receives the Imprint.

TAL_KARMA_SEVER_THE_KARMIC_THREAD:
#### Sever the Karmic Thread
“No debt. No blessing. No fate. For one breath, the heavens lose their claim.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Court of Cause and Effect, hidden heavenly inheritance, GM approval
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature, oath, curse, bond, possession, debt, grace, contract, summoning link, resurrection anchor, divination link, or supernatural obligation you can perceive.
If the target is unwilling or protected by another power, it makes a Charisma saving throw or contests your Karma Check with its own relevant check.
Failed Save or Successful Contest by You: Choose one narrow karmic connection. Examples include:
one oath;
one curse;
one possession bond;
one divination link;
one summoning contract;
one resurrection anchor;
one master-servant binding;
one named Karma talent affecting the target;
one debt owed to a specific creature, sect, ghost, ancestor, or divine office;
one Grace or Debt Imprint chain created by a specific event.
The chosen connection is severed for 1 hour.
Successful Save or Failed Contest by You: The connection is suppressed until the start of your next turn.
Sever the Karmic Thread cannot:
remove an entire Path;
erase a character’s whole past;
remove every curse at once;
negate all consequences of a campaign event;
permanently cancel a Secret sphere;
grant immunity to future actions;
make a guilty creature innocent;
make a promise never have been spoken.
When the severance ends, the thread may return changed. The GM decides whether the suspended connection resumes, weakens, twists, or creates a new story debt.

TAL_LIGHTNING_STORM_HEART_ENGINE:
### Storm-Heart Engine - Charge, Lightning Body
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Your body can recycle a portion of discharged lightning.
Once per turn when you consume a Charge to empower a Lightning talent, choose one:
- gain Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
- move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
- add +1 to the next Lightning Check you make before the end of your next turn;
- impose Disadvantage on the next Opportunity Attack made against you before the start of your next turn.
If you are in Lightning-God Body or True Lightning-God Mantle, choose two benefits instead of one.

TAL_MAGMA_COURT_OF_THE_LIVING_VOLCANO:
#### Court of the Living Volcano - Domain, Terrain
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 8 CP
Establish a Magma Domain of unstable volcanic ground.
You and Allies:
• ignore damage from your Molten Terrain;
• gain Resistance to Fire damage;
• ignore difficult terrain caused by ash, rubble, magma, and obsidian;
• gain Advantage on saving throws against Prone and forced movement.
Enemies:
• treat the area as difficult terrain;
• cannot Dash while touching your Molten Terrain;
• have Disadvantage on checks made to maintain footing;
• suffer Heat Pressure when they start their turn inside unless they succeed on a Dexterity saving throw.
When an enemy starts its turn inside the Domain, it makes a Dexterity saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose two:
• take 3d8 Fire or Bludgeoning damage;
• fall Prone;
• become Burning for 1d8 Fire damage until the end of its next turn;
• Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of its next turn;
• cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Choose one from the list, but if you choose damage, the damage is halved.
A creature is affected only once per turn.

TAL_MAGMA_FURNACE_STEP:
#### Furnace Step - Terrain, Armor
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Until the end of the current turn
Cost: 1 CP
Move through heat, rubble, and unstable ground.
Until the end of your turn:
• Speed increases by 10 feet;
• ignore your own Molten Terrain;
• ignore ordinary rubble, ash, volcanic stone, and obsidian difficult terrain;
• do not provoke opportunity attacks from one creature of your choice;
• leave one 5-foot patch of Molten Terrain in a space you moved through.
The patch lasts until the start of your next turn.

TAL_MAGMA_MAGMA_INITIATION:
#### Magma Initiation
When you learn Magma, choose the form your magma takes most often:
• red-gold lava;
• black slag;
• white-hot furnace stone;
• volcanic glass;
• subterranean pressure cracks;
• ash-veiled lava;
• spiritual molten ore;
• another appropriate expression.
This choice is cosmetic unless a feature says otherwise.
You learn to create small amounts of cultivated molten stone for Magma talents. These expressions are magical and fade when the talent ends unless a feature creates lasting obsidian, stone, or ruin.

TAL_MAGMA_SHAPE_THE_CRUST:
#### Shape the Crust
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 60 feet
Cost: None
Choose one patch of Molten Terrain or Obsidian Terrain you created within range.
Choose one:
• cool one 5-foot patch of your Molten Terrain into Obsidian Terrain for 1 minute;
• crack one 5-foot patch of your Obsidian Terrain, ending it and dealing Slashing damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus to one creature standing in it, Dexterity save negates;
• move one 5-foot patch of your Molten Terrain up to 5 feet across a continuous surface;
• shape one patch into a low ridge that grants Half Cover until the start of your next turn;
• open a safe stepping line through one patch for one ally until the start of your next turn.
Shape the Crust cannot move terrain through walls, across open air, or into a creature’s space unless a talent says otherwise.

TAL_MAGMA_VOLCANIC_FORGE:
#### Volcanic Forge - Forge, Strategic
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 30 days
Cost: 15 CP during the final rite, plus 25,000 gp or campaign-equivalent in rare ore, crystal, volcanic essence, Formation materials, and protective construction
Create a permanent volcanic forge, controlled magma chamber, or furnace cavern.
Choose three benefits:
• Metal and Fire projects require 25 percent less time;
• Magma talents cost 1 fewer CP once per turn while nearby, minimum 1;
• produce rare volcanic essence worth 500 gp each month;
• refine difficult ores;
• destroy dangerous materials safely;
• power large Formations;
• create obsidian defenses;
• provide constant heat;
• improve alchemical furnace work;
• support sect-scale artifact production;
• create secure disposal pits;
• warm a surrounding settlement;
• support a defensive Domain during a siege.
You may maintain a number of Volcanic Forges equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
A Volcanic Forge is infrastructure, not an adventuring-day combat talent. It creates enemies, obligations, supply lines, and territorial value.

TAL_MAGMA_VOLCANO_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
#### Volcano-Sovereign Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign embodiment of volcanic force.
For the duration:
• Size becomes Large if smaller;
• Reach increases by 5 feet;
• gain +3 AC;
• gain Immunity to Fire damage;
• gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, Cold, and Poison damage;
• ignore your own Molten Terrain and Obsidian Terrain;
• Magma Glob deals 6d10 Fire or Bludgeoning damage;
• Furnace Step may be used once per turn without spending CP;
• once per turn when you create Molten Terrain, increase its size by one 5-foot patch or expand its radius by 5 feet.
Volcanic Presence:
When an enemy starts its turn within 20 feet, it makes a Dexterity saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose two:
• take 4d8 Fire or Bludgeoning damage;
• become Burning for 2d8 Fire damage until the end of its next turn;
• fall Prone;
• Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of its next turn;
• cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Choose one, but damage is halved.
A creature is affected only once per turn.

TAL_METAL_TEMPERED_EDGE:
### Tempered Edge - Edge
When you use Sharpen, choose one:
- increase the extra damage by 1;
- change the extra damage to Slashing or Piercing after seeing whether the triggering hit dealt damage;
- if the triggering attack damaged an object, door, chain, shield, weapon, lock, or piece of armor, ignore the first 5 points of that object's damage threshold, hardness, or comparable mundane durability.
At Core Formation Realm, the ignored durability becomes 10.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_CAPERING_FOOTWORK:
#### Capering Footwork - Base Opener
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Until the end of your current turn
Cost: 1 Stamina or 1 CP through an explicit non-Body access feature
Chain Role: Opener
Adopt an unpredictable movement pattern.
Until the end of your turn:
your Speed increases by 10 feet;
you ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
you may move through the spaces of creatures larger than you, treating hostile spaces as difficult terrain;
opportunity attacks against you have Disadvantage;
gain Advantage on the next Dexterity (Acrobatics) check you make before the end of the turn;
you may create and spend one Monkey Link.
You cannot end this movement in an occupied space.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_GREAT_SAGE_EQUAL_TO_HEA:
#### Great Sage Equal to Heaven - Unique, Transformation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 Stamina or 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Chain Role: Engine, Transformation
Enter the perfected Monkey King state.
For the duration, gain:
Speed +30 feet;
Climb Speed equal to Speed;
jump distance multiplied by 10;
+3 AC;
Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage;
Advantage on Dexterity saving throws;
ability to move through hostile spaces without spending extra movement;
improvised weapons deal at least 1d12 damage;
you may create up to two Monkey Links per turn and spend up to two Monkey Links per turn, but not on the same Finish.
##### Uncatchable
Once per turn when an enemy misses you or you succeed on a Dexterity saving throw, choose one:
move up to 15 feet without provoking opportunity attacks;
make one melee weapon attack;
create a Monkey Link.
##### Laugh at Heaven
Once during the transformation, when you fail a saving throw, choose to succeed instead.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_IMPOSSIBLE_APE_REVERSAL:
#### Impossible Ape Reversal - Caper, Trick
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A creature hits you with an attack, Grapples you, Restrains you, or forces you to make a Dexterity or Strength saving throw
Cost: 8 Stamina or 8 CP
Use Limit: Once per short rest
Chain Role: Reversal
The triggering creature makes a Wisdom saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose two:
the triggering attack misses or the triggering Grapple or Restraint fails;
move up to half your Speed without provoking opportunity attacks;
the triggering creature falls Prone;
the triggering creature drops one held object;
make one melee or improvised-weapon attack against the triggering creature;
create a Monkey Link that lasts until the end of your next turn.
Successful Save: Choose one option instead.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_MONKEY_GRIP:
#### Monkey Grip - Base Link Tool
You cultivate hands, feet, knees, hooked sleeves, staff leverage, tail-like Qi, and impossible balance.
Gain the following benefits:
gain a Climb Speed equal to half your Speed;
gain Advantage on ability checks made to climb, hang, swing, balance, cling, or keep hold of an object;
you may hang from appropriate terrain using hands, feet, hooked equipment, tail-like Qi, or your staff;
while Capering Footwork is active, climbing, hanging, swinging, or changing elevation may create a Monkey Link.
Monkey Grip does not give you extra hands. You still cannot wield more weapons or shields than your body and equipment reasonably allow.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_MONKEY_STYLE_TRAINING:
#### Monkey Style Training
When you learn Monkey Style:
gain proficiency in Dexterity (Acrobatics), Dexterity (Sleight of Hand), or Strength (Athletics);
if already proficient in all three, choose one Mortal Realm Monkey Style talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
gain Capering Footwork;
gain Monkey Grip;
gain Laughing Staff and Borrowed Weapon;
choose one Mortal Realm Monkey Style talent for which you meet the prerequisites.
This means every Monkey Style practitioner can start the caper, create a link through movement or terrain, spend that link on a basic finish, and use staff or prop fighting as a natural part of the chain.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_STAFF_SWING_STEP:
#### Staff-Swing Step - Staff, Climb
Chain Role: Link
While wielding a staff or suitable long object, you may use it as a vault, brace, hook, pole, or temporary bridge.
During Capering Footwork, you may create a Monkey Link when you do one of the following with the staff:
vault over a Small or Medium obstacle;
swing around a post, branch, beam, rope, or creature at least one size larger than you;
brace against a surface to change direction;
plant the staff to change elevation by at least 5 feet.
Once per turn after creating a Monkey Link this way, move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks from one creature you can see.

TAL_MONKEY_STYLE_THOUSAND_MONKEY_UPRISIN:
#### Thousand-Monkey Uprising - Afterimage, Domain
Prerequisite: Mirror-Monkey Technique or Court of the Laughing Sage, CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 12 Stamina or 12 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Chain Role: Domain, Engine
Create a chaotic host of spectral, illusory, or Qi-formed monkeys.
Inside the aura:
enemies treat terrain as difficult terrain;
enemies cannot take Reactions;
allies gain Half Cover;
unattended objects move unpredictably, though they cannot deal damage unless a talent says so;
once per round, when an enemy inside the aura fails a saving throw, misses an attack, drops an object, or falls Prone, you create a Monkey Link.
The first time each turn an enemy inside the aura moves or attacks, it makes a Wisdom saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
fall Prone;
drop one held object;
Speed becomes 0 until the end of the turn;
take 3d8 Psychic or Bludgeoning damage.
Successful Save: No additional effect.
This is a Domain-like Monkey Style effect and follows Domain safeguards.

TAL_QIWEAVING_FEED_CURRENT:
#### Feed Current - Bond
Prerequisite: Qi Bond Package
When you apply this Bond talent to a willing bonded creature, spend 1 or more CP, up to your Proficiency Bonus.
The target gains the same amount as Temporary CP.
Temporary CP granted by this talent:
lasts for 1 minute;
may be spent only on sphere techniques or Path features;
cannot be converted into healing or CXP;
cannot be transferred again;
does not stack with itself. Use the higher amount.
A creature can benefit from your Feed Current once per short rest.

TAL_QIWEAVING_HEAVEN_TUNED_MODULATION:
#### Heaven-Tuned Modulation
Prerequisite: Modulation Package, CL 15+
When you apply a Modulation talent to a technique you activate, choose one additional minor tuning:
increase the technique’s range by 30 feet;
increase one area dimension by 5 feet;
extend a duration of 1 minute or longer by 1 round;
add your Proficiency Bonus to one damage or healing roll;
impose Disadvantage on the first ability check made to identify or counter the technique before the end of your next turn.
You may use Heaven-Tuned Modulation a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus per long rest.

TAL_QIWEAVING_MERIDIAN_GRAMMAR:
#### Meridian Grammar - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
You learn to read the grammar of active Qi.
Gain the following benefits:
increase the range of Unweave Pattern and Qi Bond to 60 feet;
when you see a creature activate a sphere technique, you may identify the sphere involved if you know that sphere or have seen the technique before;
when you target an Active Qi Pattern with Unweave Pattern, you learn its approximate Pattern Rank before deciding whether to spend CP on augments;
you have Advantage on Qiweaving Checks made to identify, study, or trace an Active Qi Pattern during exploration or downtime.
Meridian Grammar does not reveal a creature’s full list of talents or Path features.

TAL_QIWEAVING_MINOR_QI_ARTS:
##### Minor Qi Arts
You learn to perform harmless adjustments to ambient Qi.
As an Action, you may create one minor effect within 30 feet:
color, warm, chill, flavor, clean, or soil a Tiny object;
cause a faint harmless sound, scent, breeze, spark, ripple, or glow;
make a small symbol, seal, footprint, or line of script appear for 1 minute;
open or close an unlocked Tiny mundane object such as a pouch clasp or paper fan;
predict ordinary weather signs for the next hour when outdoors;
cause a candle, incense stick, lamp wick, or similar tiny flame to brighten, dim, or extinguish.
Minor Qi Arts cannot deal damage, impose a condition, create Cover, duplicate another sphere talent, activate a magic item, or deceive a careful observer by itself.
If your table uses spell cantrips directly, the GM may allow Minor Qi Arts to count as druidcraft, prestidigitation, and thaumaturgy for prerequisite and harmless utility purposes. Use your Key Ability as the spellcasting ability for such cantrips.

TAL_QIWEAVING_READ_CURRENT:
#### Read Current - Bond
Prerequisite: Qi Bond Package
When you apply this Bond talent, learn two of the following facts about the bonded target:
whether it currently has CP remaining;
whether it is maintaining Concentration;
the number of Active Qi Patterns currently affecting it, rounded up to a simple category: none, one, several, or many;
the strongest visible sphere resonance affecting it, such as Fire, Blood, Shadow, Protection, Sword, or another known sphere;
whether its circulation is stable, strained, disrupted, corrupted, or turbulent;
whether one visible Active Qi Pattern on it has a Pattern Rank no higher than your Proficiency Bonus.
Read Current does not reveal exact statistics, hidden thoughts, spell names, complete talents, or private memories.

TAL_QIWEAVING_SOVEREIGN_QIWEAVER_INCARNA:
#### Sovereign Qiweaver Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You manifest the living embodiment of the woven current. Your eyes may become rings of script, your meridians may shine through the skin, or ten thousand invisible threads may hum through the battlefield.
For the duration:
you perceive Active Qi Patterns within 120 feet that are not behind Total Cover;
your Unweave Pattern and Qi Bond range becomes 120 feet;
once during each of your turns, you may use Unweave Pattern as a Bonus Action against a pattern with Pattern Rank no higher than your Proficiency Bonus;
once per round, you may use Counterweave without expending Martial Focus;
when you apply a Modulation talent to your own technique, reduce that Modulation’s CP cost by 1, minimum 0;
when you successfully end an Active Qi Pattern, regain 1 CP. You may regain CP this way a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus during the incarnation;
hostile creatures of your choice inside 30 feet have Disadvantage on checks made to conceal, disguise, or stabilize Active Qi Patterns.
Sovereign Qiweaver Incarnation does not automatically affect Domains, Secret Inheritances, artifacts, or Formation projects.

TAL_RETRIBUTION_HAYMAKER:
### Haymaker - Counter
Aim for the target’s mouth, jaw, throat, breath-channel, or another equivalent anatomy.
After your Counterstrike hits, the target makes a Dexterity saving throw.
Failed Save: The target’s speech and breath channel is damaged until it receives magical healing or completes a short or long rest.
While damaged, whenever the creature attempts to:
speak audibly;
bite;
use a breath weapon that requires the damaged anatomy;
cast a spell with a Verbal component;
activate a sphere talent or another ability requiring clear speech;
the creature makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: The attempted speech or activation fails. If the attempt required an Action, Bonus Action, or Reaction, that action is spent. A limited-use resource is not spent unless it was already committed before the saving throw.
A creature without a meaningful mouth, throat, breath channel, or equivalent anatomy is immune.

TAL_RETRIBUTION_HEAVEN_READING_STILLNESS:
### Heaven-Reading Stillness - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+
When you prepare Counterstrike, you may choose the following as one trigger:
A hostile creature you can perceive within your reach begins any hostile action.
A hostile action includes an attack, harmful supernatural effect, deliberate attempt to Grapple or Shove, or another action that would directly harm or restrain you or an ally.
Heaven-Reading Stillness does not trigger from:
purely defensive actions;
movement by itself;
speech by itself;
concealed activity you cannot perceive;
an action whose hostility is not apparent until after it resolves.

TAL_RETRIBUTION_INTERCEPTING_STRIKE:
### Intercepting Strike - Guard
When you prepare Counterstrike, you may choose to intercept one physical attack rather than attack the creature making it.
Choose a trigger such as:
a melee weapon attack is made within your reach;
a physical projectile passes through your reach;
a physical projectile targets a creature within your reach.
When the trigger begins, take your Reaction and make one melee weapon attack or Unarmed Strike against the incoming attack.
If your attack roll equals or exceeds the triggering attack roll, negate the triggering attack.
Intercepting Strike normally cannot negate:
spell attacks;
beams;
intangible supernatural effects;
area effects;
massive projectiles such as boulders or ballista bolts unless you wield a weapon or use a technique capable of intercepting them.
Reactive Interception: Expend Martial Focus to use Intercepting Strike as a Reaction without preparing Counterstrike first.

TAL_RETRIBUTION_RAGING_BULL:
### Raging Bull - Counter
When your chosen trigger begins, move up to half your Speed in a straight line before making the Counterstrike.
This movement:
must end with the triggering creature within your reach;
uses your movement for the round;
provokes Opportunity Attacks normally;
does not allow movement through occupied spaces or sealed barriers unless another rule permits it.
If you cannot reach the triggering creature, you may ignore the trigger and continue waiting.

TAL_RETRIBUTION_RETURNING_BLADE_ACROSS_E:
### Returning Blade Across Empty Ground - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Raging Bull, CL 15+
When Raging Bull activates, you may move up to your Speed rather than half your Speed.
During this movement:
you may move across liquids and vertical surfaces without falling until the movement ends;
Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage;
you may turn once by up to 90 degrees;
you must still end with the triggering creature within your reach.
Returning Blade Across Empty Ground is cultivated movement, not teleportation.

TAL_SAND_SAND_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
#### Sand-Sovereign Incarnation - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP; once per long rest
You manifest as a sovereign of dunes, a storm-robed immortal, a glass-crowned desert monarch, a body of flowing grains, or a silent burial king.
For the duration:
you gain a Burrow Speed of 40 feet through sand, dust, dry soil, gravel, and loose earth;
you may move through spaces occupied by Sand Terrain you control as though they were not Difficult Terrain;
you have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage from non-artifact weapons;
you can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide if the entire route is filled with sand, dust, or loose grain and your carried equipment can transform with you;
once on each of your turns, you may create up to two Shallow Sand Terrain squares within 60 feet without spending an Action;
when a creature misses you with a melee attack, you may move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks and leave one Shallow Sand Terrain square in your previous space;
your Sand Control Limit increases by your Proficiency Bonus.
You cannot pass through sealed Barriers, airtight containers, solid stone, living bodies, or consecrated anti-transform zones without an appropriate talent, opposed Cultivation Check, or GM permission.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_COURT_OF_TEN_THOUSAND_EMPT:
#### COURT OF TEN THOUSAND EMPTY SLEEVES - DOMAIN
“The sovereign counted every sword, seal, talisman, and hidden weapon. Counting them had been the mistake.”
Prerequisite: Empty-Sleeve Hand, CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Area: 30-foot Emanation originating from you
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short or long rest
Establish a Scoundrel Domain in which the battlefield behaves like a rigged shell game.
For the duration:
use Dirty Trick and Steal against any valid target inside the Domain;
unattended Tiny or Small objects and suitable loose clutter inside the Domain count as accessible when a legal route exists;
once during each of your turns, use Dirty Trick or Steal without spending an Action or Bonus Action;
apply up to two different Trick talents to one successful Dirty Trick or Steal;
once per turn, draw, stow, plant, catch, drop, or reposition one ordinary handheld object inside the Domain without spending an Action;
once per round when a hostile creature inside the Domain misses an attack or fails a D20 Test, apply Exploited Opening to it;
when you succeed on Dirty Trick or Steal inside the Domain, move up to 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.
Court of Ten Thousand Empty Sleeves does not create items, open sealed containers, bypass Total Cover, ignore a sealed Barrier, or automatically steal artifacts.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_EMPTY_HANDED_THEFT_OF_HEAV:
#### EMPTY-HANDED THEFT OF HEAVEN - EMPTY-SLEEVE
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A creature inside your Empty-Sleeve Hand range activates an accessible handheld item, weapon technique with a physical weapon, consumable, talisman, focus, or device
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Make a Scoundrel Check against the target’s Cultivation Save DC. A stronger protected object or effect may require an opposed Cultivation Check.
Success: Choose one:
steal the triggering object before its use resolves;
redirect the triggering object’s effect to another legal target;
cause the object to activate harmlessly;
replace one ordinary consumable with one harmless Tiny substitute you possess;
remove one ordinary weapon from the target’s grasp before its weapon technique resolves;
suppress the triggering object’s activation until the end of your next turn.
Failure: The triggering effect resolves normally. Move up to 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.
Empty-Handed Theft of Heaven cannot automatically overcome an artifact, fused object, natural body part, inaccessible anchor, Legendary transformation, or Secret Inheritance.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_EMPTY_SLEEVE_HAND:
#### EMPTY-SLEEVE HAND - REALM EVOLUTION
Prerequisite: CL 5+
While holding Martial Focus, you may manifest an Empty-Sleeve Hand whenever you use Dirty Trick or Steal.
Your Empty-Sleeve Hand:
extends your Dirty Trick and Steal range to 30 feet;
travels along one clear legal route to a target you can perceive;
may perform the same physical manipulation your own hand could perform through Dirty Trick or Steal;
may carry a successfully stolen object back into one of your free hands;
may drop, reposition, or plant an object in a legal accessible location;
vanishes immediately after the maneuver resolves.
Your Empty-Sleeve Hand may appear as:
a spectral sleeve;
a translucent hand of Qi;
an invisible hooked thread;
a weighted cord moving too quickly to follow;
a flicker of footwork that makes witnesses uncertain whether you ever crossed the distance.
The Empty-Sleeve Hand does not:
remain on the battlefield after the maneuver;
grant general telekinesis;
manipulate arbitrary objects without using Dirty Trick or Steal;
open a sealed container remotely;
pass through Total Cover or a sealed Barrier;
automatically remove an artifact, soul-bound object, or complete suit of armor;
exert enough force to Shove, Grapple, lift a creature, or replace the Brute, Wrestling, Thread, Force, or Space spheres.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_RIGGED_ESCAPE:
#### RIGGED ESCAPE - ESCAPE
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You gain Grappled, Prone, or Restrained, or become the target of an Opportunity Attack
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Choose one:
move up to 30 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
stand from Prone without spending movement;
immediately repeat one check or saving throw to end Grappled or Restrained with Advantage;
exchange spaces with one willing ally within 30 feet if both spaces are legal;
use Dirty Trick against one creature inside your Empty-Sleeve Hand range.
Rigged Escape cannot move through a sealed Barrier or leave an effect that does not permit physical escape without an appropriate check.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_SCOUNDREL_TRAINING:
#### SCOUNDREL TRAINING
When you learn Scoundrel:
gain proficiency in Dexterity (Sleight of Hand);
if already proficient, choose one Mortal Realm Scoundrel talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent;
choose one Mortal Realm Trick talent for which you meet the prerequisites as a bonus talent.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_SOVEREIGN_OF_TEN_THOUSAND_:
#### SOVEREIGN OF TEN THOUSAND EMPTY SLEEVES - REALM EVOLUTION
“The cultivator raised both hands. They were empty. Everyone else checked their pockets.”
Prerequisite: Court of Ten Thousand Empty Sleeves, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign manifestation of the Scoundrel Dao: a robe of grasping afterimages, spectral sleeves filled with impossible hidden tools, laughing spiritual hands, or another suitable expression.
For the duration:
gain Fly Speed 40 feet and Hover;
increase Empty-Sleeve Hand range to 60 feet;
use Dirty Trick or Steal once during each of your turns without spending an Action or Bonus Action;
apply up to three different Trick talents to one successful Dirty Trick or Steal;
regain Martial Focus whenever you succeed on Dirty Trick or Steal;
gain one additional Reaction each round, usable only for Scoundrel talents;
your supernatural Scoundrel talents may affect incorporeal creatures, spiritual projections, exposed spiritual anchors, and active talismans;
when you steal one unattended handheld object within range, draw it into your hand or place it into any legal space you can perceive within range.
Sovereign of Ten Thousand Empty Sleeves does not grant unrestricted telekinesis, allow arbitrary theft through sealed Barriers, or automatically overcome artifacts and stronger cultivation protections.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_STEAL_EQUIPMENT:
#### STEAL EQUIPMENT - EMPTY-SLEEVE
Prerequisite: Master Thief, CL 10+
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
When you use Steal, attempt to remove one worn item, including:
a belt;
sash;
cloak;
quiver;
scabbard;
component pouch;
robe;
shield;
helmet;
worn talisman;
suit of armor;
comparable worn equipment.
Make the Steal check with Disadvantage. Master Thief does not remove this Disadvantage.
On a success, the object appears in your free hand or one legal unoccupied space inside your Empty-Sleeve Hand range.
A fused object, soul-bound item, artifact, spiritually protected treasure, or scene-defining object may resist with an opposed Cultivation Check or another appropriate defense.
At Core Formation, stealing a complete suit of armor is intentionally possible. The technique is audacious, supernatural, and highly visible.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_STEAL_FOOTING:
#### STEAL FOOTING - EMPTY-SLEEVE, TRICK
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you succeed on Dirty Trick against a creature no more than one size larger than you, steal its footing.
Choose one:
move it up to 10 feet along the ground into legal spaces;
give it the Prone condition;
reduce each of its Speeds to 0 until the start of your next turn;
prevent it from taking Reactions until the start of your next turn.
If the target is standing on unstable terrain, balancing, climbing, flying through physical wings, or moving rapidly when you apply this Trick, choose two different results instead.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_STEAL_TALENT:
#### STEAL TALENT - EMPTY-SLEEVE
Prerequisite: Steal Skill, CL 10+
Use Limit: Once per long rest per creature
When you use Steal Skill, choose one observed sphere talent, martial technique, or comparable learned ability instead of a skill proficiency.
You must have observed the ability during the last 10 minutes or otherwise possess reliable knowledge that the target has it.
The target makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Cultivation Save DC.
Failed Save: For 1 minute:
the target cannot use the stolen ability;
the target cannot use abilities whose prerequisite is the stolen ability;
you may use the stolen ability when you meet its prerequisites and can pay its costs.
Successful Save: No effect.
You may maintain only one stolen talent at a time.
Steal Talent cannot steal:
a Path;
a Realm;
an entire sphere portfolio;
inherent anatomy;
a bloodline;
Legendary Actions;
Lair Actions;
a transformation sustained by the target’s body when you cannot legally assume it;
a Secret Inheritance;
an ability whose prerequisites you cannot meet.
If you steal a base sphere and the target possesses additional talents beyond the base, make the initial Scoundrel Check with Disadvantage.

TAL_SCOUNDREL_STRIP_THE_BATTLEFIELD_BARE:
#### STRIP THE BATTLEFIELD BARE - EMPTY-SLEEVE
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Area: 60-foot Emanation originating from you
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Every hostile creature of your choice inside the area makes a Dexterity saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose two different consequences for that creature:
steal one accessible held or worn object;
give it the Prone condition;
reduce each of its Speeds to 0 until the end of your next turn;
prevent it from taking Reactions until the end of your next turn;
suppress one ordinary Stance, Guard, or comparable temporary martial effect until the end of your next turn;
move it up to 20 feet along the ground if it is Huge or smaller;
apply Exploited Opening.
Successful Save: Choose one consequence other than stealing worn equipment or suppressing a temporary effect.
Stolen objects appear in your hands or legal spaces of your choice within 30 feet of you.
An artifact, soul-bound object, or superior spiritually protected object may require an additional opposed Cultivation Check.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_ANCESTRAL_WRIT:
### Ancestral Writ - Pavilion, Lineage, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
You can invoke the old words correctly.
When you have access to a legitimate ancestral record, founding oath, old charter, saint’s instruction, sect law, clan genealogy, or lineage tablet, spend one Merit Die and make a Sect Check.
On a success, the Writ grants one non-combat effect:
delay an unlawful punishment until review;
open a sealed but non-secret archive category;
protect a junior from being erased from records;
require a hall to answer a formal question;
preserve a property, title, or duty from casual seizure;
grant safe guest status to a named petitioner for 24 hours;
prove that a tradition, promise, or boundary once existed.
On a failure, the Writ is ambiguous, politically inconvenient, incomplete, or challenged.
This talent cannot compel an ancestor to appear, create a divine miracle, or override a current sect master without consequence.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_CONTRIBUTION_EXCHAN:
### Contribution Exchange - Ledger, Steward
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
You know how to turn merit into lawful access.
During downtime in an institution where you have Standing, spend one Merit Die to request one ordinary exchange:
a Common recipe fragment;
supervised use of a mundane workshop;
a basic map;
common medicinal supplies;
common harvesting permissions;
mundane travel papers;
a letter of introduction;
a minor discount on institution-provided services;
permission to borrow a common tool for one duty.
If the request has a gold cost, reduce the cost by 10 percent per number rolled on the Merit Die, to a maximum reduction of 50 percent. This reduction represents legitimate contribution credit, not bargaining.
The GM may cap, deny, or require a mission for rare resources.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_COURTYARD_GRANT:
### Courtyard Grant - Household, Lineage
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You secure a stable place in the sect’s body.
You may spend 30 days, appropriate Standing, and GM-approved cost or patronage to establish a named courtyard, classroom, field office, dormitory wing, guest suite, workroom, or small hall.
While using this place for non-combat work, you and your invited allies gain the following benefits:
regain all Merit Dice after a Long Rest if you perform 10 minutes of duties there;
gain Advantage on one Sect Check per day made inside the place;
safely store ordinary records, tools, clothing, and non-rare supplies;
maintain a small staff or student group if you have Disciple Register.
If the place is attacked, seized, politically undermined, or neglected, the benefits pause until restored.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_DEACON_S_SEAL:
### Deacon’s Seal - Steward, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You can speak with recognized departmental authority.
When you are in an institution where you have Inner or Core Standing, you may spend one Merit Die to issue a lawful non-combat instruction to lower-Standing members of your department, hall, mission team, or work crew.
Examples include:
close the storehouse until the audit ends;
assign workers to evacuation duty;
require mission reports by sunset;
move students to the lecture courtyard;
open ordinary records for inspection;
preserve evidence;
send a runner to an elder;
suspend a minor privilege pending review.
Targets obey only if the instruction is lawful, plausible, and within your recognized authority. This is not mind control. People may resist, appeal, lie, delay, or exploit unclear orders.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_DEPARTMENT_LEDGER:
### Department Ledger - Steward, Ledger
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You can manage a hall-scale project.
When you supervise a non-combat downtime project for at least one day, spend one Merit Die and choose one:
reduce the project’s time by 10 percent per number rolled on the Merit Die, maximum 50 percent;
reduce ordinary wastage, spoilage, or loss by the same percentage;
identify the most likely bottleneck;
protect the project from one minor bureaucratic disruption;
create a clean report that grants Advantage on one later petition for funding, permission, or reinforcements.
This cannot reduce the cost of rare named ingredients, Heavenly Materials, Secret Inheritances, land purchases, bribes, or story-required sacrifices unless the GM permits it.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_DISCIPLE_REGISTER:
### Disciple Register - Lineage, Steward
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You can responsibly manage juniors.
During downtime, you may register a small group of willing juniors, workers, apprentices, or students under your supervision. The group size can be up to twice your Proficiency Bonus.
While they are assigned to safe, non-combat duties, choose one benefit:
their ordinary work counts as one competent assistant for a downtime project;
they preserve records well enough to grant Advantage on one later audit or report;
they maintain a basic facility such as a classroom, field shed, dormitory room, or medicine queue;
one member may carry a message, document, or ordinary object through safe institutional channels.
If you exploit, endanger, abandon, or humiliate the registered group, lose access to this talent in that institution until you repair the relationship.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_DORMITORY_NETWORK:
### Dormitory Network - Household, Etiquette
You can use shared sleeping quarters, laundry yards, kitchens, queues, and chore rotations as a rumor network.
After spending at least 10 minutes in a dormitory, kitchen, outer yard, servant hall, or similar place, make a Sect Check.
On a success, learn one useful mundane rumor about one of the following:
a current mission;
a missing person;
a common grievance;
a disliked senior;
a useful clerk;
an upcoming inspection;
a public lecture;
an ordinary resource shortage;
an accepted local custom.
The DC is usually 12 for ordinary gossip, 15 for sensitive hall gossip, or 18 for information people are afraid to repeat.
Spending one Merit Die on the check also lets you avoid revealing that you were asking.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_ELDER_S_MANDATE:
### Elder’s Mandate - Lineage, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
Your words can become institution-level instruction.
When you have Elder Standing, equivalent authority, or a recognized emergency commission, spend one Merit Die to issue a non-combat mandate affecting one hall, branch, expedition, village protectorate, archive, medicine ward, or comparable department.
Examples include:
open emergency grain stores;
suspend a dangerous mission board category;
require a public accounting of missing disciples;
grant temporary guest protection to refugees;
authorize a medical quarantine;
assign a branch hall to prepare for winter;
order the archive to preserve threatened records;
call all juniors of a lineage to public instruction.
The mandate lasts until fulfilled, revoked, or challenged by equal or higher authority.
This cannot order attacks, assassinations, forced cultivation, theft, executions, or other combat actions through the sphere.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_EMERGENCY_MUSTER:
### Emergency Muster - Steward, Household
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You can organize people when panic would waste lives.
As an Action outside combat, or during a disaster scene at the GM’s discretion, spend one Merit Die and issue evacuation, shelter, triage, fireline, floodline, or missing-person instructions to a group that can hear or receive your orders.
Make a Sect Check.
On a success, reduce confusion and ordinary casualties in the affected area. The GM chooses the exact effect, such as:
a crowd exits through safe routes;
workers carry water to the right place;
juniors gather at the assigned courtyard;
records or medicine are saved from a burning hall;
villagers avoid a collapsing bridge;
noncombatants hide instead of running into danger.
This talent cannot defeat an enemy or prevent harm that only combat, magic, or sacrifice could stop.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_NAME_ON_THE_ANCESTR:
### Name on the Ancestral Ledger
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Sect Stewardship, Found a Branch Hall or Ancestral Writ, GM approval.
Your name is not merely written in the register. The register answers when your duty is called.
Once per campaign arc, when you stand before a legitimate institutional witness such as an ancestral tablet, sect master, elder council, founding stele, branch altar, public merit roll, grand archive, or oath hall, you may invoke your recorded service.
State one non-combat institutional claim:
this junior is under my protection;
this village is owed shelter;
this archive must not be burned;
this mission’s dead must be named;
this medicine must be distributed;
this branch hall must be heard;
this false charge must face witnesses;
this oath has not expired;
this person deserves a place in the register;
this sect must remember what it promised.
Make a Sect Check. Add all unspent Merit Dice you possess to the roll, expending them.
On a success, the institution must answer the claim in a meaningful way before it can lawfully ignore, punish, erase, or overrule it. The answer may be help, hearing, delay, protection, recognition, public debate, a trial, or a demand for repayment.
On a failure, the claim is heard but contested. You learn who or what stands against it.
This inheritance does not compel cosmic justice, defeat tyrants, or rewrite the sect’s heart. It ensures that service has a voice strong enough to force the powerful to speak back.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_PRESERVE_THE_LINEAG:
### Preserve the Lineage - Lineage, Household, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
When a sect, branch, hall, village protectorate, archive, disciple cohort, or lineage household faces collapse from disaster, scandal, famine, evacuation, invasion aftermath, plague, corruption, or succession crisis, you may spend one Merit Die and commit yourself to preservation.
For the next 30 days, while you personally work on non-combat preservation, you may add your Merit Die to one relevant check per day without spending it.
Valid checks include:
evacuation;
rationing;
archive preservation;
medical triage;
witness collection;
debt negotiation;
inheritance transfer;
morale recovery;
refugee placement;
junior disciple protection;
lawful succession;
rebuilding a hall.
At the end of the 30 days, if the institution survives in some recognizable form, regain all spent Merit Dice and gain one lasting institutional relationship chosen with the GM.
This talent does not guarantee victory against enemies. It gives structure to saving what remains.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_PUBLIC_MERIT_ROLL:
### Public Merit Roll - Ledger, Etiquette
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You can make service visible.
After a mission, project, disaster response, harvest, investigation, teaching period, or public duty, spend one Merit Die and make a Sect Check to prepare a fair public account.
On a success, choose one:
one overlooked worker receives proper credit;
one false claimant is exposed as suspicious;
one ally gains temporary improved Standing for one scene;
one rival cannot easily erase your contribution;
one superior receives a clean summary and is less likely to misunderstand the result.
On a success by 5 or more, choose two.
This talent does not force corrupt superiors to act fairly, but it makes unfairness more visible.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_SECRET_REALM_CHARTE:
### Secret Realm Charter - Mission, Steward, Lineage
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
You can prepare an expedition as an institution, not a mob.
When a sect, clan, academy, or alliance prepares a secret realm, ruin, inheritance ground, dangerous harvest, diplomatic mission, disaster survey, or pilgrimage, spend one Merit Die during planning and make a Sect Check.
On a success, create a Charter that defines:
who is responsible for the expedition;
who may enter;
who records discoveries;
how gathered resources are divided;
how injuries and deaths are reported;
what must not be touched;
who speaks for the institution outside the gate.
While the Charter is respected, participants have Advantage on non-combat checks made to resolve disputes about access, shares, reports, and duties.
This talent cannot make the secret realm safer by itself and does not grant combat bonuses inside it.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_SECT_SUPPLY_CHAIN:
### Sect Supply Chain - Steward, Mission
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You can move useful things without pretending logistics are magic.
When you have at least one day of preparation and access to a functioning institution, spend one Merit Die to arrange transport, storage, permits, or scheduling for a non-combat supply movement.
Examples include:
medicine to a village;
grain to an outer dormitory;
common tools to a gathering expedition;
blank talisman paper to a classroom;
winter robes to a mountain outpost;
harvested ingredients to an Alchemy hall;
noncombatants away from a dangerous district.
The GM sets travel time, risk, and cost. This talent reduces confusion and ordinary loss, but it does not make bandits vanish, prevent storms, or create guards unless guards already exist and are assigned.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_STEWARD_S_AUDIT:
### Steward’s Audit - Ledger, Steward
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
You can smell corruption in a clean stack of paper.
After spending 10 minutes inspecting records, stores, work rosters, medicine cabinets, mission reports, or contribution ledgers, make a Sect Check.
On a success, learn whether one of the following is present:
missing supplies;
forged entries;
false mission completion;
hidden favoritism;
unusual waste;
unpaid labor;
duplicate claims;
a person using the wrong authority.
On a success by 5 or more, also learn the most likely place to investigate next.
This talent reveals discrepancies, not the full truth behind them.

TAL_SECT_STEWARDSHIP_STIPEND_DISCIPLINE:
### Stipend Discipline - Ledger
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
You know how to stretch a monthly stipend, store receipts, and avoid the trap of appearing richer than you are.
When you receive legal pay, stipend, mission reward, sect ration, or institutional support, you may spend one Merit Die to gain one of the following benefits:
avoid one minor fee, bribe, late penalty, or bureaucratic deduction;
identify the safest place to store or convert the payment;
gain Advantage on one check to budget supplies for a non-combat journey or duty;
detect whether a payment is short, marked, cursed by paperwork, or politically dangerous.
This cannot multiply money or generate wealth from nothing.

TAL_SHADOW_ANIMATED_SHADOW:
### Animated Shadow
Prerequisite: Shadow Lurk, CL 7+
Your Shadow Lurk becomes more substantial.
Its HP becomes:
2 x CL
It uses the Strength score of its original source.
It gains nonmagical shadowstuff versions of the source’s ordinary equipment.
Once during its turn, it may make one ordinary weapon attack or unarmed strike using the source’s attack modifier.
The attack deals half ordinary damage.
It still cannot activate:
Path features;
sphere talents;
Forged Techniques;
consumable items;
supernatural equipment;
limited-use abilities.

TAL_SHADOW_BORROWED_SILHOUETTE:
### Borrowed Silhouette
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 10 minutes
Cost: 3 CP
Choose one creature you can see.
An unwilling creature makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: Your silhouette resembles its silhouette.
Successful Save: No effect.
For the duration, gain Advantage on checks made to:
imitate the target’s build at a distance;
confuse observers in Dim Light;
conceal yourself among similar figures;
create uncertainty over which body cast which shadow.
Borrowed Silhouette does not copy:
voice;
memories;
equipment;
aura;
exact facial details.

TAL_SHADOW_SHADOW_DOPPELGANGER:
### Shadow Doppelganger
Prerequisite: Animated Shadow, CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Range: 30 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 6 CP
Create one combat-ready echo of yourself or one willing creature.
The doppelganger acts immediately after your turn.
As a Bonus Action, command it to:
Attack;
Dash;
Disengage;
Dodge;
Help;
Hide.
Without a command, it Dodges.
The doppelganger may make one:
ordinary weapon attack;
unarmed strike;
base Cultivation Attack costing no CP.
The copied attack deals half ordinary damage.
The doppelganger cannot trigger:
additional attacks;
CP talents;
limited-use features;
Domains;
Nascent Soul Realm talents;
Secret talents;
Forged Techniques;
summons.

TAL_SHADOW_SHADOW_MANTLE:
### Shadow Mantle
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 3 CP
Wrap yourself in layered silhouettes.
Gain:
+2 AC;
Resistance to Psychic and Necrotic damage;
Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks;
Disadvantage on opportunity attacks made against you;
the ability to see normally through ordinary Darkness.
Shadow Mantle does not automatically allow sight through supernatural Darkness.

TAL_SHADOW_SHADOW_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
### Shadow-Sovereign Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign silhouette standing between illumination and absence.
Gain:
Fly Speed 60 feet and Hover;
+3 AC;
Resistance to Psychic, Necrotic, and nonmagical weapon damage;
Shadow Step range becomes 60 feet;
use Shadow Step once per turn without spending CP;
maintain one Shadow Lurk or Shadow Doppelganger without Concentration;
apply Shadow Mark with Shadow Fang even when the attack misses.

TAL_SHADOW_SHADOW_STEP:
### Shadow Step
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: Half your Speed
Cost: 1 CP
Teleport from a Shadowed Space you occupy into another Shadowed Space you can see.
This movement:
does not provoke opportunity attacks;
ignores nonmagical difficult terrain;
cannot pass through a sealed barrier;
cannot cross a Dimensional Lock;
requires a legal visible destination.

TAL_SHIELD_CATCH_BLADE:
#### CATCH BLADE - DEFLECT, COUNTER
When the triggering attack misses and was made with a melee weapon, make a Disarm attempt against that weapon without spending an Action.
Add any magic enhancement bonus granted by your Shield to the Disarm attack roll.
Catch Blade does not automatically disarm:
natural weapons;
body parts;
integrated weapons;
a weapon too large for your Shield to meaningfully catch;
a weapon wielded by a narrative-scale creature unless the GM permits the attempt.

TAL_SHIELD_HEAVEN_REBUKING_BASH:
#### HEAVEN-REBUKING BASH - COUNTER
Prerequisite: Smashing Counter, Projected Shield Face, CL 10+
When Smashing Counter succeeds, choose one additional effect:
push the target an additional 15 feet;
deal Bludgeoning damage equal to 2d8 + your Strength modifier;
give the target the Prone condition after the push;
move up to 15 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks and remain adjacent to the target if possible.
At CL 17+, increase the additional push to 30 feet and the damage to:
4d8 + your Strength modifier

TAL_SHIELD_MOVING_RAMPART:
#### MOVING RAMPART - FACE
Prerequisite: Flexible Cover, Projected Shield Face, CL 5+
When you establish Flexible Cover:
you may use it as a Bonus Action without expending Martial Focus;
your movement does not end the Shield Face;
change the selected edge once during your turn without spending an Action;
allies may move with you behind the projected face, provided they remain within 5 feet of its defended side.
The Shield Face still ends at the start of your next turn.

TAL_SHIELD_ORBITING_SHIELD_DISC:
#### ORBITING SHIELD DISC - REALM EVOLUTION
Prerequisite: Returning Shield Disc, CL 10+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Release your Shield into a controlled orbit around you.
For the duration:
count as wielding the Shield;
retain its Shield Bonus;
keep both hands free;
may use Shield talents normally;
the Shield may originate Returning Shield Disc attacks from any legal space within 10 feet of you;
after each Returning Shield Disc attack, place the Shield in any legal space within 10 feet of you before it resumes orbiting;
your Shield cannot independently improvise, take Actions, or move beyond its listed control distance.
The Shield falls into your hand or into your space when the effect ends.

TAL_SHIELD_RETURN_THE_HEAVENSENT_BLOW:
#### RETURN THE HEAVENSENT BLOW - COUNTER
Prerequisite: Blockade, Perfect Redirection, CL 15+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You perceive a line, cone, breath weapon, projectile storm, or physically traveling cultivation effect whose route crosses one of your Shield Faces
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per Long Rest
Make a Cultivation Check against the creator’s Cultivation Save DC or another appropriate DC determined by the GM.
Successful Check: Choose one:
turn the effect up to 180 degrees and resolve its remaining route in a new legal direction;
split the effect around the defended side of your Shield Face, causing protected creatures behind it to take no damage or additional effects;
drive the effect into one legal unoccupied area within 60 feet where its remaining route can resolve harmlessly.
Failed Check: Creatures behind the Shield Face gain Resistance to the triggering damage and Advantage on saving throws against its additional effects.
Return the Heavensent Blow does not automatically redirect:
teleportation;
possession;
gaze effects;
internal effects;
a Domain;
a Secret Inheritance;
a narrative-scale calamity beyond the Shield’s current Realm.

TAL_SHIELD_RIDING_THE_FALLING_STAR:
#### RIDING THE FALLING STAR - MOVEMENT
Prerequisite: Shield Skate, Projected Shield Face, CL 7+
When using Shield Skate:
you may cross water, snow, loose sand, unstable rubble, and similar surfaces;
you may descend vertical surfaces safely;
you reduce falling damage by five times your Cultivation Level;
if you fall at least 20 feet before reaching the ground, you may move up to your Speed along the ground immediately after landing.
Riding the Falling Star is shield-assisted movement. It does not grant flight.

TAL_SHIELD_SEAL_THE_BREACH:
#### SEAL THE BREACH - FACE
Prerequisite: Projected Shield Face, Flexible Cover, CL 10+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Manifest one 15-foot-wide, 15-foot-high Shield-Qi Face centered on one edge of your space.
Seal the Breach is a temporary Barrier attached to you.
The face:
moves with you;
blocks physical movement through its surface;
blocks attacks, projectiles, breath weapons, line effects, and similar effects that must physically cross its surface;
blocks Incorporeal Movement through its physical boundary;
may be rotated once during your turn without spending an Action;
may be rotated as a Reaction when a creature you perceive begins moving.
The Barrier does not automatically block:
teleportation;
planar travel;
Ethereal travel;
possession;
gaze attacks;
effects originating behind the face;
spiritual effects that do not physically cross its boundary.
Seal the Breach ends if you stop wielding your Shield or have the Incapacitated condition.

TAL_SHIELD_SHIELD_SKATE:
#### SHIELD SKATE - MOVEMENT
When moving down an incline or taking the Dash action, you may use a Bonus Action to throw your Shield beneath your feet and skate across the ground.
Until the end of the current turn:
increase your Speed by 20 feet;
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain that your Shield can physically cross;
do not benefit from the Shield’s AC bonus during movement made through Shield Skate;
recover and re-equip the Shield at the end of your movement without using the Utilize action.
The GM determines whether terrain can physically support Shield Skate.

TAL_SHIELD_SHIELD_SOUL_NEVER_FALLS:
#### SHIELD SOUL NEVER FALLS
Prerequisite: Sovereign Shield-Soul Incarnation, CL 15+
When you would drop to 0 HP, lose Concentration on a Shield talent, or have your Shield destroyed, choose one:
drop to 1 HP instead of 0 HP;
maintain Concentration until the end of your next turn;
suppress the Shield’s destruction until the end of your next turn;
immediately establish one projected Shield Face without spending an Action.
Once you use Shield Soul Never Falls, you cannot use it again until you finish a Long Rest.

TAL_SHIELD_SHIELD_WITHOUT_DISTANCE:
#### SHIELD WITHOUT DISTANCE - REALM EVOLUTION
Prerequisite: Shield-Flight Rescue, CL 15+
Your Shield Soul may appear wherever your intent can still legally reach.
Gain the following benefits:
increase Shield-Flight Rescue range to 300 feet;
when using Cover Ally through Projected Shield Face, increase its range to 120 feet;
your Shield may return to your hand from anywhere on the same battlefield at the end of your turn unless sealed, suppressed, carried across a dimensional boundary, or prevented by an equivalent effect;
when you use Returning Shield Disc, the Shield may ricochet around corners along a clear sequence of surfaces and Shield Faces, ignoring Half Cover and Three-Quarters Cover.
Shield Without Distance does not grant remote perception, teleport an ally, or pass through Total Cover, sealed Barriers, or Dimensional Locks.

TAL_SHIELD_SOVEREIGN_SHIELD_SOUL_INCARNA:
#### SOVEREIGN SHIELD-SOUL INCARNATION - REALM EVOLUTION
“Behind the cultivator stood no fortress. The fortress had learned to walk.”
Prerequisite: Projected Shield Face, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per Long Rest
Awaken a Shield Soul and manifest a sovereign rampart around your body.
Your incarnation may appear as:
a colossal ancestral shield floating behind you;
a wheel of interlocking celestial discs;
a tortoise-shell mandala;
a mirror-bright sun shield;
a mountain gate carried in one hand;
a spectral fortress marching one step behind you.
For the duration:
gain a Fly Speed of 40 feet and Hover;
increase Projected Shield Face dimensions by 20 feet in width and 10 feet in height;
increase Cover Ally range to 60 feet when a clear legal route exists;
use Active Defense once per round without spending a Reaction or expending Martial Focus;
gain one additional Reaction each round, usable only for Shield talents;
when Active Defense applies, reduce damage from the triggering attack by your Proficiency Bonus before Resistance, whether or not you know Interposing Shield;
Shield Faces created by your talents count as Barriers against physical crossing unless you choose otherwise when creating them;
your Shield talents affect incorporeal creatures, spiritual projections, ghost strikes, and physically traveling spiritual techniques normally;
regain Martial Focus whenever a hostile attack misses because of your Active Defense, once per round.
The incarnation does not automatically block teleportation, possession, gaze effects, or spiritual techniques that do not physically cross a Shield Face.

TAL_SHIELD_WORLD_SHOULDERING_FACE:
#### WORLD-SHOULDERING FACE - FACE
Prerequisite: Seal the Breach, CL 15+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A structure, siege projectile, massive creature, collapsing terrain feature, or physically traveling calamity would cross one of your Shield Faces
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per Long Rest
Until the end of your next turn, one Shield Face you created becomes a World-Shouldering Face.
It may hold against:
a collapsing gate;
a siege projectile;
a charging Gargantuan creature;
a falling tower section;
a flood front;
an avalanche edge;
a dragon’s breath;
another comparable physically arriving threat.
The GM may require a Strength saving throw, Constitution saving throw, or Cultivation Check against an appropriate DC.
Success: The face holds long enough to protect the defended side and create one meaningful opportunity: escape, counterattack, rescue, repositioning, or reinforcement.
Failure: The face still reduces the harm, buys a shorter opportunity, or changes the scene in a meaningful way before breaking.
World-Shouldering Face does not permanently hold back a sea, mountain, divine manifestation, or comparable narrative-scale threat without a project, Forged Technique, or Secret Inheritance.

TAL_SMOKE_EVIDENCE_IN_THE_ASH:
### Evidence in the Ash - Witness
Prerequisite: Funeral Incense Boundary, CL 10+
When you use Funeral Incense Boundary, record one additional fact:
whether the attacker was within 30 feet, 60 feet, or farther away;
whether the attacker was living, undead, construct, spirit, or unknown;
whether the attack came from above, below, the same level, or no normal direction;
whether the harmful effect carried CP, spell energy, a Formation, or mundane force.

TAL_SMOKE_INCENSE_BODY_OF_THE_VANISHING_:
### Incense Body of the Vanishing Witness
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 7 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Your breath, shadow, and spiritual residue become smoke-script.
For the duration:
you are lightly obscured while not in bright wind or heavy rain;
when you move at least 10 feet, leave a 5-foot cube of Smoke Veil in one space you left until the start of your next turn;
once per round, place a Smoke Trace without using your once-per-round limit;
when a hostile creature with your Smoke Trace misses you with an attack, move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks from that creature;
gain Resistance to Fire and Poison damage.

TAL_SNIPER_COUNTER_ARCHER_S_BREATH:
#### Counter-Archer’s Breath - Counter-Shot
Prerequisite: Intercepting Shot, CL 5+
When you use Intercepting Shot and successfully negate the triggering attack, you may choose one additional effect:
regain Martial Focus;
make a Scoot Shot against the attacker’s weapon or ammunition container;
move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
impose Disadvantage on the attacker’s next ranged attack before the end of its next turn.

TAL_SNIPER_FALLING_STAR_EXECUTION:
#### Falling Star Execution - Snipe
Prerequisites: Head Shot, Killing Aperture, CL 15+
When you use Head Shot against a creature at least 60 feet away, you may expend Martial Focus and spend 2 CP before the attack roll.
On a hit, the attack deals an additional 4d10 damage.
If this attack reduces the target to 0 Hit Points, choose one:
the target dies instantly if it is a non-legendary creature without special survival features;
one creature within 10 feet of the target must make a Dexterity saving throw or be Blinded until the end of its next turn by debris, blood, bone, splinters, shattered stone, or Qi backlash;
the projectile continues into a second legal target within 30 feet of the first target and makes one secondary attack with Disadvantage;
the death or collapse becomes silent and precise, leaving no obvious source of the shot to creatures that did not perceive your position.
This talent intentionally replaces the older gore-focused Fragmenting Shot with a broader Tianxia execution effect. The GM can allow a brutal visual expression if it suits the table.

TAL_SNIPER_FORMATION_ANCHOR_SHOT:
#### Formation Anchor Shot - Snipe, Utility
Prerequisite: Trap Technician, CL 5+
When you can perceive an exposed formation anchor, ritual node, talisman nail, ward-pin, hinge-rune, banner knot, or similar physical focus, you may expend Martial Focus and make a Snipe Shot against it.
On a hit, choose one:
suppress one minor function of the anchor until the start of your next turn;
impose Disadvantage on the next check made to activate or maintain the formation before the start of your next turn;
deal normal damage to the anchor;
create an Aimed Line to that anchor for yourself or one ally until the end of your next turn.
Important or scene-defining anchors may require a project, opposed Cultivation Check, or multiple successful shots.

TAL_SNIPER_HUNDRED_BREATH_WAIT:
#### Hundred-Breath Wait - Focus, Mark
Prerequisites: CL 11+
If you spend at least one full round observing a target without attacking it, you may mark it with a Hundred-Breath Wait.
For 1 minute or until you attack another target, your next Snipe Shot against the marked target gains the following benefits:
it has an Aimed Line;
it ignores Disadvantage from long range;
it gains a bonus to damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
if it misses, you regain Martial Focus.
You can maintain only one Hundred-Breath Wait at a time.

TAL_SNIPER_MERIDIAN_GRAZING_SHOT:
#### Meridian-Grazing Shot - Snipe
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Your shot grazes a meridian crossing, nerve line, spirit channel, or armor seam.
On a hit, choose one:
the target cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn;
the target has Disadvantage on the next Constitution saving throw it makes to maintain Concentration before the start of your next turn;
the target has Disadvantage on the next Strength or Dexterity saving throw it makes before the start of your next turn;
the target cannot regain Hit Points or Temporary HP until the start of your next turn.

TAL_SNIPER_SEVER_THE_NAME_FROM_THE_DISTA:
#### Sever the Name from the Distance - Mark
Prerequisites: CL 15+
When you hit a creature with a Snipe Shot, you may spend 1 CP to create a Nascent Mark for 1 minute.
While the Mark lasts:
you always know the direction to the target while it remains on the same plane and within 1 mile;
your first ranged attack against it each turn has an Aimed Line;
it gains no benefit from being Invisible against your Sniper talents;
if it teleports or uses a movement technique, you may use your Reaction to learn its new exact location if it remains within 1 mile.
A creature can end the Mark early by succeeding on a Charisma saving throw at the end of its turn, by entering a sealed anti-divination effect, or by using an appropriate cleansing technique.

TAL_SNIPER_SHOOT_THE_RETURNING_BLADE:
#### Shoot the Returning Blade - Counter-Shot
Prerequisites: Intercepting Shot, CL 15+
When a projectile, thrown weapon, flying sword, returning weapon, animated weapon, or weapon-like technique passes within your weapon’s normal range, you may use your Reaction to make a ranged weapon attack against it.
On a hit, choose one:
knock it to the ground in an unoccupied space within 30 feet;
redirect it toward a legal target within 30 feet, comparing your attack roll to the new target’s AC;
break its return path, preventing it from returning until the end of its next turn;
suppress one non-artifact weapon technique carried by it until the start of your next turn.
Artifact weapons, sovereign flying swords, Secret Inheritance weapons, and scene-defining projectiles may require an opposed Cultivation Check.

TAL_SNIPER_SPIRIT_WEIGHTED_PROJECTILE:
#### Spirit-Weighted Projectile - Snipe
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When making a Snipe Shot, you may expend Martial Focus to fill the projectile with a thin line of Qi.
On a hit, the attack counts as magical or cultivation-enhanced for overcoming Resistance or Immunity to nonmagical attacks.
In addition, choose one:
the projectile remains lodged until removed and cannot be casually shaken loose;
the target’s Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of your next turn;
the target cannot benefit from being Invisible against your next ranged attack before the end of your next turn;
the target’s next Concentration saving throw before the start of your next turn has Disadvantage.

TAL_SNIPER_STAR_SCRAPER_LINE:
#### Star-Scraper Line - Snipe, Line
Prerequisites: Perfect Shot, CL 11+
As a Bonus Action, you may impose Disadvantage on your next ranged weapon attack before the end of your turn to increase the weapon’s base range to 1 mile for that attack.
You may attack a target without direct line of sight or line of effect if all the following are true:
you know the target’s exact location;
there is at least some straight open path between you and the target, even if that path must arc over terrain, over a wall, through a canyon, above a mountain ridge, or across open sky;
the target is not completely enclosed by protective surfaces;
the projectile could plausibly travel the full route.
The attack ignores ordinary cover along intermediate parts of the path, but the target’s immediate cover applies unless another talent ignores it.
If an ally, familiar, spirit, scouting technique, formation, or divination provides live exact location, this talent can exploit that information.

TAL_SNIPER_SUPPRESS_THE_FORMATION_LINE:
#### Suppress the Formation Line - Snipe, Utility
Prerequisites: Formation Anchor Shot, CL 11+
When you hit an exposed formation anchor, ward pin, talisman array node, siege trigger, ritual channel, or domain focus with Formation Anchor Shot, you may spend 1 CP or expend Martial Focus to attempt a deeper suppression.
Make a Sniper technique check using your attack bonus or Cultivation Check, whichever is more appropriate. The DC is the formation’s DC, the creator’s Cultivation Save DC, or a GM-set DC for the structure.
On a success, choose one:
suppress one function for 1 minute;
open one 5-foot gap in a Barrier-like effect until the start of your next turn;
impose Disadvantage on checks to maintain the effect for 1 minute;
prevent one triggered defense from activating this round;
mark the anchor so the next attack against it before the end of your next turn has Advantage.
On a failure, the anchor is not suppressed, but your shot reveals one visible consequence, weakness, or protective response if any exists.

TAL_SOUND_READ_THE_VIBRATION:
#### Read the Vibration
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Cost: None
Listen to vibration in air, ground, water, walls, objects, weapons, or living bodies.
Make a Sound Check against a DC set by the GM or opposed by a relevant Dexterity (Stealth), Dexterity (Sleight of Hand), Wisdom (Perception), or cultivation concealment check.
On a success, learn one:
whether a creature moved through a nearby space recently;
whether a wall, door, vessel, bell, bridge, or barrier is hollow, cracked, tensioned, sealed, or reinforced;
whether an invisible or hidden creature is making meaningful sound within range;
whether an object or structure is resonant, brittle, or warded against sound;
whether a spoken phrase, bell, song, or chant carries supernatural influence.
Read the Vibration does not automatically reveal exact location, see through walls, identify all creatures, or bypass stealth. It provides a clue or contested perception method.

TAL_SOUND_SOUL_ECHO_HEARING:
#### Soul-Echo Hearing - Hearing, Soul-Sound
Prerequisite: Read the Vibration, CL 10+
You can hear the echo of spirits, possession pressure, soul wounds, oath-shaken voices, false speech, and names spoken with supernatural weight.
As an Action, make a Sound Check against a creature within 60 feet or a place you are investigating.
On a success, learn one:
whether a creature is possessed, spirit-bound, or haunted;
whether a spoken statement carries supernatural coercion;
whether a name, title, vow, or mantra was recently used with power;
whether a ghost, echo, or residual scream remains in the area;
whether a Silence effect is natural, magical, spiritual, or domain-based.
Soul-Echo Hearing does not read thoughts or reveal lies automatically.

TAL_SOUND_SOUND_INITIATION:
#### Sound Initiation
When you first learn Sound, choose one expression as your primary method:
voice;
bell;
drum;
zither or stringed instrument;
flute or reed;
whistle;
clap or footfall;
mantra or scripture chant;
bone resonance;
another GM-approved sound practice.
This choice is descriptive unless a variant or feature says otherwise.
You learn to create minor cultivated sound within 60 feet. As an Action, you may create one harmless sound no louder than a shout, throw your voice to a visible point, dampen one small noise, cause one unattended object to hum, or cause a small surface to vibrate.
These minor sounds cannot deal damage, impose conditions, replace a check, transmit complex messages through barriers, or imitate a specific creature well enough to deceive without a check.

TAL_SOUND_SOUND_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
#### Sound-Sovereign Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign vessel of world-ringing vibration.
For the duration:
gain Resistance to Thunder and Psychic damage;
gain Blindsight 30 feet based on vibration and soul-sound;
Resonant Note may target two creatures within range instead of one;
once per turn when a creature fails a saving throw against your Sound talent, it cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn;
you may speak or transmit through your own Sound talents even inside ordinary Silence;
Soundwalk Step range increases by 30 feet;
your Sound talents ignore ordinary Thunder Resistance.
Sound-Sovereign Incarnation does not ignore immunity, artifact silence, Domain suppression, or Total Cover unless another feature says so.

TAL_SOUND_THUNDER_MERIDIAN_STRIKE:
#### Thunder-Meridian Strike - Voice, Resonance
Prerequisite: Body Resonance Strike or Throat-Thunder Body, CL 5+
When you hit with a melee attack or Unarmed Strike, spend 2 Stamina or 2 CP.
The target takes 2d8 Thunder damage and makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn;
Speed reduced by 10 feet until the start of your next turn;
Disadvantage on its next Concentration saving throw before the start of your next turn;
apply Resonance until the end of your next turn.

TAL_SPACE_SPATIAL_AWARENESS:
### Base Ability - Spatial Awareness
Tag: Anchor Art.
Action Type: Multi-Mode
Split Candidate Buckets: action, passive
Timing Detail: Passive and Action
Split Review Decision: split_required_distinct_combat_buckets
Recommended Factory Realization: modes=PASSIVE_SPATIAL_AWARENESS->passive, ACTION_ACTIVE_INSPECTION->action
Range: 60 feet.
Cost: 0 CP for passive awareness; 1 CP to inspect actively.
Passive Effect: You sense obvious spatial disturbances within range. You know when a creature you can perceive teleports, opens a portal, enters or exits a pocket space, uses extradimensional storage, crosses a planar boundary, or forces a space wider or narrower than it should be.
Active Inspection: As an Action, spend 1 CP and choose one creature, object, doorway, area, or visible spatial effect within range. Make a Cultivation Check against the effect’s creator or against a DC set by rarity and concealment.
On a success, learn up to two of the following:
whether the target is spatially sealed;
whether the target has teleported within the last hour;
whether the target carries extradimensional storage;
whether the target is linked to an anchor;
whether a doorway or surface hides a pocket space;
whether a barrier blocks teleportation;
the approximate CL of the spatial effect;
whether the disturbance is stable, decaying, trapped, or contested.
Spatial Awareness does not reveal secret doors unless they are spatially distorted, and it does not identify ordinary locks.

TAL_SPIRIT_COMPANIONS_BINDING_SEAL:
### Binding Seal
A Binding Seal restrains or compels a spirit.
Binding Seal is Restricted or Forbidden in many orthodox sects unless used to contain hostile spirits, seal plague spirits, imprison murderous ghosts, restrain demons, secure a battlefield threat, or protect civilians.
To place a Binding Seal on an unwilling spirit, the spirit must be one of the following:
- defeated;
- restrained;
- trapped in a vessel;
- inside a prepared circle, shrine, formation, body, or object;
- reduced to 0 Hit Points or equivalent spiritual collapse;
- willingly accepting punishment;
- unable to flee because of another legal effect.
The spirit makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Cultivation Save DC.
On a failure, the Binding Seal takes hold.
On a success, the spirit resists and the Action or ritual is wasted, though the GM may allow partial containment for a scene.
While Binding Seal holds:
- the spirit cannot willingly move beyond the bond's range or vessel limits;
- the spirit cannot directly attack you unless the seal cracks;
- you may command limited service through Manifest the Spirit Nature;
- each coercive command that violates the spirit's Nature or Taboo increases Bond Strain by 1;
- the spirit may seek loopholes, sabotage, malicious compliance, or escape.
A Binding Seal is not friendship. It is a chain.

TAL_SPIRIT_COMPANIONS_COVENANT_BOND:
### Covenant Bond
A Covenant Bond is a willing relationship with a spirit.
The spirit must be willing, persuaded, repaid, rescued, honored, defeated honorably, inherited, or otherwise narratively available.
A Covenant Bond creates a Major Spirit Bond.
While the Covenant Bond remains stable:
- you and the spirit can communicate simple ideas while within 1 mile of each other;
- you always know the direction to the spirit while on the same plane or layer of reality;
- the spirit can be called, dismissed, or sheltered according to its Manifestation rules;
- the spirit may use Spirit Nature Expressions you have unlocked;
- you may make offerings to reduce Bond Strain;
- the spirit may refuse commands that violate its Nature, Need, or Taboo.
Covenant Bond is the default ethical mode of this sphere.

TAL_SPIRIT_COMPANIONS_MANIFESTATION_LIMI:
### Manifestation Limits
A spirit cannot use a Nature Expression if:
- the expression violates its core Nature;
- the spirit is sealed, asleep, banished, or suppressed;
- the host or vessel is broken;
- Bond Strain is at crisis and the GM rules the spirit refuses;
- the spirit's Taboo has just been violated;
- you cannot pay the required cost;
- the effect requires a legal target or origin the spirit does not have.

TAL_SWORD_FLOWING_WATER_SLASH:
#### Flowing Water Slash - Hand
Trigger: You hit a creature with a Sword attack
Use Limit: Once per turn
Choose one:
move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks from the target;
move around the target into one adjacent legal space;
gain +1 AC against the target until the start of your next turn;
if the target bears your Sword Intent, reduce its Speed by 5 feet until the start of your next turn.

TAL_SWORD_HEART_OF_THE_SWORD:
#### Heart of the Sword - Sword-Heart
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Form a stable Sword Heart.
While wielding a Sword, controlling a Flying Sword, or maintaining a Sword-Qi blade:
gain Advantage on saving throws against Charmed and Frightened;
gain Advantage on checks made to resist being Disarmed;
recognize whether your own Sword Intent is being suppressed, imitated, or spiritually distorted;
once per round when a creature bearing your Sword Intent misses you, move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks from that creature.
Heart of the Sword is a prerequisite for advanced Sword-Heart talents.

TAL_SWORD_IRON_SWORD_BODY:
#### Iron Sword Body - Hand
Prerequisite: Body Refining, CL 5+
While wielding a Sword:
use Constitution for Sword attack and damage rolls if higher;
use Constitution as your Sword key ability;
spend Stamina instead of CP on Sword talents;
gain +1 AC;
gain Advantage on saving throws against forced Disarm effects.
Iron Sword Body does not grant Sword Beyond Hand by itself.

TAL_SWORD_SEVERING_FATE:
#### Severing Fate
“The sword did not cut the body first. It cut the future in which the enemy believed it would survive unchanged.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Heart of the Sword, Sword Intent Manifestation, hidden fate-severing scripture
Action Type: Action
Range: Sword reach or 120 feet through Sword Qi
Cost: 15 CP or 15 Stamina
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature, object, temporary Barrier, or ordinary ongoing supernatural effect.
##### Creature
Make one Sword attack or ranged Cultivation Attack with:
Advantage;
no Disadvantage;
Resistance to Slashing and Force damage is ignored.
Hit: Deal:
12d10 Slashing or Force damage
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose three:
become Stunned until the end of your next turn;
cannot regain HP until the end of your next turn;
Speed becomes 0 until the end of your next turn;
cannot take Reactions until the end of your next turn;
end one ordinary ongoing supernatural effect affecting it;
suppress one temporary Barrier, summon, or regeneration effect until the end of your next turn;
apply Meridian-Cutting Strike without spending its cost.
Successful Save: Choose one.
##### Object, Barrier, or Effect
Make one Cultivation Check against a GM-set DC.
On a success, choose one:
cut open one major breach;
dispel one ordinary ongoing effect;
sever one temporary supernatural tether;
destroy one temporary Barrier;
disable one Formation Anchor until repaired.
Severing Fate does not automatically destroy:
artifacts;
Formation cores;
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
Realm-defining structures;
permanent karmic bonds;
major narrative destinies.
Those may still be contested or meaningfully damaged according to the GM.

TAL_SWORD_SWORD_QI_STEP:
#### Sword-Qi Step - Sword-Qi
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 30 feet
Cost: 2 CP or 2 Stamina
Move to one visible unoccupied space.
This movement:
does not provoke opportunity attacks;
may cross occupied spaces;
cannot cross sealed barriers;
cannot cross a Dimensional Lock;
is rapid sword-guided movement, not general Space control.
If you end adjacent to a creature bearing your Sword Intent, gain Advantage on your next Sword attack against it before the end of the turn.

TAL_SWORD_SWORD_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
#### Sword-Sovereign Incarnation
Prerequisite: Heart of the Sword, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP or 15 Stamina
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign embodiment of the sword path.
For the duration:
gain Fly Speed 40 feet and Hover;
gain Resistance to Slashing, Force, and Psychic damage;
Sword Intent Strike extra damage becomes 4d10;
Sword Qi Wave damage becomes 6d10;
Sword Intent lasts until the end of your next turn;
once per turn after applying Sword Intent, move 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks;
once per turn when a creature bearing your Sword Intent misses you, make one Sword attack or Sword Qi Wave as a Reaction;
ordinary disarming effects fail against you.

TAL_THE_HIDDEN_EYE_COURT_OF_THE_HIDDEN_E:
##### Court of the Hidden Eye - Martial Domain
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Uses: Once per Long Rest
Area: 60-foot Emanation originating from you
Establish a Martial Domain of sharpened observation.
While the Domain lasts:
you know when a creature you can perceive enters or leaves the Domain;
you may take the Search action as a Bonus Action;
Analyze requires a Bonus Action without expending Martial Focus;
when you successfully Analyze a creature inside the Domain, learn one additional Analyzable Characteristic;
a creature Analyzed by you cannot gain Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made against you;
allies of your choice inside the Domain add half your Proficiency Bonus, rounded down, to Passive Perception.
Court of the Hidden Eye does not grant sight through Total Cover, automatically reveal hidden creatures, or make every creature inside the Domain Analyzed.

TAL_THE_HIDDEN_EYE_HEAVEN_WATCHING_SURVE:
##### Heaven-Watching Survey - Awareness, Realm Evolution
Time: 10 minutes
Area: 1-mile-radius sphere centered on you
Uses: Once per Long Rest
Enter a state of profound cultivated awareness.
Learn the following about the area:
major terrain features;
obvious concentrations of creatures;
recent large-scale movement;
active battles, fires, collapses, or comparable disturbances;
the presence and general direction of a magical effect or Formation whose scale is large enough to influence the surveyed area;
one broad clue about a creature Analyzed by you if it passed through the area within the last 24 hours.
Heaven-Watching Survey does not reveal exact creature locations, penetrate sealed spaces, identify every individual, read thoughts, or replace Divination.
Heaven-Watching Survey is a magical cultivation effect.

TAL_THE_HIDDEN_EYE_SOVEREIGN_HIDDEN_EYE_:
##### Sovereign Hidden Eye Incarnation - Realm Evolution
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Uses: Once per Long Rest
Manifest the perfected attention of your Nascent Soul.
While the Incarnation lasts:
you hold Martial Focus and cannot lose it unless you choose to expend it;
when you expend Martial Focus, regain it at the start of your next turn;
you may Analyze one creature you can perceive at the start of each of your turns without spending an Action or making a check;
when you automatically Analyze a creature this way, learn one Analyzable Characteristic;
you have Blindsight within 30 feet;
you have Advantage on Initiative rolls, Search checks, Study checks, and saving throws against Illusion effects;
creatures Analyzed by you cannot gain Advantage on attack rolls against you.
Sovereign Hidden Eye Incarnation does not reveal creatures behind Total Cover or grant unrestricted knowledge.

TAL_THE_HIDDEN_EYE_TRACK_THE_SCENE:
##### Track the Scene - Awareness
You have Advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks made to find or follow tracks.
When you successfully follow tracks no more than 24 hours old, you learn broad information about the tracked creatures’ behavior while leaving the trail, such as whether they:
paused to rest or eat;
split into multiple groups;
carried a heavy burden;
moved hurriedly;
fought or argued;
attempted to conceal their trail;
suffered an injury;
changed travel pace;
were joined by another creature.
You learn detailed information only when the creatures left physical evidence supporting that conclusion.

TAL_THE_HIDDEN_EYE_TRAINED_AWARENESS:
##### Trained Awareness - Awareness
Gain proficiency in one of the following skills:
Intelligence (Investigation);
Wisdom (Perception);
Wisdom (Survival).
You may learn this talent multiple times, choosing a different skill each time.

TAL_THE_HIDDEN_EYE_WALKING_DREAM_SENTINE:
##### Walking-Dream Sentinel - Awareness, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Somnambulance
When an effect would give you the Unconscious condition solely by putting you to sleep, you may enter a walking-dream state instead.
While in the walking-dream state:
you do not gain the Unconscious condition from that sleep effect;
you remain aware enough to move, take Actions, Bonus Actions, and Reactions, and defend yourself;
you have Disadvantage on Intelligence and Charisma ability checks;
you cannot maintain Concentration;
you cannot use a technique that requires careful speech, patient study, or detailed tool use unless the GM decides otherwise.
The walking-dream state ends when the sleep effect ends.
Walking-Dream Sentinel does not prevent the Unconscious condition caused by reaching 0 Hit Points, a poison, a physical injury, or an effect that is not sleep.

TAL_TRAP_COURT_OF_THE_HIDDEN_NAIL:
### Court of the Hidden Nail — Martial Domain
“The battlefield was not empty when you arrived. You were merely allowed to believe it was.”
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short or long rest
Establish a 30-foot-radius Emanation centered on yourself.
While the Court persists:
your active trap limit increases by your Proficiency Bonus;
once per turn, set one trap in an unoccupied space within your reach without spending an Action;
a trap set this way lasts until the Court ends or until triggered;
your warned allies do not trigger your traps inside the Court;
when one of your traps triggers, move up to 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks, or regain Martial Focus if it is absent;
you know which of your traps inside the Court triggered, was disarmed, or was destroyed.
Court of the Hidden Nail ends early if you have the Incapacitated condition.

TAL_TRAP_THE_EMPTY_ROAD_WAS_NEVER_EMPTY:
### The Empty Road Was Never Empty
“A careless enemy enters a battlefield. A wise enemy asks who decided where the battlefield begins.”
Prerequisite: Trap sphere, Court of the Hidden Nail, CL 17+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: Initiative is rolled, or one hostile creature enters a space within 60 feet that you can perceive
Use Limit: Once per long rest
For 1 minute, establish a 60-foot-radius Emanation centered on yourself.
When you activate the inheritance, place a number of temporary traps equal to your Proficiency Bonus in legal unoccupied spaces within the Emanation.
For the duration:
your active trap limit increases by your Proficiency Bonus;
each trap you set may use two compatible Trigger talents without expending Martial Focus;
once per turn, after a hostile creature moves at least 5 feet inside the Emanation, relocate one untriggered trap you set to one legal unoccupied space within 10 feet of its previous location;
a relocated trap remains physical and must have a plausible route, anchor, and mechanism;
warned allies do not trigger your traps;
you immediately know when one of your traps inside the Emanation triggers, is disarmed, or is destroyed.
This inheritance does not create permanent infrastructure. It expresses preparation at mythic speed and scale for one decisive scene.

TAL_TRAP_TRAP_WITHIN_THE_TRAP:
### Trap Within the Trap — Trigger Talent
Prerequisite: False Trigger, CL 15+
When False Trigger produces its warning sound, immediately place one additional trap in one unoccupied space within 5 feet of the original trap.
The additional trap:
must use a pattern you know;
counts against your active trap limit;
lasts for 1 minute or until triggered;
cannot also use Trap Within the Trap.

TAL_UNMAKING_BLACK_STAR_VESSEL:
### Black Star Vessel — Black Vein
**Prerequisite:** CL 15+, Fourth Ruin Form: Black-Vein Body
When you would suffer Ruin Backlash, you may choose to become a Black Star Vessel until the end of your next turn.
While in this state:
- you do not reduce Black Vein Strain after the triggering Ruin Backlash;
- your Ruin damage ignores Resistance;
- once before the state ends, when you hit with an Unmaking talent, add 8d10 Ruin damage;
- you cannot regain HP;
- you have Disadvantage on death saving throws.
When the state ends, suffer Ruin Backlash again.
If this second Backlash would reduce you to 0 HP, you may remain at 1 HP instead, but your Black Vein Strain becomes 6 and you gain one level of Exhaustion.

TAL_UNMAKING_FIFTH_RUIN_FORM_DOMAIN_OF_C:
### Fifth Ruin Form: Domain of Collapse — Ruin Form, Anti-Structure
**Prerequisite:** CL 15+, Hollowing Field
**Action Type:** Action
**Range:** Self
**Area:** 60-foot emanation
**Duration:** Concentration, up to 1 minute
**Cost:** 4 CP
You become the center of a collapsing agreement.
For the duration:
- hostile creatures in the area cannot regain HP on the same turn they take Ruin damage from you;
- temporary qi structures, summoned constructs, barriers, wards, and non-Secret defensive effects in the area take Ruin damage equal to your Cultivation Level at the start of each of your turns;
- once per turn, when you deal Ruin damage to a creature in the area, add 4d10 Ruin damage;
- when a hostile creature in the area casts, activates, or sustains a technique with Concentration or an equivalent state, it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take Ruin damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus d10.
At the end of each of your turns while the domain persists, suffer one cost:
- gain 2 Black Vein Strain;
- take Ruin self-damage equal to 5d6 + your Proficiency Bonus;
- destroy one non-artifact External Channel you are carrying;
- reduce your current and maximum HP by 10 until you finish a Long Rest.
If the domain ends because your Concentration breaks, suffer Ruin Backlash twice.

TAL_VERDANT_GROWTH_INHERITANCE_ORCHARD_P:
### Inheritance Orchard Preparation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
During downtime, plant an inheritance orchard, living archive, medicinal grove, temple tree, root-library, or clan shelter.
This is not an ordinary combat talent and does not complete instantly.
A completed project may provide story benefits such as:
shelter for refugees;
medicinal herb production;
seed-script records;
training grounds for Verdant Growth disciples;
grove nodes for Formations;
living witnesses to oaths;
seasonal fruit that supports cultivation sessions;
a sanctuary against poison, famine, drought, or corruption.
The GM sets time, cost, land, caretakers, enemies, and maintenance requirements.

TAL_VERDANT_GROWTH_ORCHARD_OF_BITTER_MED:
### Orchard of Bitter Medicine - Bloom
Prerequisite: CL 10+, Graft the Wound Shut
When you use Graft the Wound Shut, choose one additional benefit:
end the Poisoned condition on the target;
allow the target to repeat one saving throw against a disease or poison affecting it;
reduce ongoing poison damage the target takes before the start of your next turn by 2d8 + your key ability modifier;
remove one Growth Mark from the target and grant Temporary HP equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus.
This does not cure magical disease, curses, or corruption unless the GM rules the affliction is plant, poison, or disease based.

TAL_VERDANT_GROWTH_ROOTED_WITNESS_GROVE:
### Rooted Witness Grove - Bloom, Spirit
Prerequisite: CL 10+
You can Study a Living Claim to learn what passed near it.
As an Action, touch one of your Living Claims that lasted at least 1 minute.
Ask one of the following questions about events since the claim was created:
which creatures passed within 10 feet of it;
whether blood was spilled nearby;
whether Fire damage affected the area;
whether a creature lied, wept, prayed, or swore an oath within 10 feet;
whether an undead, construct, fiend, celestial, fey, or spirit passed nearby.
The answer is sensory and plantlike: pressure, scent, tremor, sap-memory, pollen, or leaf direction. It does not identify a creature by name unless the plant already knew that creature.

TAL_VERDANT_GROWTH_THE_SEED_THAT_REMEMBE:
### The Seed That Remembers the Forest
“A single seed falls. The forest that has not yet been born recognizes its ancestor.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Grove Domain: Court of Root and Branch, Rooted Witness Grove, hidden seed-line scripture
Action Type: Action
Range: 300 feet
Area: Up to a 120-foot-radius area containing at least one legal Living Medium, Grove Node, seed, corpse, root, wooden object, or willing living creature
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
You plant one impossible seed of your Dao into the battlefield.
The area becomes a nascent forest of root-lines, branch choices, medicinal bloom, thorn law, and living witness.
For the duration:
create up to six Living Claims anywhere in the area when the inheritance begins;
every creature of your choice that starts its turn in the area gains 1 Growth Mark;
allies of your choice in the area gain Temporary HP equal to your CL at the start of their turns;
enemies treat your Living Claims as difficult terrain;
once per round, when an enemy with a Growth Mark damages an ally, use one Verdant Response without spending a Reaction or Growth Mark;
when a creature with at least 3 Growth Marks would be reduced to 0 HP, you may either allow the death or bind it in roots at 1 HP and Restrained until the inheritance ends.
When the inheritance ends, choose one of the following:
the growth withers, leaving harmless leaves, seed-dust, broken roots, and disturbed soil;
one noncombat seedling remains as a story mark;
one willing creature carries a harmless seed-script memory of what happened;
the GM preserves a living consequence for future story.
The inheritance does not create permanent resources, a finished forest, free food, rare herbs, or a safe settlement unless the GM makes it the seed of a separate project.

TAL_VOID_ERODE_TECHNIQUE:
### Erode Technique - Null
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A creature within 60 feet gains Temporary HP, damage reduction, an AC bonus, a Speed bonus, Resistance, Invisible, or a cost reduction from an ordinary temporary effect
Cost: 1 CP or 1 Stamina
Choose one benefit created by the triggering effect.
Apply one option:
reduce Temporary HP gained by your Proficiency Bonus;
reduce one damage reduction by your Proficiency Bonus until the start of your next turn;
reduce one AC bonus by 1 until the start of your next turn;
reduce one Speed bonus by 10 feet until the start of your next turn;
suppress one temporary Resistance until the start of your next turn;
prevent Invisible from that effect until the start of your next turn;
prevent one cost reduction from reducing a cost below its listed value.
Erode Technique cannot affect artifacts, Domains, Secret Inheritances, Formation cores, Realm-defining transformations, or permanent features.

TAL_VOID_NO_PURCHASE_BODY:
### No-Purchase Body - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Void Shell, CL 10+
While Void Shell is active:
Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage;
forced movement against you is reduced by 10 feet;
when a creature hits you with a melee attack, you may apply one Void Pressure from Void Needle to that creature once per turn.

TAL_VOID_NULLIFICATION_SEAL:
### Nullification Seal - Null
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP or 5 Stamina
Choose one creature within range.
The target makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one active ordinary temporary benefit affecting the target. Suppress it while this talent lasts.
Possible benefits include:
one AC bonus;
one Speed bonus;
one temporary Resistance;
one flight effect;
one invisibility effect;
one regeneration effect;
one cost reduction;
one ordinary stance or aura.
At the end of each of the target’s turns, it repeats the saving throw, ending the suppression on itself on a success.
Successful Save: Suppress the selected benefit until the start of your next turn.

TAL_VOID_RETURN_THE_TECHNIQUE_TO_NOTHING:
### Return the Technique to Nothing
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Void sphere, GM approval
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A creature you can see within 120 feet activates a spell, sphere talent, Forged Technique, or supernatural technique
Cost: 15 CP or 15 Stamina
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Name the technique as it forms.
Make a Cultivation Check contested by the triggering creature’s Cultivation Check.
You Succeed: The technique fails to take hold. Its resource cost is spent. If it was an ongoing effect already present, suppress it until the end of your next turn instead.You Fail: The technique resolves normally, and the triggering creature becomes Hollowed until the start of your next turn.
Return the Technique to Nothing cannot permanently erase:
a Path;
a sphere;
a creature;
an artifact;
a Domain;
a Secret Inheritance;
a Formation core;
a Realm-defining transformation;
a permanent karmic bond.
A Domain, Secret Inheritance, artifact, Formation core, or Realm-defining technique may require a special scene, an opposed Cultivation Check with Disadvantage, or may simply be immune at the GM’s discretion.

TAL_VOID_VOID_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
### Void-Sovereign Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 10 CP or 10 Stamina
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign outline around a hollow center.
While this incarnation lasts:
gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and Hover;
gain Resistance to Force, Necrotic, and Psychic damage;
use Empty Step once per turn without spending CP or Stamina;
your Void Needle targets up to two creatures within range;
creatures hit by your Void Needle become Hollowed until the start of your next turn;
when a Hollowed creature misses you with an attack roll, use Empty Step up to 10 feet without spending a Reaction.

TAL_VOID_VOID_TRAINING:
### Void Training
When you learn Void:
gain Void Needle;
learn one Mortal Realm Void talent for which you meet the prerequisites;
choose Force, Necrotic, or Psychic as your default Void damage type.
Whenever a Void talent lets you choose Force, Necrotic, or Psychic damage, you may use your default type without deciding again.

TAL_VOID_WORLD_OF_NOTHING:
### World of Nothing - Void Domain Evolution
Prerequisite: Court of the Empty Horizon, CL 15+
When you create Court of the Empty Horizon, you may spend 4 additional CP or Stamina.
If you do, the Domain becomes World of Nothing.
Additional effects:
allies inside the Domain may ignore Difficult Terrain created by the Domain;
allies inside gain Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus at the start of their turns;
enemies inside cannot regain CP or Stamina from ordinary temporary effects;
the first time an enemy inside the Domain gains an ordinary temporary benefit each round, that benefit is suppressed until the start of its next turn;
when an enemy fails the Domain’s saving throw, it also cannot benefit from Invisible until the start of its next turn.

TAL_WATER_ABYSSAL_PRESSURE_SEAL:
##### Abyssal Pressure Seal - Pressure
When a creature is Restrained by Whirlpool Prison, affected by Drowning Pressure, or inside your Court of the Endless Tide, you may use an action and spend 4 CP to seal it in abyssal pressure.
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
On a failed save, until the end of your next turn:
it is Restrained;
it cannot speak clearly;
it cannot regain Hit Points;
it has Disadvantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain Concentration;
if it attempts to teleport, fly, or move through a planar or spatial technique, it must first succeed on a Water check contested by your Cultivation Save DC.
On a successful save, it is Soaked and cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.

TAL_WATER_CLEANSING_WATER:
##### Cleansing Water - Cleansing
When you create a Cleansing Basin, improve it as follows:
the area can end the Burning, covered-in-smoke, or mundane contamination state on one creature each round;
an ally that benefits from the Basin gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
the Basin can wash away mundane poison, acid residue, dust, ash, or filth from a creature or object.
Cleansing Water does not cure magical disease, regenerate injury, remove curses, or replace the Life sphere.

TAL_WATER_COURT_OF_THE_ENDLESS_TIDE:
##### Court of the Endless Tide - Domain
Action Type: Bonus Action
Area: 60-foot Emanation from you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 3 CP
You establish a tide court. The battlefield gains a spiritual slope toward your chosen sea.
While the Domain lasts:
you may maintain one additional Basin or Current;
Water Lash may originate from any point inside the Domain;
once on each of your turns, you may use Return the Flow without using a Bonus Action;
hostile creatures treat your Basins and Currents as Difficult Terrain;
allies of your choice ignore Difficult Terrain from your Water effects;
when a hostile creature fails a saving throw against one of your Water effects, you may move it 10 feet into a legal space;
when you create a Basin, you may choose two forms from Shape Current instead of one, such as Mist plus Pressure or Cleansing plus Flow.
The Domain does not fill the entire area with physical water unless you use talents that create floodwater.

TAL_WATER_CRUSHING_CURRENT:
##### Crushing Current - Pressure
When a creature fails its saving throw against your Pressure Basin, you may apply Drowning Pressure until the start of your next turn.
Choose one effect:
the target cannot speak clearly;
the target cannot take Reactions;
the target has Disadvantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain Concentration;
the target cannot regain Hit Points until the start of your next turn.
If the target was already Soaked, you may choose two effects.

TAL_WATER_MIRROR_WATER_REPLY:
##### Mirror-Water Reply - Mist / Current
When a creature misses you or an ally inside your Mist Basin or while Soaked, you may use your Reaction and spend 1 CP.
Choose one:
move the missed creature 10 feet into a legal space if it fails a Strength saving throw;
move the protected creature 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
make the attacker Soaked and give the next attack roll against it Advantage before the start of your next turn.

TAL_WATER_OCEAN_SOVEREIGN_INCARNATION:
##### Ocean-Sovereign Incarnation - Realm Evolution
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP Uses: Once per long rest unless a feature says otherwise
You become a sovereign current. Your body, breath, defense, and water effects move as one sea.
While this incarnation lasts:
you gain Swim Speed equal to twice your Speed and can breathe underwater;
Water Lash range becomes 300 feet;
Water Lash may originate from any Water Source, Basin, or Current you control within range;
once on each of your turns, you may use Return the Flow without an action;
your Water Control Limit increases by two Basins or Currents;
you may maintain Court of the Endless Tide without Concentration while this incarnation lasts;
when a creature fails a save against your Water effect, you may apply Soaked, move it 10 feet, or impose one Drowning Pressure option;
when you reduce damage with Water Shield, you may move the protected creature up to 30 feet.

TAL_WATER_SACRED_SPRING:
##### Sacred Spring - Spring / Project
You may perform a 10-minute rite at a clean Water Source or Cleansing Basin, spending 3 CP.
For 24 hours, the site becomes a Sacred Spring. A creature that spends 10 minutes washing, drinking, or meditating there gains one benefit:
remove one level of Exhaustion caused by thirst, heat, smoke, forced march, or environmental hardship;
gain Advantage on the next saving throw against Poisoned or disease before the next long rest;
recover additional Hit Points equal to your CL during a short rest;
cleanse mundane filth, ash, smoke residue, or spiritual grime visible to ordinary senses.
A Sacred Spring cannot remove curses, resurrect the dead, replace Life, or produce infinite economic water. Long-term springs require project rules, maintenance, and local spiritual geography.

TAL_WRESTLING_COURT_OF_THE_CLOSED_DISTAN:
#### Court of the Closed Distance - Martial Domain
“Inside the court, every road becomes a clinch.”
Prerequisite: CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per short rest
For the duration:
count as one size larger when initiating or maintaining grapples;
gain Advantage on saving throws and checks against Grapple, Shove, and forced movement;
dragging or carrying one Grappled creature does not cost additional movement;
when one creature within reach misses you with a melee attack, move 5 feet toward it without provoking opportunity attacks;
once per turn when one creature fails a save against your Grapple option or fails an escape check, regain Martial Focus;
one Grappled creature of your choice grants you Half Cover against creatures other than itself.
Court of the Closed Distance ends early if you become Incapacitated.

TAL_WRESTLING_CULTIVATION_SUPPRESSING_GR:
#### Cultivation-Suppressing Grip - Slam, Hold
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When you apply this Slam, choose one ordinary ongoing supernatural effect affecting the Grappled creature that you can perceive.
Make a Cultivation Check against:
10 + effect rank
For an ordinary spell, use spell level as effect rank.
For another effect without a listed rank, the GM assigns a rank based on its source and strength.
Successful Check: Suppress the effect until the start of your next turn.Successful Check by 5 or More: Dispel the effect instead when appropriate.
If the target is a summoned creature, the effect that summoned it may be suppressed until the start of your next turn.
Cultivation-Suppressing Grip does not automatically dispel:
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
artifacts;
Formation cores;
Realm-defining transformations;
permanent karmic bonds.

TAL_WRESTLING_IMPALE:
#### Impale - Hold
When you deal damage to one creature with a melee weapon wielded in two hands, use a Bonus Action to attempt to impale it.
The target makes a Strength or Dexterity saving throw, choosing which, against your Wrestling Save DC.
Failed Save: The target gains the Grappled condition.
Successful Save: No additional effect.
While the grapple lasts:
the weapon maintains the grapple instead of a free hand;
you must keep holding the weapon;
you cannot attack another creature with that weapon;
the target counts as Grappled by you for Wrestling talents;
the target escapes using your Wrestling escape DC.

TAL_WRESTLING_IRON_CLINCH:
#### Iron Clinch - Hold
While one creature is Grappled by you:
gain +1 AC against that creature;
gain Advantage on saving throws against forced movement caused by that creature;
the creature cannot gain Advantage on its escape check merely because an ally uses the Help action.

TAL_WRESTLING_JOINT_LOCKING_SCRIPTURE:
#### Joint-Locking Scripture - Slam, Hold
Prerequisite: CL 5+
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one until the start of your next turn:
cannot take Reactions;
has Disadvantage on weapon attack rolls;
has Disadvantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws;
cannot effectively use one held object requiring two hands.
Successful Save: Cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.

TAL_WRESTLING_MERIDIAN_CRUSHING_CLINCH:
#### Meridian-Crushing Clinch - Slam, Hold
Prerequisite: Joint-Locking Scripture, CL 10+
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose two until the start of your next turn:
cannot take Bonus Actions;
cannot take Reactions;
has Disadvantage on attack rolls;
has Disadvantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws;
cannot use ordinary movement modes requiring the limb or body part you are controlling;
cannot provide Somatic components with the controlled limb.
Successful Save: Choose one.
Meridian-Crushing Clinch does not permanently injure the target.

TAL_WRESTLING_SOUL_CLINCH_SEED:
#### Soul-Clinch Seed - Hold
Prerequisite: CL 7+
Your wrestling techniques begin to hold more than flesh.
When you attempt to Grapple one spirit, ghost, Incorporeal creature, or possessing entity that you can perceive:
your eligible grappling hand counts as magical;
you may establish a spiritual grapple even if ordinary physical contact would fail;
the target uses the normal Grapple saving throw;
the grapple ends if you can no longer perceive the target.
Soul-Clinch Seed does not automatically end possession or pull a possessing entity free.

TAL_WRESTLING_SOVEREIGN_GRAPPLING_INCARN:
#### Sovereign Grappling Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become an incarnation of perfect leverage.
For the duration:
count as two sizes larger when Grappling, Shoving, dragging, carrying, and using Wrestling talents;
gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage;
gain Advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws;
when a creature fails a saving throw against your Grapple option, apply one Slam talent without spending a Bonus Action once per turn;
dragging or carrying Grappled creatures costs no additional movement;
use Living Weapon with one creature up to one size larger than you after size increases are applied;
once per turn when one Grappled creature fails an escape check, regain Martial Focus.

TAL_WRESTLING_THE_HOLD_HEAVEN_COULD_NOT_:
#### The Hold Heaven Could Not Escape
“Heaven attempted to withdraw. The cultivator tightened one hand and informed Heaven that the discussion was not finished.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Court of the Closed Distance, World-Pinning Clinch, hidden restraint scripture
Action Type: Action
Range: Reach
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature within reach.
It makes a Strength or Dexterity saving throw, choosing which, against your Wrestling Save DC.
Failed Save: Until the end of your next turn:
the target becomes Grappled and Restrained;
ordinary size limits do not apply;
the target cannot teleport, travel between planes, or become Incorporeal;
the target cannot be moved away from you unless you permit it;
apply up to three different Slam talents you know immediately;
the target has Disadvantage on saving throws and checks made to escape this hold.
At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the saving throw, ending the effect on a success.
Successful Initial Save: The target cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.
The Hold Heaven Could Not Escape does not automatically overcome:
artifacts;
Formation cores;
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
Realm-defining transformations;
major narrative entities beyond the scope of ordinary combat.
Those may require a contested Cultivation Check or a specific narrative condition.

TAL_WRESTLING_TOMBSTONE_BURIAL:
#### Tombstone Burial - Throw, Capture
Prerequisite: Berserker sphere Shatter Earth, Living Weapon, Earth-Shattering Slam, CL 10+
When Earth-Shattering Slam Restrains one target in broken ground, choose to drive it underground.
Move the target downward through ordinary soil, stone, wood, or similar material:
| Cultivation Level | Maximum Depth |
| --- | --- |
| 10-16 | 10 feet |
| 17-20 | 20 feet |
If the path breaks through a floor, roof, or hollow structure, the creature falls normally after emerging.
While Restrained underground:
the target cannot breathe unless it has an appropriate feature;
it suffers the normal 2024 suffocation hazard when it runs out of breath or is choking;
escaping the Restrained condition does not automatically remove it from the hole.
After escaping, it must still climb, fly, burrow, teleport, or otherwise leave the burial space legally.
Tombstone Burial cannot pass through:
metal;
artifacts;
Formation cores;
sealed barriers;
Realm-defining structures.

TAL_WRESTLING_WORLD_PINNING_CLINCH:
#### World-Pinning Clinch - Hold, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Your grapples may affect creatures up to three sizes larger than you.
When you Grapple a creature larger than you:
count as attached to the creature rather than automatically moving it;
move with that creature when it moves unless an effect removes you;
the creature cannot move you through a space too small for you;
the creature has Disadvantage on attacks made against creatures other than you;
you may apply Slam talents normally.
If a feature increases your effective size, apply that increase before World-Pinning Clinch.

TAL_YANG_NO_SEAL_HOLDS_THE_SUN:
#### No Seal Holds the Sun
Action Type: Action
Range: 90 feet
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per Long Rest
Saving Throw: Wisdom
Choose one creature, object, Barrier, Formation Anchor, sealed door, spiritual lock, or ongoing suppressive effect within range that has one of your Rising Marks. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw if it is a creature or if its creator is present and able to contest the effect.
On a failed save, choose one appropriate effect:
one non-Secret effect reducing Speed ends;
one non-Secret effect preventing Reactions ends;
one non-Secret effect imposing Restrained, Paralyzed, Stunned, or Incapacitated ends;
one mundane or lower-Realm seal opens enough to allow passage for one creature before closing again;
one Barrier, ward, or Formation Anchor loses Hit Points equal to 5 x your CL;
one concealed object or hidden passage emits bright light until the end of your next turn.
On a successful save, the effect is not ended, but the target gains a Rising Mark that lasts for 1 minute.
This talent cannot automatically break Secret Inheritances, artifacts, divine seals, Realm-defining Domains, or higher-Realm suppressive effects.

TAL_YANG_THE_ACTION_BECOMES_MORE_REAL:
#### The Action Becomes More Real
Action Type: No Action
Trigger: You spend a Kindled Mark
Cost: 3 CP
Choose one of the following effects appropriate to the triggering response:
if you used Complete Force, the bonus damage is maximized instead of rolled;
if you used Complete Aim, the die is treated as its maximum result;
if you used Complete Step, the Speed increase lasts until the start of the marked creature’s next turn;
if you used Complete Breath, the marked creature also gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
if you used Complete Resolve, the marked creature gains Advantage on the next saving throw it makes before the start of your next turn.
You can use The Action Becomes More Real only once on each of your turns.

TAL_YANG_THE_ACTION_CANNOT_STAY_SMALL:
#### The Action Cannot Stay Small
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A marked creature within 90 feet completes an Action, Bonus Action, Reaction, spell, sphere talent, forged technique, monster action, or cultivation ability
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per Short Rest
Saving Throw: Constitution if the creature is unwilling
Spend the creature’s Rising Mark.
If the creature is willing, choose one complete result appropriate to the triggering action:
one damage roll from the action gains an additional 4d10 Fire, Radiant, or Force damage;
one healing or Temporary Hit Point effect from the action gains an additional 4d10 Hit Points or Temporary HP;
one movement effect from the action increases by 30 feet;
one condition the action would end cannot be reimposed by the same source until the start of the creature’s next turn;
one Barrier, construct, summoned creature, or created effect from the action appears with additional Hit Points equal to 5 x your CL.
If the creature is unwilling, it makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the action completes with dangerous surplus. Choose one overcomplete result:
the creature takes 6d10 Fire, Radiant, or Force damage after the action resolves;
the creature cannot benefit from being Hidden or Invisible until the end of your next turn;
the creature cannot take Reactions and cannot willingly repeat the same named action until the end of its next turn;
one created, summoned, or conjured effect from the action emits bright light in a 20-foot radius and has Vulnerability to the next damage roll that hits it before the start of your next turn.
On a successful save, the action functions normally, but the target gains a Rising Mark immediately after the action resolves.
Declare this talent immediately when the trigger occurs.

TAL_YIN_BLACK_MOON_READS_THE_FLAME:
#### Black Moon Reads the Flame
Action Type: No Action
Trigger: You apply a Waning Mark to a creature that dealt Fire, Radiant, Lightning, Thunder, or Yang-aspected damage during the current turn
Cost: None
You learn one of the following facts about the triggering effect, chosen by you:
whether it was a spell, sphere talent, forged technique, item, innate feature, or monster action;
whether the effect spent CP, a spell slot, item charges, or another limited resource;
whether the creature can use the same effect again before the end of its next turn;
whether the effect came from the creature’s body, soul, weapon, item, Formation, or external patron.
This feature does not identify every detail of the effect, but it tells you how the overextension entered the world.

TAL_YIN_THE_ACTION_ARRIVES_INCOMPLETE:
#### The Action Arrives Incomplete
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A marked creature within 90 feet completes an Action, Bonus Action, Reaction, spell, sphere talent, forged technique, monster action, or cultivation ability
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per Short Rest
Saving Throw: Wisdom
Spend the creature’s Waning Mark. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw.
On a failed save, choose one incomplete result appropriate to the triggering action:
one damage roll from the action is reduced by half;
one target of the action gains Advantage on its saving throw;
healing or Temporary HP granted by the action are reduced to 0 for one target;
teleportation or special movement granted by the action is reduced by half;
one condition the action would end continues until the start of the target’s next turn;
one Advantage granted by the action is canceled;
one summoned, created, or conjured effect from the action appears with half its normal Hit Points or duration.
On a successful save, the action functions normally, but the target gains a Waning Mark immediately after the action resolves.
This talent does not undo an action after the table has moved on. Declare it immediately when the trigger occurs.

TRAP_BASE_ACTIVATION_TRAP:
### Activation Trap — Snare Pattern
Rig one ordinary consumable item to activate when the trap is triggered.
Examples include:
Alchemist’s Fire;
Acid;
Ball Bearings;
Caltrops;
dyes;
perfumes;
smoke pellets;
noise-makers;
appropriate ordinary Alchemy or Tinker consumables.
When triggered, the item activates. If the item normally requires a target, target the triggering creature. If the item creates an area, its point of origin is one of the trap’s spaces, chosen when you set the trap.
You may load multiple copies of the same consumable. Each trigger activates only one loaded item. Activation Trap remains armed while at least one loaded item remains.
Unused recoverable items may be removed from a disarmed or expired trap.

WARLEADER_BASE_MOMENTUM_MARKS:
### Momentum Marks
A Momentum Mark represents the pressure gathered when allies follow your command.
You can hold a number of Momentum Marks equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
You gain 1 Momentum Mark the first time on each turn that one of the following happens:
a Commanded ally benefits from your active Standard;
a Commanded ally hits a creature you have verbally or visibly identified as the objective;
a Commanded ally uses the Help action to aid another Commanded ally;
a Commanded ally succeeds on a saving throw after gaining a bonus or reroll from one of your Warleader talents.
Momentum Marks last until combat ends, until you are Incapacitated, or until you complete a short or long rest.
You cannot gain more than one Momentum Mark from the same creature on the same turn.

WATER_BASE_RETURN_THE_FLOW:
##### Return the Flow
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 60 feet
Cost: 0 CP
Choose one Water effect you created within range. Move it up to 10 feet, end it early, or convert it into one of the following minor Return effects:
one creature in or adjacent to it becomes Soaked;
one ally in or adjacent to it moves 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
one ordinary flame in or adjacent to it is extinguished;
you regain awareness of the nearest obvious Water Source within 60 feet.
You cannot use Return the Flow to move a creature through a wall, closed door, Barrier, or sealed effect.

WRESTLING_BASE_GRAPPLING_REMINDER:
#### Grappling Reminder
When you use the Grapple option of an Unarmed Strike:
choose one creature within 5 feet;
the target must be no more than one size larger than you;
you must have one hand or another eligible grappling body part free;
the target makes a Strength or Dexterity saving throw, choosing which;
on a failed save, it gains the Grappled condition.
While Grappled:
the target’s Speed is 0 and cannot increase;
the target has Disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures other than the grappler;
when the grappler drags or carries the target, each foot of movement costs 1 additional foot unless the target is Tiny or at least two sizes smaller than the grappler.
A Grappled creature may use its Action to make a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against the grapple’s escape DC, ending the condition on a success.
A grapple also ends if:
the grappler becomes Incapacitated;
the target leaves the grapple’s range;
the grappler releases the target without spending an Action.

WRESTLING_BASE_ONE_GRAPPLE_PER_HAND_OR_B:
#### One Grapple per Hand or Body Part
One hand may maintain one grapple.
A feature may permit grappling through:
one hand;
two hands;
a weapon;
a tail;
a tentacle;
a maw;
another eligible body part.
Whatever part maintains the grapple cannot be used for another purpose unless a rule explicitly says otherwise.

WRESTLING_BASE_RESTRAINTS_AND_UTILIZE:
#### Restraints and Utilize
The 2024 equipment rules give Rope, Chains, and Manacles their own binding rules.
When a Wrestling talent allows you to secure a creature with Rope, Chains, Manacles, or a similar restraint:
take the Utilize action unless the talent says otherwise;
satisfy the item’s normal requirements;
use the item’s normal escape and break rules unless the talent explicitly replaces them.

insight.anchor-between-heaven-and-earth:
**Prerequisite:** Gravity sphere, CL 12+.

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Intelligence, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you would be moved against your will, knocked Prone, or dropped from flight, you may use your Reaction and spend 2 CP or Stamina to anchor yourself.

Until the start of your next turn:

your Speed becomes 0;

you cannot be moved against your will by effects of Core Formation or lower;

you do not fall unless the surface supporting you is destroyed;

attacks against you have Advantage until the start of your next turn.

insight.anchored-soul:
**Prerequisite:** Space sphere, CL 8+.

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Dexterity score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

You gain Advantage on saving throws against:

teleportation imposed against your will;

banishment;

forced entry into a pocket space;

possession through spatial displacement;

planar travel imposed against your will.

Once between Full Cultivation Sessions, when you are teleported unwillingly, you may return to your previous space immediately after the effect resolves if that space is unoccupied and within 60 feet.

insight.bell-and-formation-custodian:
**Prerequisite:** Music sphere, Formations sphere, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Dexterity score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When designing a Formation, ritual hall, bell tower, drum terrace, concert court, funeral rite, or morale project, use one Music principle you know as a seed concept.

Choose one principle from:

Measure;

Tone;

Chord;

Dissonance;

Echo Performer;

Battle Cadence;

Soul-Sound;

Silence-Breaking Note.

This does not create the project automatically.

The project still requires time, materials, site access, a power source whose Source CL is at least the project's Source CL, and maintenance.

insight.blackglass-executioner:
**Prerequisite:** Obsidian Glass Scripture or Cinderglass Shards, CL 10+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Strength, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Once per turn when a hostile creature takes Slashing damage from your Obsidian Terrain or Cinderglass Shards, choose one:

• reduce its Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn;

• prevent Reactions until the start of your next turn;

• mark it with black-glass residue, preventing ordinary Invisible from benefiting it until the start of your next turn;

• add your Proficiency Bonus to the damage.

insight.blood-furnace-heart:
**Prerequisite:** Blood Pump, CL16+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

**Source CL:** Body Refining Source CL unless a named Sphere or other Source Rule supplies the effect.

When Blood Pump successfully replaces a reduction to 0 Hit Points, choose one benefit after you are set to 1 Hit Point:

- move up to 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
- end one ordinary Frightened condition affecting you;
- end one ordinary Grappled or Restrained condition affecting you;
- regain Stamina equal to your Proficiency Bonus, not above your maximum; or
- gain Temporary Hit Points equal to `2 × your Proficiency Bonus`.

An equal- or higher-Source-CL effect that explicitly prevents the chosen removal is not ended. Movement requires a legal destination.

insight.bloodline-core-fusion:
**Prerequisite:** Bloodline Cultivator, Ancestral Bloodline Awakening, or another active bloodline engine; CL12+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Intelligence, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you activate a bloodline feature explicitly tagged **Surge**, **Transformation**, or **Release**, choose two different Fusion benefits:

- gain Temporary Hit Points equal to `2 × your Proficiency Bonus`;
- move 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
- regain 2 Qi;
- gain Advantage on your next saving throw before the end of your next turn;
- end ordinary Frightened or Charmed when its Source CL is lower than yours;
- move your Domain Armament 20 feet; or
- your next lineage-tagged attack or technique before the end of your next turn deals additional damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

One bloodline activation triggers Bloodline-Core Fusion once.

insight.chain-walking-immortal:
**Prerequisite:** Chains sphere, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Dexterity, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

You may move along your own chains as though they were stable ground.

You gain the following benefits:

climb at full Speed using chains;

swing across gaps without checks when a valid chain route exists;

use Chain Bridge once per scene without spending CP;

ignore ordinary falling damage if a valid anchor exists within 60 feet and you are not incapacitated.

insight.cleansing-adept:
**Prerequisite:** Water sphere, Cleansing Water, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Wisdom, Dexterity, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When a creature benefits from your Cleansing Basin, choose one additional benefit:

it may immediately repeat a saving throw against Poisoned or disease;

it gains Advantage on its next death saving throw before the start of your next turn;

it removes one mundane contamination, smoke effect, or environmental grime.

insight.clinch-gate-adept:
**Prerequisite:** Iron Fist sphere, Dragon-Step Clinch, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you maintain a body clinch:

the target no longer has Advantage on checks to escape solely because the clinch is maintained without a hand;

you may use Rising Knee once per turn without requiring the target to already be Grappled by hand;

when the target misses you with a melee attack, reduce its Speed by 5 feet until the start of its next turn.

insight.counter-chant-specialist:
**Prerequisite:** Counter-Chant, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you use Counter-Chant:

increase range by 30 feet;

if the opposed check succeeds, regain 1 CP;

if the target bears your Resonance, it has Disadvantage on its opposing check.

insight.dawn-ward-adept:
**Prerequisite:** Radiance, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you use Dawn Ward, choose one:

increase the damage reduction by 1d8;

the protected creature gains Advantage on its next saving throw against Charmed, Frightened, possession, or corruption before the end of your next turn;

if the damage is reduced to 0, the attacker becomes Dawnmarked until the start of your next turn.

insight.demon-emperor-s-price:
**Prerequisite:** Demon Emperor Incarnation, CL 15+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When Demon Emperor Incarnation ends, you may reduce Corruption gained by 1.

If you do, choose one price:

lose one Hit Die until your next Full Cultivation Session;

suffer Disadvantage on the next social check against an orthodox cultivator;

gain 1 Demonic Debt recorded against you;

one visible demonic sign remains until purified.

insight.dune-court-architect:
**Prerequisite:** Sand sphere, Court of Ten Thousand Dunes, CL 12+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Dexterity, Wisdom, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you design a Formation, battlefield, desert fortress, burial pit, glass garden, caravan route, training ground, or ambush site, you may use one Sand technique as the conceptual seed.

The project may include one Sand-themed benefit, such as:

warning tracks;

collapsing dunes;

sand-hidden vault doors;

glass alarm chimes;

concealed burial traps;

heat-mirage screens;

quicksand corridors;

sand-memory witness zones.

This Insight does not create the project automatically. It requires materials, time, anchors, labor, maintenance, and at least one vulnerability chosen from exposed Anchor, water saturation, high wind, excavation, disrupted maintenance, or a weakness printed by the project rules.

insight.embodied-domain:
**Prerequisite:** Internalized Sphere Insight, access to one Domain talent, CL12+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

**Source CL:** Body Refining Source CL unless a named Sphere or other Source Rule supplies the effect.

When you activate a Domain belonging to an internalized Sphere, choose one bodily manifestation for that activation. It lasts while the Domain remains active:

- +1 AC;
- Speed increases by 10 feet;
- Advantage on Strength saving throws;
- Advantage on Constitution saving throws;
- Resistance to one damage type the Domain itself can deal;
- ignore difficult terrain created by that Domain; or
- gain Temporary Hit Points equal to `2 × your Proficiency Bonus` when the Domain begins.

Only one manifestation from this Insight applies to a Domain activation. The Temporary Hit Points are gained once, not each round. Domain suppression also suppresses the manifestation.

insight.empty-hand-weapon-master:
**Prerequisite:** Iron Fist sphere, Open-Hand Disarm, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you successfully disarm a creature with Open-Hand Disarm, choose one:

catch the item if you have a free hand;

kick the item up to 15 feet into a legal space;

immediately use one Unarmed Strike against the disarmed creature;

if you possess Scoundrel, immediately plant a Tiny object on the target without spending an Action.

Use this Insight once per round.

insight.erased-name:
**Prerequisite:** Void Sphere or Void-Touched Cultivator, CL16+, and recorded Secret access

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Wisdom or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Choose one permanent cost when gaining this Insight:

- unfamiliar people struggle to remember your face;
- mundane records of you fade unless renewed during each Full Cultivation Session;
- your reflection is absent;
- resurrection requires a personal Anchor bearing your true identity;
- wards and ancestral sites treat you as an unknown presence; or
- one former title or identity permanently disappears from ordinary memory.

Gain Advantage on saving throws and opposed checks against Divination, tracking cultivation, dream intrusion, memory alteration, possession, name-based curses, and oath effects that do not possess your true-identity Anchor.

An effect whose Source CL is lower than yours cannot learn your exact location through remote divination unless it already possesses a personal Anchor tied to your true identity.

insight.ethical-exorcist:
**Prerequisite:** Spirit Companions sphere

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Wisdom, Charisma, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

You have Advantage on the Cultivation Check for **Break the Cruel Seal**, **Exorcist's Mercy**, or **True Name Mercy** when your declared purpose is one of the following:

- free a spirit from coercive control;
- calm a maddened, frightened, wounded, or contaminated spirit;
- separate a spirit and Host without destroying either;
- release a spirit to a legal vessel, manifestation, afterlife route, reincarnation route, shrine, or other state accepted by its Source Rule.

If another Source Rule expressly says it uses one of those Spirit Companions procedures, the Advantage applies to that use as well.

The benefit does not apply when your actual purpose is enslavement, extraction of involuntary service, destruction of a Complete Soul, theft of a spirit's vessel or Name, or conversion of an unwilling spirit into your companion.

insight.falling-star-footwork:
**Prerequisite:** Gravity sphere, CL 8+.

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Intelligence, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When using Reverse Gravity Step, Feather Body, or Body Lightening:

you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks from creatures whose reach you leave during the first 10 feet of movement;

you may move across liquid surfaces during your turn;

you may move across fragile surfaces without breaking them;

once per scene, you may use Reverse Gravity Step without spending CP or Stamina.

insight.feed-the-breakthrough-furnace:
**Prerequisite:** Profane Breakthrough Pressure, CL 10+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you use Profane Breakthrough Pressure and the check succeeds, choose one:

gain Temporary HP equal to your CL after the cultivation session;

regain all missing CP up to half your maximum CP;

reduce Corruption by 1 if the breakthrough involved defeating or purifying an inner demon;

gain Advantage on your next saving throw against tribulation backlash.

If the check fails, gain 2 Corruption instead of 1.

insight.foundation-array-custodian:
**Prerequisite:** Earth sphere, Formations sphere, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Strength, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When designing a Formation, road, gate, wall, tomb, courtyard, sect foundation, battlefield camp, or long-term terrain project, use one Earth Foundation, Burden, or Settlement principle as a seed concept.

This does not create the project automatically.

The project still requires:

terrain physically connected to the project footprint;

preparation time;

material costs;

labor or Formation anchors;

maintenance;

a clear vulnerability or counterplay condition.

insight.furnace-soul-awakening:
**Prerequisite:** Spirit Awakening, CL4+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Wisdom, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

You may learn Magma despite its ordinary Path restrictions. If this is a new Sphere for you, gain the normal free talent granted when learning a new Sphere.

When using Magma through Spirit Awakening:

- use Resonance for Magma talents;
- use Wisdom as your Magma key ability;
- your Magma talents may affect spirits, ghosts, Incorporeal creatures, possessing Intruders, soul-bound creatures, and spiritual parasites when those targets are otherwise legal;
- when a Magma talent deals Fire damage to one of those spiritual targets, you may change that Fire damage to Radiant or Psychic damage before resistances and immunities are applied; and
- once per round when a spirit, ghost, or possessing Intruder takes damage from your Magma talent, choose one result until the start of its next turn:
  - it cannot take Reactions;
  - it cannot willingly enter a creature's body;
  - it becomes visible as a heat shimmer and cannot benefit from ordinary Invisible; or
  - it suffers one Heat Pressure effect allowed by the Magma rules.

Furnace-Soul Magma is obvious to Spiritual Sense unless concealed by another Source Rule. Spirit courts, ghost sects, and karmic entities may recognize its pressure.

This Insight does not make ordinary lava spiritual, allow external projection that the Magma talent does not already permit, or authorize soul destruction.

insight.gravitic-soul:
**Prerequisite:** Spirit Awakening, CL4+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Intelligence, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

You may learn Gravity as a Spirit Awakening Sphere. If this is a new Sphere for you, gain the normal free talent granted when learning a new Sphere.

When using Gravity through Spirit Awakening:

- use Resonance for Gravity talents;
- use Wisdom as your Gravity key ability;
- use Wisdom instead of Strength when resisting forced movement, being knocked Prone, or resisting supernatural anchoring;
- your Gravity talents can express the weight of vows, souls, fear, obligation, judgment, and identity when the target and talent are otherwise legal; and
- when a creature fails a saving throw against **Weight of the Mountain**, **Black-Star Grip**, or **Heaven's Weight**, it has Disadvantage on Concentration saving throws until the start of its next turn.

This Insight changes access, key ability, resource, and expression. It does not let Gravity damage or rewrite a soul, vow, memory, or identity unless the specific Gravity talent or another Source Rule grants that authority.

insight.harmonic-analyst:
**Prerequisite:** Sound sphere, CL 4+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Gain Advantage on checks to identify:

brittle objects;

hollow walls;

hidden bells or alarms;

damaged barriers;

unstable bridges;

resonant Formation Anchors;

creatures using voice-based magic.

Once per scene, when you succeed on Read the Vibration, ask one additional question from its list.

insight.heartstring-physician:
**Prerequisite:** Music sphere, Healing Hymn, CL 10+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Dexterity score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When a creature receives healing from your Healing Hymn, choose one:

it ends one nonmagical Frightened effect;

it gains Advantage on the next death saving throw before the end of its next turn;

it reduces its Exhaustion penalty for one roll before the end of its next turn, but does not remove Exhaustion;

it gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

A creature can benefit from Heartstring Physician only once per scene.

insight.imperial-archivist:
**Prerequisite:** Qi Cultivation, CL8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Intelligence or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

At the end of a Full Cultivation Session, prepare one **Archive Question** concerning a named creature, place, item, technique, sect, historical event, law, lineage, Formation, or cultivation phenomenon.

Before your next Full Cultivation Session, when the question becomes relevant, choose one result category:

- direct clue;
- documented precedent;
- investigation avenue;
- known weakness category;
- historical relationship;
- legal or sectarian obligation; or
- scholarly inference.

Resolve the question from records that actually exist in the setting. The adjudicator provides one truthful result in the chosen category. If no relevant record exists, the result is: **No surviving record**, followed by the nearest documented lead that can be investigated. A scholarly inference must be labeled as inference.

This Insight cannot fabricate lost knowledge, reveal a Secret erased from every record, or provide information no archive, witness record, or documented precedent could contain.

insight.imperial-quartermaster-training:
**Prerequisite:** Qi Cultivation, CL8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Gain proficiency in one of the following: Animal Handling, Investigation, Persuasion, land vehicles, water vehicles, navigator's tools, cartographer's tools, or one merchant or appraisal tool printed by the equipment rules. If already proficient, gain a +2 bonus to checks with the chosen proficiency.

During expedition preparation, choose two Quartermaster benefits:

- reduce ordinary supply costs by 20 percent;
- acquire one Common consumable listed as normally sold, gathered, or produced in the current settlement or region without a separate search procedure;
- identify the most likely logistical failure from food, water, transport, shelter, storage, customs, route security, or medical supply;
- establish one concealed mundane cache holding up to `50 × your CL` pounds of ordinary supplies;
- gain Advantage on one bureaucracy, requisition, customs, or military-supply check during the expedition; or
- increase the carrying capacity of one vehicle or storage Formation by 25 percent through correct loading.

The chosen benefits last for that expedition or operation and do not create Rare, Restricted, or Secret goods.

insight.iron-shirt-adept:
**Prerequisite:** Iron Fist sphere, Body Conditioning or Iron Shirt Practice, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

While holding Martial Focus and wearing no Heavy armor:

reduce falling damage by 5 × your Proficiency Bonus;

gain Advantage on one Constitution saving throw against a physical shock, poison, or bodily disruption once per scene;

when a hostile creature damages you with an Unarmed Strike or natural weapon, it takes Bludgeoning damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

insight.item-spirit-midwife:
**Prerequisite:** Blacksmith sphere, Spirit-Listening Tap, CL 10+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Intelligence, Strength, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When working on an item with an item spirit seed, you may spend 1 hour coaxing it.

Choose one:

calm a hostile or fearful seed for one scene;

learn one material it desires;

learn one use it dislikes;

grant its bearer Advantage on one roll made with the item before the next Full Cultivation Session;

prevent one minor item-spirit complication from worsening until the next Full Cultivation Session.

This does not force obedience.

insight.lava-walking-immortal:
**Prerequisite:** Magma sphere, CL8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Strength, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Gain:

- Immunity to damage from your own Molten Terrain;
- Resistance to Fire damage;
- the ability to cross ordinary lava without sinking or taking ordinary lava damage for up to 1 minute at a time;
- Immunity to ordinary extreme heat; and
- the ability to leave temporary obsidian footholds behind you while crossing lava, each lasting until the start of your next turn.

A lava, magma, or fire effect bypasses these protections only if its Source CL is higher than yours or it is Artifact, Secret, divine, Immortal, or explicitly states that it bypasses Fire Immunity or environmental protection.

insight.legacy-broken-seal:
**Prerequisite:** Discover and release a sealed power within yourself

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Choose one ability score and increase it by 2, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm. If you gain Broken Seal through level selection, this +2 replaces rather than stacks with the normal +1 level-selection ability increase printed above.

Also choose one lasting consequence:

- a visible mutation that cannot be concealed without a feature;
- recurring dreams that reveal your presence to one named hostile or interested power when you complete a Full Cultivation Session;
- a spiritual mark detectable by ordinary spiritual examination;
- one named hostile entity can sense your approximate direction while on the same plane and within 10 miles;
- when a named trigger occurs, you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your own Cultivation Save DC or lose Reactions until the start of your next turn; or
- a recorded oath or obligation whose breach makes this Insight's cultivation benefit dormant until restitution is completed.

The chosen consequence is part of the character record and cannot be removed by ordinary retraining.

---

insight.merciful-reaper:
**Prerequisite:** Death, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Wisdom, Intelligence, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When a creature dies within 30 feet, you may use your Reaction to choose one:

prevent its corpse from being animated for 24 hours;

preserve its soul from ordinary destruction for 24 hours;

allow it to speak one final sentence;

end one ordinary possession affecting its corpse;

grant one ally who can hear the final breath Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

This Insight is favored by orthodox Death cultivators.

insight.name-the-distant-enemy:
**Prerequisite:** Stars, CL 12+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Wisdom, Intelligence, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you successfully apply Stable Stellar Mark to a creature, you may learn one of the following:

its current direction from you;

whether it is on the same plane;

whether it is under a teleportation, invisibility, or concealment effect;

whether it has damaged you or an ally during the current scene;

whether it is protected by a Star Anchor, Formation, or spatial ward.

You can use this Insight a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus between Full Cultivation Sessions.

insight.nine-finger-director:
**Prerequisite:** Puppetry sphere, Two-Body Control, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Intelligence, Dexterity, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you maintain more than one active puppet vessel, choose one vessel at the start of each turn as your leading hand.

The leading hand gains one of the following benefits until the start of your next turn:

+10 feet Speed;

+2 AC;

Advantage on the next Strength or Dexterity save it makes;

the next Puppet Strike made through it deals extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

insight.obsidian-sculptor:
**Prerequisite:** Magma, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Strength, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When one of your Magma talents ends, choose one affected 10-foot area.

Transform it into one:

• obsidian barrier;

• jagged difficult terrain;

• short staircase;

• defensive ridge;

• Half Cover position;

• simple obsidian platform;

• sealed volcanic cap over a pit, vent, or fissure.

The structure lasts 1 hour unless destroyed.

insight.one-breath-one-line:
**Prerequisite:** Perfect Shot, CL 10+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Dexterity, Wisdom, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you use Perfect Shot, you may also ignore Disadvantage from one of the following for that attack:

long range;

Prone attacker;

light obscurement;

a hostile creature within 5 feet of you;

firing through a narrow opening.

You must still have a legal target and route.

insight.perfect-pitch:
**Prerequisite:** Music sphere, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Dexterity score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Gain Advantage on checks made to:

identify a voice;

detect imitation;

recognize supernatural sound;

notice concealed listeners;

break silence effects;

analyze musical techniques;

recognize whether a Music effect is mortal, spiritual, Formation-supported, or artifact-supported.

insight.red-thread-sensitivity:
**Prerequisite:** Thread sphere and Spirit Awakening, Karma sphere, Heartbinder, Knot Weaver, or another printed Source Rule authorizing relationship perception

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Dexterity, Intelligence, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

**Action Type:** Action  
**Range:** 60 feet  
**Targets:** Two creatures you can see

Study the relationship threads between the targets. Learn whether at least one genuine, active relationship recorded through kinship, oath, debt, affection, command, mentorship, ownership, custody, hostility, worship, or a Spirit Bond from the following list connects them:

- affection or loyalty;
- debt or obligation;
- rivalry or hatred;
- fear or coercive dependence;
- oath, vow, contract, or formal duty;
- familial, ancestral, teacher-disciple, sect, office, or companion bond.

If more than one category applies, learn the category with the strongest current spiritual pressure; if tied, learn all tied categories.

You do not learn exact terms, memories, hidden names, who is morally correct, or whether either creature intends to honor the relationship.

If the relationship is concealed by a ward, Fate effect, false thread, Secret, Domain, or another cultivation source, make a Thread Cultivation Check against that source's Cultivation Save DC. On a success, read the relationship normally and learn that it was concealed. On a failure, learn only **Obscured Relationship**.

This Insight detects genuine relationships; it does not create consent or let you perceive a relationship that no longer exists merely because it existed in the past.

insight.resonance-breaker:
**Prerequisite:** Music sphere, Disruptive Harmony or Silence-Breaking Note, CL 10+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Dexterity score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

When you succeed on a Music Check to suppress, disrupt, or identify a Sound, Music, War, Formation, or Spirit effect, gain one benefit:

regain 1 CP;

regain Martial Focus;

grant one ally within 30 feet Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;

impose Disadvantage on the next Concentration saving throw made by the disrupted creature before the start of your next turn.

Use Resonance Breaker once per scene.

insight.samsara-memory:
**Prerequisite:** Samsara-Wheel Cultivator, reincarnation inheritance, or genuine former-life awakening; CL8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

At the end of a Full Cultivation Session, choose one Former-Life Memory:

- one skill proficiency;
- one tool proficiency;
- one language or script;
- one weapon-group proficiency;
- one narrow historical field; or
- one non-Secret Sphere talent from a Sphere you already know and for which you meet every prerequisite.

The Memory remains until you replace it during another Full Cultivation Session.

A talent selected this way uses your Qi and Qi Cultivation statistics when legal and cannot be inherited, permanent, identity-exclusive, or dependent on anatomy or an Asset you do not possess.

Once per scene, reroll one failed roll that directly uses the active Former-Life Memory. You must use the new result.

insight.siege-magma-adept:
**Prerequisite:** Magma, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Constitution, Strength, or Intelligence score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

Once per turn when damaging an object, structure, vehicle, Barrier, or Formation Anchor through a Magma talent, choose one:

• add your Proficiency Bonus to one damage roll;

• deal double damage to an unattended ordinary object or mundane structure;

• ignore ordinary hardness;

• reveal a visible crack, weak point, pressure seam, or load-bearing failure.

This does not automatically destroy artifacts, permanent Formations, Domains, or Realm-defining structures.

insight.soul-shackles:
**Prerequisite:** Spirit Awakening, Chains sphere, CL4+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Strength, Dexterity, or Wisdom score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

You may use Wisdom as your Chains key ability.

If you can perceive the target through Spiritual Sense, Soul Gaze, or another legal sense, your Chains talents can target and restrain:

- manifested or unbodied spirits;
- ghosts and Incorporeal creatures;
- astral bodies and projections;
- possessing Intruders and visible possession links;
- spiritual manifestations that are valid creatures or Assets.

This permission does not make an untargetable Complete Soul destructible and does not let a mundane chain cross planes or enter a sealed vessel unless the Chains talent or another Source Rule permits it.

When you apply **Chain-Script Seal** to a possessing Intruder or its possession link, the Host has Advantage on the next saving throw it makes against that possession before the end of its next turn.

insight.thousand-lamp-meditation:
**Prerequisite:** Radiance, CL 8+

**Ability Increase (Level Selection):** Increase your Charisma, Wisdom, or Constitution score by 1, to the maximum allowed by your current Realm.

During a Full Cultivation Session, you may maintain a circle of harmless dawn lamps.

Choose up to a number of willing creatures equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

Each chosen creature gains one of the following benefits until it completes a 10-minute recovery procedure:

Advantage on the first saving throw it makes against Frightened;

Advantage on the first saving throw it makes against Charmed;

Advantage on the first saving throw it makes against possession or spiritual contamination;

Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

A creature can benefit from only one Thousand-Lamp Meditation at a time.

printed_option:Dawn Wave:
##### Heavenly Radiance - The Undying Dawn

“The night did not end. It was simply made too honest to continue.”

Prerequisite: CL 15+, Solar Radiance Form

Action Type: Bonus Action

Duration: 1 minute Concentration: Not required

Cost: 15 CP

Use Limit: Once per long rest

Transform into an incarnation of sovereign dawn.

For the duration:

gain Fly Speed 60 feet and Hover;

gain Immunity to Radiant damage;

gain Resistance to Necrotic, Fire, and Psychic damage;

shed Bright Light in a 120-foot radius and Dim Light for another 120 feet;

suppress non-Legendary magical Darkness, ordinary illusion concealment, ordinary invisibility, and ordinary fear auras inside your Bright Light;

Radiance Strike deals 8d10 Radiant damage instead of its normal damage;

once per turn when Radiance Strike hits an Unclean target, suppress one visible corruption-derived temporary benefit until the start of your next turn.

###### Dawn Wave

While Heavenly Radiance is active, when you use Radiance Strike, you may instead release one of the following:

a single-target beam with a range of 120 feet;

a 60-foot line, 10 feet wide;

a 30-foot cone.

The line and cone require Dexterity saving throws for half damage instead of attack rolls. Creatures that fail are Dawnmarked until the end of your next turn.

When the transformation ends, gain 1 level of Exhaustion unless you ended the encounter with at least half your maximum CP remaining.

printed_option:Modulation Talents:
##### Technique Categories

Qiweaving talents use the following tags.

###### Modulation Talents

A Modulation talent alters one sphere technique you activate.

Unless a talent says otherwise:

apply only one Modulation talent to one technique;

choose the Modulation when you activate the technique;

pay any additional CP cost immediately;

the Modulation cannot make an illegal target legal;

the Modulation cannot remove an effect’s basic limitations unless it says so.

tianxia.path.spirit_awakening.feature.so:
# CL2 — Soul Gaze

**Action Type:** Action  
**Range:** 60 feet  
**Cost:** 1 Resonance

Choose one creature you can see. You may instead choose a creature Resonance Marked by you within range even if you cannot see it, provided it is not behind total spiritual concealment.

Learn:

- its current and maximum Hit Points;
- its broad creature nature and cultivation Path, if any;
- whether its effective CL or relevant Source CL is lower than, equal to, or higher than yours;
- its damage resistances, immunities, and vulnerabilities;
- its surface emotional state;
- whether it is affected by an ordinary curse, possession, coercive Hosting, Heart Demon, dream intrusion, memory interference, spiritual contamination, Spirit Scar, or obvious soul injury;
- the broad category of one Spirit Bond, possession link, or Spiritual Anchor currently sustaining an obvious effect upon it.

Soul Gaze does not automatically reveal:

- a protected Soul Anchor;
- a spirit’s complete Nature or Bond contract;
- Secret or divine identity;
- hidden phases or unrevealed transformations;
- exact unspent Cultivation Points;
- protected memories;
- the complete text of an unknown feature;
- a concealed effect whose Source Rule defeats ordinary spiritual diagnosis.

When protected information is contested, make a Cultivation Check against the protecting effect. On failure, identify which category of information was concealed, but not its contents. You cannot retry against the same concealment until it changes, you gain new evidence, or a new scene begins.

---

# CL1 — Soulward Response

**Action Type:** Reaction  
**Trigger:** You fail an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw.  
**Cost:** 1 Resonance  
**Limit:** Once per round

Add your Proficiency Bonus to the saving throw, potentially turning failure into success.

Soulward Response:

- is not saving throw proficiency;
- is used after you learn that the roll failed;
- cannot modify a death saving throw;
- cannot modify a breakthrough, training, forging, or ordinary ability check;
- cannot modify the same saving throw more than once;
- cannot stack with another feature that adds Proficiency Bonus to the same saving throw;
- does not automatically end an ongoing effect unless the successful-save result says it does.

At CL11, Soul Armor improves this response.

---

tianxia.path.spirit_awakening.feature.sp:
# CL1 — Spiritual Sense

Spiritual Sense is always active unless suppressed.

## Range

| CL | Range |
|---:|---:|
| 1–10 | 10 feet |
| 11–16 | 30 feet |
| 17–20 | 60 feet |

Within range, you perceive active souls, spirits, possessing entities, projected souls, spiritually animated corpses, and creatures with ordinary living consciousness even when normal sight cannot perceive them.

Against an ordinary living creature, Complete Soul, or spirit within range, Spiritual Sense functions as Blindsight. It does not automatically perceive:

- soulless traps or objects;
- mundane writing, color, or visual detail;
- a construct with no mind, spirit, or animating soul;
- a corpse with no active spirit or necromantic animation;
- a creature behind total cover;
- a successfully concealed soul, Secret concealment, divine veil, artifact-level masking, sealed spirit, or stronger spiritual absence.

Spiritual Sense also tells you whether a perceived entity is broadly:

- Embodied, Manifested, Hosted, possessing, projected, Unbodied, Anchored, or Contained;
- Resonance Marked by you;
- under an obvious ordinary possession, coercive Hosting, or spirit-manifestation effect.

It does not reveal exact statistics, thoughts, memories, Soul Anchor, Spirit Nature, Subpath, full Bond terms, or hidden Source Rules.

## Read the Spirit

**Action Type:** Action  
**Range:** Your Spiritual Sense range

Choose one soul, spirit, possession link, spiritual residue, Soul Fragment, or spiritual effect you perceive. Learn:

- its broad category;
- whether its Source CL is lower than, equal to, or higher than yours;
- whether it is stable, strained, damaged, concealed, Hosted, bound, possessing, Anchored, or suppressed;
- whether it is a Complete Soul, Soul Fragment, Spiritual Imprint, or uncertain mixture.

For a concealed or protected effect, make a Cultivation Check against its save DC. If it has no save DC, use `8 + source Proficiency Bonus + source key ability modifier`.

On failure, you know that spiritual concealment or interference is present, but not its exact nature. You cannot retry until the effect changes, you obtain a new Source Rule or evidence, or a new scene begins.

---

tianxia.talent.alchemy.formula_intensifi:
### Formula Intensification - Cauldron
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
When you use Field Formula, you may spend +2 CP to choose one additional effect:
increase the damage dice by one step, from d6 to d8 or d8 to d10;
increase the range by 30 feet;
increase an area by 5 feet;
move yourself 10 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks immediately after the technique resolves;
push one affected creature 10 feet on a failed save or hit.
You may choose only one additional effect per use.

tianxia.talent.alchemy.grand_pill_hall:
### Grand Pill Hall - Refinement
Prerequisite: CL 15+, Sect Pill Hall.
You may construct or supervise a Grand Pill Hall.
Cost: 50,000 gp.
Time: 1 year.
A Grand Pill Hall can support:
army supply;
city relief;
epidemic treatment;
sect cultivation;
bulk Common and Uncommon pill production;
modest Rare pill production;
ingredient preservation;
training of apprentice alchemists;
safe storage for one Heavenly Material.
This project requires logistics, guards, materials, labor, and political protection. It is a strategic asset, not a portable talent.

tianxia.talent.alchemy.living_pill_spiri:
### Living Pill Spirit - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+, Pill Spirit Creation.
When you awaken a Pill Spirit from a Very Rare or higher recipe, you may bind it as a Living Pill Spirit.
A Living Pill Spirit remains for up to 7 days or until consumed, sacrificed, or released.
While within 60 feet of you, it can:
take the Help action for Alchemy Checks;
warn you if a pill, poison, or ingredient within 30 feet is flawed or contaminated;
carry one Tiny pill or dose;
deliver one medicinal pill to a willing creature within 30 feet as an Action on your turn;
sacrifice itself to turn one failed Alchemy Check into a success, though not a success by 5 or more.
You may maintain only one Living Pill Spirit at a time.

tianxia.talent.alchemy.sect_pill_hall:
### Sect Pill Hall - Refinement
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You may construct or supervise a Sect Pill Hall.
Cost: 5,000 gp.
Time: 30 days.
A Sect Pill Hall requires space, ventilation, storage, assistants, fuel, records, tools, and at least one proper cauldron.
Benefits while using the Pill Hall:
Common and Uncommon refinement time is halved;
Batch Refinement maximum increases by your Proficiency Bonus;
ingredients stored there do not spoil under ordinary conditions;
the hall can produce bulk Common and Uncommon pills during downtime if supplied with ingredients and trained assistants;
the hall grants Advantage on checks to identify pills and alchemical contamination.
This does not grow ingredients.

tianxia.talent.ash.ash_form:
#### Ash Form - Unique Ash Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 4 CP
Become a drifting cinder-body.
Gain:
Fly Speed 30 feet and Hover;
Resistance to nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage;
Resistance to Fire and Necrotic damage;
ability to move through occupied spaces as difficult terrain;
ability to pass through openings as narrow as 1 inch;
Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks inside Ash Terrain, Smoke, or burned terrain.
Ash Form does not allow movement through solid barriers.

tianxia.talent.ash.ash_sovereign_incarna:
#### Ash-Sovereign Incarnation
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign cinder-body.
Gain:
Fly Speed 60 feet and Hover;
Resistance to all damage except Force and Radiant;
Immunity to Fire damage;
Immunity to Smothered;
ability to pass through openings as narrow as 1 inch;
Cinder Brand damage becomes 6d10;
Ashen Step range becomes 60 feet;
use Ashen Step once per turn without spending CP;
create one Remnant in an unoccupied space you pass through once per turn.

tianxia.talent.ash.ashen_step:
#### Ashen Step - Unique Ash Talent
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 20 feet
Cost: 1 CP
Dissolve into cinders and reform in one visible unoccupied space.
This movement:
does not provoke opportunity attacks;
ignores nonmagical difficult terrain;
may pass through occupied spaces;
cannot pass through sealed barriers;
may pass through openings as narrow as 1 inch.
If you begin or end inside Ash Terrain, Smoke, or near an ordinary fire, increase the range by 10 feet.

tianxia.talent.ash.ashes_of_the_fallen:
#### Ashes of the Fallen - Remnant Talent
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: A creature within 60 feet drops to 0 HP, or a temporary Construct is destroyed
Cost: 3 CP
Use Limit: Once per round
Create one Remnant in the triggering space.
Then choose one:
create a 10-foot-radius Ashfall area centered there until the start of your next turn;
gain Temporary HP equal to 2 x Proficiency Bonus;
move up to 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks;
reduce the CP cost of your next Ash talent before the end of your next turn by 2, minimum 1;
apply Ashen Brand to one creature within 30 feet.

tianxia.talent.ash.burial_ground:
#### Burial Ground - Remnant Talent
Prerequisite: CL 7+
Cost: +2 CP
When you create Ashfall, consume any number of your Remnants inside or adjacent to its area.
For each consumed Remnant, choose one benefit:
increase Ashfall radius by 5 feet;
increase its duration by 1 minute, maximum 10 minutes;
one hostile creature of your choice inside has Disadvantage on its first saving throw against that Ashfall;
create one new Remnant in an unoccupied space inside when Ashfall ends.
No single Ashfall may consume more Remnants than your Proficiency Bonus.

tianxia.talent.ash.court_of_the_last_emb:
#### Court of the Last Ember - Ash Domain
“The battle had ended. The ash disagreed.”
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 7 CP
The area becomes Ash Terrain.
##### You and Allies
ignore your Ash Terrain;
gain Resistance to Fire and Necrotic damage;
gain Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks inside Ash Terrain or Smoke;
may move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks after an enemy misses them.
##### Enemies
cannot gain Temporary HP;
have Disadvantage on Concentration saving throws while Smothered;
cannot benefit from the Invisible condition gained from the Hide action while coated in visible ash.
When an enemy starts its turn inside, it makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
take 2d8 Fire, Necrotic, or Psychic damage;
become Smothered until the start of its next turn;
cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
halve healing received until the start of its next turn;
reduce Speed by 10 feet until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Healing received is reduced by your Proficiency Bonus until the start of its next turn.

tianxia.talent.ash.read_the_ruins:
#### Read the Ruins - Unique Ash Talent
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 10 minutes
Range: Touch
Cost: 1 CP
Study ash, soot, cinders, cremation residue, or burned remains.
Learn broad information:
whether the source was ordinary, magical, alchemical, or spiritual;
approximate age of the residue;
whether a creature died nearby;
whether Fire, Magma, Lightning, Sun, or another major heat effect contributed;
whether spiritual residue remains;
whether destruction was sudden or gradual.
Read the Ruins provides evidence, not perfect historical reconstruction.

tianxia.talent.barrage.ten_angle_shot:
#### Ten-Angle Shot - Blitz
Prerequisite: Ricochet Scripture, CL 12+
When using Redirection:
ignore Three-Quarters Cover;
bend the projectile up to three times;
treat one visible reflective, hard, or angled surface as a legal redirection point;
attack a target you cannot see directly if you can see a valid projectile path to it. Total Cover still blocks the attack unless the path genuinely reaches the target.

tianxia.talent.beastmastery.permanent_co:
#### Permanent Control - Forbidden Tamer Talent
Prerequisite: Beast Tamer, Enduring Control, CL 10+
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 8 hours
Target: One creature currently affected by Beast Tamer
Attempt to turn temporary dominance into permanent control.
The target makes a Charisma saving throw with Advantage.
Failed Save: It remains under your control until the bond is broken.
Successful Save: It becomes immune to your Permanent Control.
Permanent Control:
does not create trust;
does not create a Bonded Companion;
does not grant Companion Archetypes;
does not grant Beast Nature;
does not grant Realm Evolutions;
may be recognized as coercive spiritual injury;
is forbidden or heavily restricted in most orthodox sects. A sapient creature may receive additional protections at the GM’s discretion.

tianxia.talent.beastmastery.the_first_pa:
#### The First Pact Beneath Heaven
“Before saddle, collar, whistle, or scripture, two creatures stood beneath the same storm and chose not to abandon one another.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Spirit-Beast Covenant or One Rider, One Beast, hidden primordial pact scripture
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You, one Beast Ally, or one Bonded Companion within 120 feet would drop to 0 HP, fail a saving throw against control, or be separated by forced movement
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one:
the protected creature drops to 1 HP instead of 0 HP;
the protected creature succeeds on the triggering saving throw;
negate the forced movement;
call one willing Beast Ally on the same plane into an adjacent unoccupied space;
end one ordinary hostile control effect affecting one Beast Ally. Until the end of your next turn:
Beast Allies within 60 feet cannot be Charmed or Frightened;
Beast Allies within 60 feet gain Resistance to all damage;
you and one Beast Ally may move up to half Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks;
your commands cannot force suicidal behavior. The First Pact does not create ownership.
It reveals the relationship that existed strongly enough to answer.

tianxia.talent.beauty.mirror_of_the_hear:
### Mirror of the Heart
When a creature bearing your Beauty Mark speaks with you for at least 1 minute, you may spend 1 CP and make a Wisdom (Insight) check contested by the target's Charisma (Deception).
On a success, you learn one of the following:
- what the target wants from you right now;
- what the target fears losing face over;
- whether the target is pretending not to care;
- what emotion your presence most strongly stirs in the target.
This does not reveal deep secrets or hidden memories unless the GM decides the scene supports it.

tianxia.talent.beauty.red_lip_command:
### Red Lip Command
Action Type: Action
Range: 30 feet
Target: One creature Charmed by you or bearing your Beauty Mark
Duration: Until the end of the target's next turn
Cost: 1 CP
Save: Wisdom
You issue a short, graceful command.
The command must be simple and non-suicidal, such as:
- stop;
- listen;
- kneel;
- wait;
- look at me;
- step aside;
- put that down;
- answer politely;
- leave them alone.
The target makes a Wisdom saving throw.
On a failed save, it follows the command until the end of its next turn, provided the command does not directly harm it, force it to betray a core vow, violate an obvious survival instinct, or force romance, intimacy, or sexual conduct.
A command to kneel, bow, or step aside does not automatically knock the creature Prone unless the GM rules that the creature chooses such a posture.
On a successful save, the target ignores the command, and its Beauty Mark ends.

tianxia.talent.beauty.thousand_faces_of_:
### Thousand Faces of the Heart
When you use Adorn the Moment, you may choose one emotional face:
- compassion;
- authority;
- innocence;
- grief;
- joy;
- terror;
- longing;
- serenity;
- judgment;
- wonder.
Until the effect ends, your Beauty talents may express through that emotional face.
Once before the effect ends, when a creature fails a saving throw against one of your Beauty talents, you may learn whether that emotional face was effective, resisted, painful, offensive, or strangely familiar to the target.

tianxia.talent.berserker.the_blow_heaven:
#### The Blow Heaven Refused to Receive
“The cultivator did not strike harder than Heaven. The cultivator struck after Heaven understood that it could not step aside.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Heaven-Crushing Exertion, hidden war-god scripture
Action Type: Action
Range: Reach or thrown-weapon range
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per week
Make one Batter attack.
Before rolling:
gain Advantage;
ignore Disadvantage;
choose up to four Exertion talents you know;
treat the target as already Battered;
ignore Resistance to the attack’s damage;
ignore ordinary object Damage Thresholds.
Hit: Add:
12d10 Force damage
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: It is Stunned until the end of your next turn and pushed up to 30 feet.
Successful Save: It cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.
If the attack strikes an object, structure, or temporary Barrier, deal double total damage.
The Blow Heaven Refused to Receive does not automatically destroy:
artifacts;
Formation cores;
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
Realm-defining structures.
Those may still be meaningfully damaged or contested according to the GM.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.anvil_remember:
### Anvil Remembers the Disciple - Project
Prerequisite: Apprentice’s Anvil, CL 10+
Your Apprentice’s Anvil becomes a spiritual workshop seed.
Choose one creature who trains with you for at least 1 hour during downtime.
Until the next long rest, when that creature uses an item you repaired, fitted, tempered, or prepared, it gains one of the following benefits once:
add your Proficiency Bonus to one attack roll;
add your Proficiency Bonus to one ability check;
reduce one damage instance to the item by 2 x Proficiency Bonus;
gain Temporary HP equal to your Intelligence modifier + Proficiency Bonus when the item fulfills its named purpose.
You can maintain this benefit for a number of creatures equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.apprentice_s_a:
### Apprentice’s Anvil - Project
During a long rest or downtime scene, designate one portable anvil, stone block, heavy stump, furnace plate, bell, or tool chest as your Apprentice’s Anvil.
While you have access to it:
reduce the time required for mundane repairs by half;
gain Advantage on Smith’s Tools checks made to teach another creature basic repair work;
once per day, prepare one additional item with Portable Forge Kit;
use the anvil as a focus for Blacksmith project work.
If lost or destroyed, create a new Apprentice’s Anvil with 8 hours of work and suitable materials.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.armor_knows_it:
### Armor Knows Its Owner - Temper
When you Fit Armor for a willing creature wearing armor or carrying a shield, the target may immediately adjust straps, stance, grip, or breathing.
Choose one:
the target stands from Prone without spending movement;
the target ends one nonmagical Grappled state caused by equipment, terrain, or a mundane restraint;
the target gains Advantage on the next Strength or Dexterity saving throw made before the start of your next turn.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.birth_of_the_i:
### Birth of the Item Spirit - Spirit, Project
Prerequisite: Spirit-Listening Tap, Tempering Sequence, CL 15+
You can begin the true awakening of an item spirit.
Choose one masterwork, magical, ancestral, named, sect-significant, or personally forged item that has received at least three successful Blacksmith projects from you.
Perform a project requiring:
rare materials;
a suitable forge or equivalent spiritual site;
at least 7 days of work;
GM-approved story cost;
one final Smith’s Tools check.
On a success, the item gains a stable item spirit seed.
A stable item spirit seed may grant one of the following, chosen with the GM:
the item remembers its rightful bearer;
the item grants Advantage once per long rest when used for its named purpose;
the item warns its bearer of one kind of flaw or danger;
the item resists being used against its purpose;
the item becomes eligible for future spirit-awakening projects.
This talent does not create a fully independent companion or artifact by itself.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.break_the_bad_:
### Break the Bad Nail - Flaw
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you use Expose the Flaw on a nonmagical object, lock, trap mechanism, restraint, hinge, wheel, chain, weapon, shield, or armor, you may spend 1 CP.
On a failed save or successful check, choose one:
the object is damaged;
the object becomes stuck or loose, your choice;
one function of the object fails until repaired;
one creature relying on the object has Disadvantage on the next attack roll or ability check involving it before the start of your next turn.
Magic items and artifacts resist this talent unless the GM allows it.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.forge_fitted_a:
### Forge-Fitted Armor - Temper
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you use Fit Armor, you may spend 1 CP to extend the Temporary Temper to 1 minute.
While the temper lasts, choose one:
+1 AC;
reduce Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage from nonmagical attacks by your Proficiency Bonus once per round;
ignore the first 5 feet of forced movement each round;
Advantage on saving throws against being knocked Prone.
A suit of armor or shield can benefit from only one Forge-Fitted Armor temper at a time.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.forge_fitted_w:
### Forge-Fitted Weapon - Temper
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you use Set Edge, you may spend 1 CP to extend the Temporary Temper to 1 minute.
While the temper lasts, the weapon gains one of the following benefits:
+1 to attack rolls;
+1 to damage rolls;
the weapon counts as magical for overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks;
once during the duration, the wielder may reroll one damage die and use the new roll.
A weapon can benefit from only one Forge-Fitted Weapon temper at a time.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.incarnation_of:
### Incarnation of the Living Forge
“He no longer stood beside the furnace. The furnace breathed from behind his ribs, and every hammer in the hall struck when his heart struck.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 6 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a living forge.
For the duration:
your hands, breath, and tools count as a complete forge for Blacksmith talents;
you can maintain up to five current workpieces;
your Forge Mark limit on each current workpiece increases by 2;
once per turn, place 1 Forge Mark on a current workpiece without using an action;
when you spend a Forge Mark, gain Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
your Blacksmith Temporary Tempers may last for 10 minutes instead of 1 minute;
you have Resistance to Fire and Lightning damage;
you have Advantage on saving throws against Exhaustion caused by heat, labor, smoke, or forced work.
While this Incarnation lasts, a creature that uses one of your current workpieces for its named purpose can add your Intelligence modifier to one roll.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.quench_against:
### Quench Against the Grain - Quench
Prerequisite: CL 7+
When a creature uses a weapon, armor, shield, tool, or object bearing one of your Forge Marks, use your Reaction to spend that mark and interrupt the material’s bad habit.
Choose one:
turn one missed attack with the weapon into a hit if the attack missed by 2 or less;
turn one hit against the armor or shield wearer into a miss if the attack hit by 2 or less;
add your Proficiency Bonus to one ability check using the tool;
reduce damage dealt to the object by 2d6 + Intelligence modifier.
Use Quench Against the Grain once per round.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.ring_test_the_:
### Ring-Test the Artifact - Flaw, Spirit
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When you use Read the Flaw on a magic item, artifact fragment, spirit weapon, ancient tool, formation component, sect token, or cursed object, you may spend 2 CP to perform a ring-test.
On a successful check, learn three of the following:
the item’s strongest function category;
one condition that would anger or resist the item;
one condition that would please or awaken the item;
whether the item is cursed, hungry, sleeping, damaged, incomplete, or bound;
whether the item has an item spirit seed;
whether the item was forged, grown, carved, scripted, stolen, sacrificed into, or born naturally;
what general kind of material or story is needed to improve or repair it.
On a failed check, you learn one true but incomplete impression and the item resists further ring-tests from you until your next long rest.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.the_first_hamm:
### The First Hammer That Named Iron
“Before swords had edges and before bells had voices, the first hammer struck the first stubborn thing and asked: What are you willing to become?”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Incarnation of the Living Forge, Ring-Test the Artifact, hidden forge scripture, and a named workpiece worthy of inheritance
Action Type: Multi-Mode
Timing Detail: 1 hour, or Action during a climactic forging scene with GM approval
Split Review Decision: gm_gated_combat_action_plus_procedure_variant
Recommended Factory Realization: procedures=ONE_HOUR_TRUE_NAMING_FORGE, CLIMACTIC_ACTION_EXCEPTION
Target: One legal workpiece
Cost: 10 CP and a permanent narrative cost approved by the GM
Use Limit: Once per month, or once per major story arc for permanent results
Name the workpiece’s true purpose and strike it with the First Hammer method.
The workpiece must be one of the following:
a personally forged item;
an ancestral or sect-significant item;
a broken item being restored;
a masterwork item ready to awaken;
a magical item being reforged;
a Formation core or artifact fragment approved by the GM;
a body-vessel, spirit-vessel, or oath-vessel approved by the GM.
Choose one inheritance result.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.unmake_by_know:
### Unmake by Knowing - Flaw
Prerequisite: CL 10+
When you have successfully used Read the Flaw on an object, barrier, construct, weapon, armor, shield, trap, vehicle part, or similar crafted thing, you may spend 2 CP and 1 Forge Mark to attempt to unmake one function.
Make a Smith’s Tools check against the target’s relevant DC.
Successful Check: One non-artifact function of the object is suppressed until repaired or until the end of the scene, whichever is shorter.Failed Check: The object resists your work and cannot be targeted by your Unmake by Knowing again until your next short rest.
Examples include:
a lock no longer locks;
a hinge jams;
a shield strap snaps;
a bow loses tension;
a trap trigger sticks;
a barrier section weakens;
a construct limb stutters.
Unmake by Knowing does not delete magic, but it may expose where another sphere can suppress it.

tianxia.talent.blacksmith.weapon_birth_p:
### Weapon-Birth Preparation - Project
Prerequisite: CL 5+
You can prepare a mundane weapon, tool, armor piece, shield, or object to receive a future forged technique, talisman script, formation mark, sect seal, or spiritual upgrade.
The preparation requires:
1 hour of work;
appropriate tools;
materials worth an amount set by the GM;
a successful Smith’s Tools check against a DC set by the item’s quality.
On a success, the item becomes prepared for one future project.
The next project using that item gains one of the following benefits:
reduce required time by one step;
reduce one material requirement by a modest amount;
gain Advantage on the first crafting check;
reduce the chance of a flaw or complication.
An item can hold one preparation from you at a time.

tianxia.talent.blood.blood_armament:
#### Blood Armament - Unique Blood Talent
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: Self
Duration: 1 hour
Cost: 1 CP and 1 HP
Shape hardened blood into one simple or martial melee weapon with which you are proficient.
The weapon:
counts as magical for overcoming ordinary Resistance;
may deal its normal damage type or Piercing damage;
dissolves if it leaves your possession for more than 1 minute;
may be dismissed without spending an Action. When you create the weapon, choose one cosmetic form such as:
spear;
saber;
knife;
bow-limb blade;
claw;
chain;
ritual needle. Blood Armament does not grant weapon proficiency.

tianxia.talent.blood.blood_armor:
#### Blood Armor - Unique Blood Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 3 CP and 5 HP
Form hardened blood around your body.
Gain:
+2 AC;
Resistance to Slashing damage;
Advantage on saving throws against bleeding effects;
Advantage on saving throws against forced movement caused by physical impacts.
The HP cost:
cannot be reduced;
cannot be transferred;
cannot be paid with Temporary HP.

tianxia.talent.blood.blood_emperor_incar:
#### Blood Emperor Incarnation
“My blood is not inside my body. My blood is the battlefield.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Become a sovereign blood-body.
Gain:
Fly Speed 40 feet and Hover;
Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, and Necrotic damage;
Immunity to ordinary bleeding effects;
Blood Thread damage becomes 6d10 Necrotic or Piercing damage;
Bloodsense range becomes 1 mile;
Crimson Sacrifice costs 4 HP per replaced CP instead of 5 HP;
apply Blood Thread automatically to one Bloodied enemy that starts its turn within 20 feet.
##### Crimson Aura When a Bloodied enemy starts its turn within 20 feet, it makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Take 4d8 Necrotic damage and you regain HP equal to half the damage dealt.
Successful Save: Take half damage. You regain no HP.
A creature takes this damage only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.blood.blood_puppet:
#### Blood Puppet - Forbidden Thread Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
Choose one Bloodied living creature bearing your Blood Thread.
The target makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: At the start of each of its turns, choose one:
move it up to half its Speed;
force it to drop one held object;
prevent it from taking Reactions;
force it to fall Prone;
reduce its Speed to 0 until the end of the turn. At the end of each of its turns, it repeats the saving throw, ending the effect on a success.
Successful Save: The target cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.
Blood Puppet cannot force:
self-harm;
attacks;
spellcasting;
cultivation techniques;
movement into obviously lethal hazards.

tianxia.talent.blood.blood_river_passage:
#### Blood River Passage - Unique Blood Talent
Prerequisite: CL 12+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 60 feet
Cost: 4 CP
Move through a line of blood, blood mist, spilled vital fluid, or one of your Blood Threads.
Teleport into one visible unoccupied space within range adjacent to:
a creature bearing your Blood Thread;
a Blood Sample you can see;
a visible pool of spilled blood;
your own Blood Armament;
one allied creature bound through Shared Veins. Blood River Passage cannot cross a Dimensional Lock, sealed barrier, or planar boundary.

tianxia.talent.blood.bloodline_ascension:
#### Bloodline Ascension - Bloodline Rite
Prerequisite: Bloodline Awakening, CL 15+
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 8 hours
Range: Touch
Target: One willing creature
Cost: 12 CP
Use Limit: Once per Realm per creature
Permanently awaken one latent bloodline feature.
Choose one approved benefit:
Darkvision 120 feet;
Climb Speed;
Swim Speed;
Fly Speed 30 feet;
Resistance to one appropriate damage type;
natural weapon dealing 1d10;
Speed +10 feet;
+1 to one ability score within the Realm maximum;
Advantage against one narrow condition or hazard;
one equivalent bodily feature. A creature may receive only one permanent Bloodline Ascension benefit per Realm.
The benefit must fit its ancestry, mutation, lineage, or established bodily theme.

tianxia.talent.blood.bloodline_awakening:
#### Bloodline Awakening - Bloodline Rite
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 1 hour
Range: Touch
Target: One willing creature
Duration: 24 hours
Cost: 5 CP
Awaken one existing inherited or bodily theme.
Examples include:
beast ancestry;
dragon blood;
spirit ancestry;
celestial heritage;
demonic lineage;
amphibious adaptation;
unusual senses;
hardened skin;
powerful musculature. Choose one approved benefit:
Darkvision 60 feet;
Climb Speed equal to Speed;
Swim Speed equal to Speed;
Resistance to one appropriate damage type;
natural weapon dealing 1d8;
Advantage on one narrow category of checks;
Speed +10 feet;
hold breath for 1 hour. Bloodline Awakening cannot invent an unrelated ancestry.
A creature gains only one Bloodline Awakening benefit at a time.

tianxia.talent.blood.bloodline_usurpatio:
