Prerequisite: CL 17+, Bloodline Ascension, forbidden blood scripture
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 8 hours
Range: Touch
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per Realm
Extract one bloodline trait from a defeated creature.
Requirements:
the creature died within the last hour;
the body or a major Blood Sample remains available;
the creature possessed a meaningful innate trait;
the creature had a CL or CR at least half your CL. Choose one narrow innate trait approved by the GM.
Examples:
Resistance to Fire;
amphibious breathing;
Darkvision;
Climb Speed;
natural armor;
one natural weapon;
one sense;
one movement mode;
one narrow bodily adaptation. You gain the trait permanently.
You may maintain a number of usurped traits equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
When gaining another beyond this limit, replace one.
Bloodline Usurpation cannot steal:
entire monster stat blocks;
Legendary actions;
lair actions;
spellcasting;
cultivation talents;
whole Paths;
Secret Inheritances;
unique narrative authority. Using Bloodline Usurpation is a serious forbidden practice in most orthodox sects.

tianxia.talent.blood.heartblood_rebirth:
#### Heartblood Rebirth
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You would die
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Transform into a blood cocoon.
Until the start of your next turn:
you are Incapacitated;
AC becomes 15;
gain Resistance to all damage except Radiant and Psychic;
cannot move voluntarily. At the start of your next turn:
return with 1 HP;
regain CP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
gain 2d10 Temporary HP. Heartblood Rebirth fails if:
your soul is destroyed;
the cocoon is destroyed;
a Secret effect prevents revival.

tianxia.talent.blood.physician_s_pulse:
