Tags: Anchor, Project
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Duration: 1 hour
Cost: 1 CP
You create a stable chain structure.
Examples include:
rope bridge;
ladder;
handhold line;
hanging platform;
climbing route;
rescue tether;
suspended walkway;
cargo sling;
temporary restraint for a door or gate.
The structure can be up to 60 feet long and supports 100 pounds x your CL.
The structure is a Chain Object. If destroyed, it collapses or vanishes safely if possible. The GM determines whether falling creatures may attempt checks or saves to catch themselves.

tianxia.talent.chains.chain_sovereign_in:
### Chain-Sovereign Incarnation
Tags: Domain, Lash, Anchor
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minuteConcentration: Not required
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You transform into a perfected chain incarnation.
For the duration, you gain:
Fly Speed 40 feet and Hover through suspended chains;
+3 AC;
Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, Slashing, and Force damage;
immunity to Prone;
reduce forced movement affecting you by 20 feet;
Chain Lash range becomes 60 feet;
Chain Lash damage becomes 6d10 Bludgeoning or Slashing damage.
#### Sovereign Binding
Once per turn when Chain Lash hits, the target makes a Strength saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
pull the target 20 feet;
knock the target Prone;
the target becomes Bound until the start of its next turn;
the target’s Speed becomes 0 until the start of its next turn;
the target cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Pull the target 5 feet.
#### Imprisoning Presence
When an enemy starts its turn within 20 feet of you, it makes a Strength saving throw.
Failed Save: It becomes Bound until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Its Speed is reduced by 5 feet until the start of its next turn.

tianxia.talent.chains.chains_domain_cour:
### Chains Domain: Court of the Ten Thousand Links
Tags: Domain, Tether, Anchor
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 7 CP
Every path remains open. Each simply ends in a chain.
For the duration, chains spread across the battlefield.
#### You and Allies
You and willing allies in the aura gain the following benefits:
Advantage on saving throws against forced movement and Prone;
reduce forced movement affecting you by 10 feet;
may use chains as ladders, handholds, or stable footing;
may move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks after resisting forced movement.
#### Enemies
Enemies in the aura suffer the following effects:
the area is difficult terrain for them;
they cannot Dash unless they succeed on a Strength saving throw at the start of their turn;
they have Disadvantage on checks made to escape Grappled, Restrained, or Bound states caused by your Chains talents.
When an enemy starts its turn inside the aura, it makes a Strength saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
it becomes Bound until the start of its next turn;
pull it 10 feet toward a point you choose;
knock it Prone;
it cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
its Speed becomes 0 until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Its Speed is reduced by 5 feet until the start of its next turn.
A creature is affected by this start-of-turn effect only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.chains.heaven_dragging_ch:
### Heaven-Dragging Chain
Tags: Lash, Anchor
Action Type: Action
Range: 180 feet
Cost: 12 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You cast a chain large enough to drag a gate, dragon, airship, mountain statue, or fleeing immortal back into consequence.
Choose one creature or object.
If the target is a creature, it makes a Strength saving throw.
Failed Save: The target takes 10d10 Bludgeoning or Slashing damage, is moved up to 60 feet toward a point you choose, and falls Prone.
Successful Save: The target takes half damage and is moved 15 feet.
Heaven-Dragging Chain may affect:
Huge creatures;
vehicles;
gates;
siege engines;
large objects;
flying creatures;
massive chains or anchors;
battlefield structures.
Against a structure or unattended object, deal double damage and move it if physically plausible.

tianxia.talent.chains.prison_of_nine_gat:
