A Prison of Nine Gates is a major sect asset. It should attract attention, prisoners, politics, revenge attempts, escape plots, and maintenance obligations.

tianxia.talent.chains.twin_tether:
### Twin Tether
Tags: Tether
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 4 CP
You link two creatures, objects, anchors, or surfaces with a chain.
Choose two targets within range. Each unwilling creature makes a Strength saving throw.
Failed Save: That target is tethered.
Successful Save: That target is not tethered.
If at least two targets are tethered, they are connected by a Tether with a maximum length of 30 feet.
While tethered:
a tethered creature becomes Bound;
the targets cannot willingly move farther apart than the Tether permits;
if one tethered creature moves, the other may be pulled if it fails a Strength saving throw;
a tethered creature may use its Action to make a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your Cultivation Save DC, ending the Tether on itself on a success.
The Tether is a Chain Object.
Twin Tether may link:
two enemies;
one enemy and one willing ally;
one enemy and one anchored object;
two objects;
one ally and one stable surface;
a flying creature and the ground.

tianxia.talent.daemonic_cultivation.devo:
#### Devour the Scripture Fragment - Parasite
Prerequisite: Demonic Technique Theft, CL 10+
When you succeed with Demonic Technique Theft, you may spend 3 additional Devoured Essence and gain 1 Corruption.
Choose one visible non-Secret, non-Domain, non-Inheritance talent effect used by the triggering creature.
Until the end of your next turn, you may reproduce a corrupted echo of that effect once, using your Daemonic key ability and Daemonic Save DC.
The echo must obey these limits:
it cannot last longer than 1 round unless the GM approves;
it cannot restore more HP than 2 x your CL;
it cannot create permanent objects;
it cannot summon permanent companions;
it cannot copy Secret Inheritances, Domains, Realm transformations, or artifacts;
if the effect would normally require a sphere-specific object, symbol, weapon, or medium, your daemonic aura provides a crude substitute.
After using the echo, make a Wisdom saving throw against your Daemonic Save DC.
Failed Save: Gain 1 Corruption.

tianxia.talent.daemonic_cultivation.ten_:
#### Ten-Thousand Demon Sutra
Prerequisite: CL 15+
During a Long Rest or full cultivation session, you may study, bind, devour, or bargain with a captured technique fragment, monster core, spirit remnant, bloodline echo, or demon scripture.
Choose one non-Secret talent from a sphere you have seen used or studied for at least one scene.
Until your next Long Rest, you may use a corrupted imitation of that talent once.
Limits:
the talent cannot be a Secret Inheritance;
it cannot create permanent infrastructure;
it cannot create a full companion;
it cannot be a Domain unless the GM explicitly permits;
it uses your Daemonic key ability and Save DC;
using it costs its normal cost + 2 CP or +2 Devoured Essence;
after using it, gain 1 Corruption.
If you learn the same talent through its proper sphere later, this imitation ends.

tianxia.talent.daemonic_cultivation.the_:
#### The Demon That Ate Its Own Name
“The first demon was chained by name. The last demon escaped by devouring the word that could command it.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Demon Emperor Incarnation, Ten-Thousand Demon Sutra, a hidden nameless demon scripture, and a personal catastrophe caused by hunger
Action Type: Special Trigger
Timing Detail: No Action when you would die, be sealed, have your soul destroyed, lose your cultivation base, or fail a decisive saving throw
Cost: All remaining CP, all Devoured Essence, and 3 Corruption
Use Limit: Once per campaign arc, or once ever unless the GM permits the demon’s return
Erase one immediate defeat by feeding it to the nameless demon.
Choose one:
instead of dying, remain at 1 HP and immediately activate Demon Emperor Incarnation;
instead of being sealed, break one ordinary seal and teleport to a visible space within 120 feet;
instead of losing your cultivation base, suppress the base-scattering effect until the end of the scene;
instead of failing a decisive saving throw, succeed and unleash World-Devouring Maw centered on yourself without harming chosen allies;
instead of having your soul destroyed, split off a daemonic remnant that can be recovered through a future quest.
Afterward:
Corruption becomes 10;
gain 3 Demonic Debt;
every trained Fate, Spirit, Protection, Heavenly Punishment, or Daemonic cultivator of equal or higher Realm within a vast narrative distance may sense that something forbidden survived;
the GM creates a permanent consequence tied to your name, shadow, reflection, or future tribulation.
This inheritance should save a character in a legendary moment, not become a weekly panic button.

tianxia.talent.destruction.heaven_cracki:
