tianxia.talent.force.pressure_sense:
### Pressure Sense - Anchor Talent
You know when one of your Pressure Anchors:
is struck;
is moved;
is destroyed;
is crossed by a creature of Small size or larger;
becomes separated from you by a planar boundary.
Pressure Sense does not reveal an exact square, a creature’s identity, or hidden information beyond the event that disturbed the anchor.

tianxia.talent.formations.formation_comp:
#### FORMATION COMPASS - BREAKING
You gain Advantage on checks made to identify a formation, locate its Array Eye, locate its Nodes, or understand its trigger.
As an Action, you may study one Formation Array within 60 feet. Make a Formation Check against the creator’s Formation Save DC.
Success: Learn one of the following:
the location of its Array Eye;
the location of one Node;
one Pattern Layer it contains;
whether it requires Concentration;
one condition that would collapse it.

tianxia.talent.formations.formation_spir:
#### FORMATION SPIRIT - PREPARED
Prerequisite: Self-Sustaining Circuit, CL 15+
You may awaken a minor spirit inside one Prepared Array or project you control.
The Formation Spirit is not a full companion. It is a semi-aware steward of the array.
It may:
Pulse one Pattern Layer according to instructions you set;
alert you within 10 miles when the array is attacked or triggered;
attempt one Formation Check per round to resist disruption;
speak in simple impressions to keyed creatures inside;
maintain a list of keyed creatures;
recognize obvious damage to Nodes, Anchors, or the Eye.
If the array collapses, the Formation Spirit becomes dormant until the array is repaired or rebuilt.

tianxia.talent.formations.heavenly_grand:
#### HEAVENLY GRAND FORMATION - PROJECT
Prerequisite: Sect Formation Design, CL 15+
You may design and construct Grand Formations.
A Grand Formation may defend a city district, mountain gate, battlefield, lake, canyon, fortress, valley, or sect territory.
A typical Grand Formation requires:
1 year of work;
at least 50,000 gp of materials;
one major Formation Core;
at least nine Anchors;
one spiritual vein, sacred site, furnace, ancestral tomb, celestial timing, or equivalent power source;
trained assistants or an organization capable of maintaining it;
a visible or discoverable vulnerability;
GM approval for its laws and limits.
Grand Formations are campaign-scale structures. They should matter politically, militarily, economically, and spiritually.

tianxia.talent.formations.sect_formation:
#### SECT FORMATION DESIGN - PROJECT
Prerequisite: CL 10+
You may design and construct sect-scale formations as downtime or campaign projects.
A Sect Formation may protect a compound, mine, shrine, gate, training yard, medicinal garden, vault, prison, ancestral hall, or similar location.
A typical Sect Formation requires:
30 days of work;
at least 5,000 gp of materials;
one Formation Core;
at least five Anchors;
a defined power source;
a maintenance procedure;
at least one defined vulnerability;
GM approval for its exact effects.
A Sect Formation is not a normal combat talent. It is strategic infrastructure and should create story hooks, defense plans, infiltration targets, and resource pressure.

tianxia.talent.formations.sovereign_of_t:
#### SOVEREIGN OF THE WORLD-DIAGRAM - DOMAIN
Prerequisite: Court of the Ninefold Array, CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: Self
Area: 60-foot-radius Emanation
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You become the moving Eye of a sovereign formation. Spiritual diagrams unfold under your feet, behind your eyes, and in the air around you.
For the duration:
the area is your Sovereign Array;
choose three Pattern Layers you know; the array gains all three;
once during each of your turns, you may Pulse one Pattern Layer without using an action;
you may spend 2 CP to Pulse a second Pattern Layer during the same turn;
keyed allies inside may use Formation Step as a Bonus Action;
hostile creatures inside cannot benefit from teleportation unless they first succeed on a Charisma saving throw;
Nodes created by this feature cannot be permanently destroyed, but each destroyed Node prevents one Pulse before reforming at the end of your next turn.
You are the Array Eye. If you become Incapacitated, the Sovereign Array collapses.

tianxia.talent.formations.star_vein_astr:
#### STAR-VEIN ASTROLABE - PREPARED
Prerequisite: Heavenly Grand Formation, CL 15+
When you build a Prepared, Sect, or Grand Formation under an auspicious timing, celestial event, spiritual tide, geomantic alignment, or matching terrain, choose one Astrolabe benefit:
increase duration by one category, such as 8 hours to 24 hours or 24 hours to 7 days;
reduce material cost by 25 percent;
conceal the Eye and Anchors from ordinary sight;
increase the Formation Save DC by 1;
allow the formation to store a number of CP equal to your Proficiency Bonus for its own automatic Pulses.
The GM determines what timing or alignment is sufficient. For important formations, finding or creating the right timing may be a story objective.

tianxia.talent.formations.triggered_arra:
#### TRIGGERED ARRAY - PREPARED
When you complete a Prepared Array, you may leave it dormant for up to 24 hours.
Choose a visible or spiritually defined trigger, such as:
a creature entering the site;
a door opening;
a spoken phrase;
a talisman breaking;
a hostile creature crossing the boundary;
a creature of a chosen type entering;
you using a Reaction while within 1 mile.
When triggered, the array activates and begins its normal duration. If it requires a choice when activated, you must make that choice when preparing the trigger unless the trigger is your own Reaction.

tianxia.talent.formations.vein_tapping_a:
#### VEIN-TAPPING ANCHORS - PREPARED
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When setting a Prepared Array on a site with a natural or artificial spiritual power source, you may bind one Node to that source.
Choose one benefit:
reduce the array’s CP cost by 1, minimum 1;
increase duration to 24 hours;
increase radius by 10 feet;
give the Eye Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage from nonmagical attacks;
allow the array to remain active for 1 round after its Eye would be destroyed, giving you a chance to repair or stabilize it.
The power source becomes a visible vulnerability. A creature that identifies the tapped source gains Advantage on Formation Checks made to disrupt the array.

tianxia.talent.gravity.gravity_sense:
#### Gravity Sense
Tag: Field Art.
You sense major gravitational distortions within 120 feet.
You know when a creature or object within that range:
changes weight supernaturally;
falls through supernatural force;
enters a Gravity Domain;
uses levitation or flight;
becomes anchored by supernatural weight;
creates a gravity well, local down, orbit, or pressure field.
You also gain a +2 bonus to Cultivation Checks made to identify or resist Gravity effects.

tianxia.talent.gravity.reverse_gravity_s:
#### Reverse Gravity Step
Tag: Weight Art, Fall Art.
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Until the end of your turn.
Cost: 2 CP or Stamina.
Choose one direction. Until the end of your turn, gravity treats that direction as down for you only.
You may:
run along walls;
run across ceilings;
leap upward as though falling sideways;
move across gaps;
drop sideways;
avoid ordinary falling damage during this movement.
At the end of the turn, normal gravity returns. If you are not standing on a surface or supported by another effect, you fall normally.

tianxia.talent.guardian.one_body:
## SECRET INHERITANCE — ONE BODY BEFORE HEAVEN
“A thousand arrows descended. None reached the people behind him.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Adamant Guardian Incarnation, hidden defensive scripture
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: One creature, area effect, Domain, or environmental calamity would damage one or more allies within 60 feet
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose any number of allies within 60 feet.
Redirect all damage those allies would take from the triggering effect to yourself.
The redirected damage:
retains its original damage types until your Resistance is applied;
is combined into one damage instance;
cannot be redirected again;
cannot be prevented through Immunity;
may be reduced by Resistance;
may be redirected into Held Harm if capacity remains;
cannot reduce you below 1 HP.
After resolving the redirected damage:
gain one level of Exhaustion;
end every Stance and Domain you are maintaining;
you cannot use One Body Before Heaven again until the limit resets.
One Body Before Heaven does not negate non-damaging consequences unless the GM determines that redirecting the damage naturally carries those consequences with it.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.esse:
### Essence-Thread Packing - Seal
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
When you Seal the Essence of a Lot, you may bind related Lots into a single recipe-ready packet.
If all Lots in the packet are used in the same Alchemy recipe, the alchemist gains one of the following benefits:
reduce the recipe’s ingredient-preparation time by half;
gain +1 to the Alchemy Check;
reduce the chance of incompatible ingredients causing a Broken product;
count the packet as organized proof of ingredient origin for sect inspection.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.ingr:
### Ingredient Compatibility - Sign
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
When you identify a Harvest Lot, you may determine one compatible use category:
Alchemy;
medicine;
poison;
beast feed;
talisman ink;
formation fuel;
crafting material;
cultivation aid;
trade luxury;
sect tribute.
If the Lot is later used in that category, the first check to use it gains +1 if the GM agrees your classification was relevant.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.medi:
### Medicine Mountain Claim - Route, Steward
Prerequisite: CL 10+, Medicine Mountain Map.
You can establish a formal claim, patrol route, seasonal schedule, or sect harvesting zone over a Resource Site or region.
During downtime, the claim provides:
better records of what the site can produce;
reduced accidental overharvesting;
clearer rights and responsibilities;
warning when outsiders harvest illegally;
improved ability to send gatherers to the correct place at the correct time.
A claim is social and logistical. It can be challenged by rival sects, clans, monsters, corrupt officials, disasters, or superior force.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.one_:
### One Leaf, One World Harvest Scripture
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Heavenly Material Recognition, Sovereign Clean Cut, GM approval, and a lost gatherer scripture or world-root pact
“Do not take the garden. Take the moment in which the garden offers one leaf.”
You may attempt to harvest a Secret material without destroying the source, even when ordinary doctrine says the source must be uprooted, slain, mined out, or consumed entirely.
This requires a major scene, not a routine check.
Declare one intended Secret harvest:
one petal from a world lotus;
one drop of dragon vein marrow;
one fruit from a tree that blooms once per age;
one thread from a heavenly silkworm cocoon;
one scale from a sleeping sovereign beast;
one ember from a tribulation-struck root;
one tear from an ancient spring;
one bone shaving from a willing saintly remnant.
Make a Gathering Check against a DC set by the GM, usually 30 or higher.
On success, gain the Secret material and preserve the source.
On success by 5 or more, the Secret material is Perfect.
On failure, choose one:
gain nothing and preserve the source;
gain the material in Bruised form but trigger a major consequence;
abandon the attempt and owe the source, guardian, sect, or Heaven a debt.
On Natural 1, the source rejects the harvest. Resolve a story consequence such as a guardian awakening, secret-realm collapse, curse mark, oath debt, sect alarm, beast pursuit, or heavenly omen.
This inheritance should be rare. It changes how sects think about priceless materials.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.secr:
### Secret-Realm Gatherer - Approach, Route
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
You are trained for timed secret realms, collapsing pocket worlds, ancient gardens, forbidden valleys, and trial grounds where every plant is contested.
When entering a bounded expedition site, choose one expedition goal:
return with the rarest material possible;
preserve the site for future entry;
avoid guardian attention;
map exits and hazards;
recover a specific quest ingredient.
For the duration of the expedition, once per Short Rest when you make a Gathering Check directly related to that goal, add a d8 to the roll after seeing the d20 but before knowing the outcome.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.sect:
### Sect Medicine-Field Steward - Steward, Route
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
You can supervise a small medicine field, herb garden, mushroom cave, spirit orchard, bee yard, silkworm room, or mineral-soak bed.
This talent does not make plants grow faster. Instead, while you supervise a site during downtime, choose one benefit:
reduce spoilage and theft;
identify one problem before it becomes a crisis;
improve the chance that ordinary workers harvest without ruining the material;
keep Common spiritual materials stable until a sect alchemist collects them;
train assistants in safe handling.
A field still requires appropriate soil, qi, water, labor, climate, guards, seeds, and time.

tianxia.talent.harvesting_gathering.spir:
### Spirit-Herb Appraisal - Sign, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
You can identify qi-infused herbs, spirit grass, medicinal fungi, old ginseng, lingzhi, dew-bearing flowers, mineral-fed roots, and similar low-grade spiritual materials.
When you Read the Sign for Common or Uncommon spiritual plant materials, learn all of the following on a success:
general element or spiritual tendency;
approximate age or maturity;
whether the material is safe to touch;
whether it is better for pills, medicine, talismans, beast feed, cultivation, or trade;
whether harvesting it will kill the source.

### Spirit-Sealing Wax - Seal
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
You create wax, thread, talisman labels, gourd plugs, spirit-paper wraps, jade slips, small jars, or comparable seals suitable for Common and Uncommon spiritual materials.
When you Seal the Essence of a Common or Uncommon Lot, choose one:
double its stable storage duration;
remove the Bruised quality if the GM agrees the damage was minor;
prevent its scent, aura, or spiritual pressure from being detected by ordinary senses;
mark the Lot so an alchemist gains Advantage on the first Pill Appraisal or ingredient-identification check made with it.

tianxia.talent.hunger.all_under_heaven_b:
### All-Under-Heaven Banquet - Banquet, Meal
Prerequisite: Nascent Soul Realm
When you use Imperial Banquet Furnace, you may include one symbolic ingredient tied to the location, such as river fish from a sacred bend, grain from famine land, beast meat from a border hunt, fruit from a sect garden, or tea from an ancestral mountain.
If the GM agrees the ingredient is meaningful to the current story, each participant may also gain one of the following until its next long rest:
- Advantage on the first Charisma check made in that region;
- Advantage on the first Wisdom (Survival) or Intelligence (History) check made to understand the region;
- the ability to ignore one ordinary meal requirement during travel;
- a symbolic omen about local hunger, scarcity, greed, or need.
This is a narrative and exploration talent. It does not reveal secrets automatically.

tianxia.talent.hunger.demon_king_roast_m:
### Demon-King Roast Method - Demon-Course, Meal, Mantle
Prerequisite: Nascent Soul Realm, Demon-Beast Digestion
When you successfully Refine the Meal using a Mighty Corrupted Portion from a demon beast, you may create Demon-King Satiety.
When you activate Digestive Mantle using Demon-King Satiety, choose two basic Mantle benefits and one of the following:
- gain Resistance to one damage type the demon beast strongly expressed until the start of your next turn;
- add 2d8 damage of an appropriate type to one successful attack before the Mantle ends;
- gain Advantage on saving throws against Frightened for the Mantle duration;
- gain a 30-foot aura of predatory pressure until the end of your next turn. Hostile creatures of lower Realm that start their turn in the aura must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have Disadvantage on the next attack roll they make before the start of their next turn.
When the Mantle ends, gain 1 Impurity. If you already have Impurity equal to or greater than your Proficiency Bonus, also make the unstable Mantle saving throw immediately.

tianxia.talent.hunger.feast_after_the_hu:
### Feast After the Hunt - Meal, Beast-Course
Prerequisite: Core Formation Realm
When a meaningful spirit beast, demon beast, monstrosity, dragon, giant beast, or comparable creature is reduced to 0 HP within 60 feet of you, you may mark it as rightful prey.
If you help prepare or consume that creature within 1 hour, your first successful Refine the Meal check using its Essence Portion gains one of the following benefits:
- reduce the CP cost by 1;
- gain Advantage on the Hunger Check;
- create 2 Satiety instead of 1;
- reduce Impurity by 1 after the meal.
You can use Feast After the Hunt once per short rest.

tianxia.talent.hunger.imperial_banquet_f:
### Imperial Banquet Furnace - Banquet, Meal
Prerequisite: Nascent Soul Realm
As a 1-hour ritual, spend 8 CP and at least one Mighty Portion to prepare a spiritual banquet for up to twelve willing creatures.
Each participant chooses one benefit lasting 8 hours:
- increase maximum HP by your Proficiency Bonus;
- gain Advantage on Constitution saving throws;
- gain Resistance to Poison damage;
- ignore nonmagical difficult terrain caused by hunger, mud, snow, exhaustion, or ordinary travel hardship;
- gain Temporary HP equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus at the start of the next combat.
A creature can benefit from only one Imperial Banquet Furnace per long rest.
If the meal used demon-beast ingredients, each participant may accept 1 Impurity to choose two benefits instead of one.

tianxia.talent.hunger.shared_bowl_method:
### Shared Bowl Method - Banquet, Meal
Prerequisite: Foundation Realm
When you successfully use Refine the Meal during a short rest, choose up to your Proficiency Bonus willing creatures who share the meal.
Each chosen creature gains one of the following benefits until its next long rest:
- Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
- Advantage on its next Constitution saving throw;
- +5 feet Speed for 1 hour;
- Advantage on its next ability check to resist hunger, thirst, spoiled food, or forced march.
A creature can benefit from only one Shared Bowl Method per long rest.

tianxia.talent.ice.nascent_soul_glacier_:
#### Nascent Soul: Glacier Soul Takes Shape
Prerequisite: Nascent Soul Realm
Action Type: Passive
Your soul has learned to hold a crystalline outline even when the body is pressured. You gain the following benefits:
your Lattice Limit increases by your Proficiency Bonus;
you may maintain one additional Fracture Mark beyond your normal limit;
you can perceive vibrations through your Frost Lattice within 120 feet, allowing you to know the location of creatures touching it unless they are protected by a higher-Realm concealment, Void effect, or similar countermeasure;
your Ice effects can exist in extreme heat for at least 1 round before environmental heat can weaken or destroy them, unless the heat comes from a higher-Realm supernatural source.

tianxia.talent.imbuement.false_vigor:
#### False Vigor - Mandate
You command a body to ignore a failing state for a time.
Imbue. Place Mandate can target one willing creature. Choose one:
the target treats its Exhaustion level as lower by an amount equal to half your Proficiency Bonus, rounded up;
the target ignores one reduction to an ability score up to twice your Proficiency Bonus;
the target immediately wakes if sleeping normally;
the target adds your Cultivation Level to the number of minutes it can hold its breath.
False Vigor does not remove Exhaustion, cure ability reduction, heal damage, or prevent the target from dying if its actual Exhaustion or damage would kill it when the Mandate ends.

tianxia.talent.imbuement.mandate_without:
#### Mandate Without Vessel - Domain
Prerequisite: Sovereign of the True Name of Things, CL 15+
Once per long rest, when you create your Court of Ten Thousand Mandates, choose one property law rather than a target family:
all unsecured metal is heavy;
all blades are dull;
all footfalls are silent;
all speech resounds;
all armor is brittle;
all arrows seek;
all doors resist opening;
all tools remember precision;
all fire-bearing weapons dim;
all exhausted bodies ignore one level of fatigue.
The law applies only inside the Court, only to valid Vessels, and only while the Court lasts. Creatures and attended items save normally if hostile.

tianxia.talent.imbuement.qi_written_mand:
#### Qi-Written Mandate - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Your commands are no longer only surface alterations. You can write them into the target’s circulating Qi or item spirit.
Gain the following benefits:
your Mandate Load increases by 1;
when you set a Mandate by spending 2 CP, it lasts 1 minute without Concentration and does not end if the target briefly leaves range;
you may target magical weapons, armor, shields, tools, talismans, and minor spirit objects with Imbuement without automatically failing, though unwilling or protected vessels still resist;
when you use Read the Vessel, you also learn whether a Vessel is safe, unstable, hungry, cursed, awakened, or resisting.

tianxia.talent.imbuement.sovereign_of_th:
#### Sovereign of the True Name of Things - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Court of Ten Thousand Mandates, CL 15+
Your Mandates can briefly touch the true name of a vessel rather than only its surface property.
Gain the following benefits:
your Mandate Load increases by your Proficiency Bonus;
your range for Place Mandate, Fray Mandate, and Counter-Mandate becomes 120 feet;
you can target incorporeal objects, spiritual equipment, visible soul-weapons, projected armor, or spiritual vessels when the GM agrees there is a perceivable Vessel;
once per round when you succeed on an Imbuement Check, regain 1 CP;
your set Mandates can last 10 minutes without Concentration by spending 3 CP instead of 2 CP.

tianxia.talent.imbuement.suppress_item_s:
#### Suppress Item Spirit - Counter
Prerequisite: CL 12+
When you use Counter-Mandate against a magic item, awakened vessel, construct, animated object, talisman, or equipment-bearing technique, you may spend 1 additional CP.
On a success, choose one:
suppress one active item property until the end of your next turn;
prevent an animated object from taking Actions until the end of your next turn;
end one temporary item-spirit awakening;
suppress an equipment bonus or item activation for 1 minute.
Artifacts and inheritance items may require an opposed Cultivation Check or may be immune unless the story permits a contest.

tianxia.talent.imbuement.true_tempering_:
#### True Tempering Command - Mandate
Prerequisite: Tempered Equipment, CL 12+
When you Imbue a weapon, armor, shield, or tool with Tempered Equipment, choose one extra property:
Hungry Edge: once per turn, extra damage equal to your key ability modifier;
Guardian Shell: the bearer reduces incoming damage by your Proficiency Bonus once per round;
Steady Tool: the bearer may treat one d20 roll lower than 10 as a 10 for a check using that tool;
Hidden Quality: the Mandate is not obvious without magical inspection;
Sect Mark: the Vessel visibly bears your sect, clan, personal, or scripture mark and has Advantage on checks to be recognized as legitimate by allies who know the mark.
A Vessel can hold only one True Tempering property at a time.

tianxia.talent.jester.absurd_agreement:
### Absurd Agreement - Punchline, Mock-Praise
Prerequisite: CL 5+Compatible Proposition: Show Your Hand
After the triggering technique resolves, the Foil makes a Wisdom saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
reduce its Speed by 10 feet until the start of its next turn;
it cannot take Bonus Actions until the start of its next turn;
it becomes Flustered;
one ally who saw the technique gains Advantage on its next attack roll against the Foil before the start of your next turn.
Successful Save: It cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.

tianxia.talent.jester.borrowed_action_ho:
### Borrowed Action, Honest Consequence - Punchline, Borrowed-Role
Prerequisite: CL 12+Compatible Proposition: Ignore the Fool or Show Your Hand
After the triggering Action resolves, choose one ordinary Action:
Dash;
Disengage;
Dodge;
Help;
Hide, if you meet its normal requirements;
Search;
Study;
Utilize with one object already in hand or within reach.
Take that Action as part of this Reaction.
Borrowed Action, Honest Consequence does not copy Magic actions, sphere talents, spells, or class features.

tianxia.talent.jester.borrowed_expressio:
### Borrowed Expression - Borrowed-Role
After observing one creature for at least 1 minute, gain Advantage on Charisma (Deception) or Charisma (Performance) checks made to imitate its:
posture;
mannerisms;
speech rhythm;
public habits;
obvious emotional presentation.
Borrowed Expression does not change your appearance or voice automatically.

tianxia.talent.jester.borrowed_gesture:
### Borrowed Gesture - Punchline, Borrowed-Role
Prerequisite: CL 5+Compatible Proposition: Show Your Hand or Ignore the Fool
After the triggering Action resolves, choose one:
take the Dodge action as part of this Reaction;
take the Disengage action as part of this Reaction and move up to 10 feet;
take the Help action as part of this Reaction to assist one ally within 30 feet that can see or hear you;
if the Foil moved willingly before triggering this Punchline, move up to half that distance without provoking opportunity attacks from the Foil.
Borrowed Gesture does not copy spells, sphere talents, or class features.

tianxia.talent.jester.fool_s_diplomacy:
### Fool’s Diplomacy
Prerequisite: Words Without Offense, CL 5+
When taking the Influence action outside combat, use Charisma (Performance) in place of Deception, Intimidation, or Persuasion when delivering the request through:
humor;
satire;
allegory;
mock praise;
self-deprecation;
a short performance.
The normal Influence rules still determine whether the request is willing, hesitant, or repugnant.

tianxia.talent.jester.painted_exit:
### Painted Exit - Pratfall
Prerequisite: CL 7+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Move up to half your Speed.
During this movement:
do not provoke opportunity attacks;
pass through hostile spaces as difficult terrain if the creature is no more than one size larger than you;
do not end movement in an occupied space;
fall Prone at the end of the movement unless you choose to remain standing.

tianxia.talent.jester.recluse_at_court_i:
### Recluse-at-Court Incarnation
“The fool remained in the center of the court and somehow stood outside every rule that expected dignity.”
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
For the duration:
use Set the Scene at the start of each of your turns without spending a Bonus Action;
maintain up to three Foils at once, choosing one Proposition for each;
deliver one Punchline per round without spending your Reaction;
move 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks after delivering a Punchline;
gain Resistance to Psychic damage;
gain Immunity to Charmed and Frightened;
when a Foil becomes Flustered, regain Martial Focus if absent.

tianxia.talent.jester.thousand_faces_one:
### Thousand Faces, One Mistake - Setup, Borrowed-Role
Prerequisite: You Meng’s Borrowed Robes, CL 10+
When you use Set the Scene, create one visible role:
cringing coward;
arrogant noble;
loyal servant;
wounded traveler;
drunken performer;
officious inspector;
familiar rival;
another role approved by the GM.
Until Set the Scene ends:
gain Advantage on one Charisma (Deception) or Charisma (Performance) check consistent with the role;
if the Foil fulfills your Proposition, choose to become Invisible to the Foil until the end of the current turn after your Punchline resolves.
Invisible from this talent ends early if you make an attack roll or deal damage.
The role does not automatically deceive creatures that cannot perceive the performance.

tianxia.talent.karma.borrowed_tomorrow:
#### Borrowed Tomorrow
Tags: Mercy, Grace, Thread
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You or an ally within 60 feet fails a saving throw or would drop to 0 Hit Points
Cost: 8 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Choose one:
turn the failed saving throw into a success;
cause the target to drop to 1 Hit Point instead of 0 Hit Points.
The protected creature gains one Karmic Burden owed to Heaven. Before its next long rest, it must choose one consequence:
lose all remaining CP;
gain one level of Exhaustion;
take 6d10 Psychic damage;
accept a meaningful narrative obligation approved by the GM;
immediately create a Grace Cause of comparable significance.
Borrowed Tomorrow postpones consequence. It does not erase it.

tianxia.talent.karma.court_of_cause_and_:
#### Court of Cause and Effect
Tags: Domain, Ledger, Debt, GraceRealm: Core Formation
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 7 CP
You establish a karmic court where every deed becomes easier to record.
Inside the Court:
your Record the Deed range increases to 120 feet;
you may use Record the Deed twice per round instead of once;
Imprints created inside the Court do not fade when the Court ends and last until your next long rest;
when a creature with one of your Debt Imprints damages another creature, it takes Psychic damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
when a creature with one of your Grace Imprints restores HP, prevents damage, or willingly accepts harm for another, it gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
a creature can trigger each Debt or Grace effect only once per turn.
The Court does not decide morality automatically. It magnifies Causes you Witness.

tianxia.talent.karma.great_oath:
#### Great Oath
Tags: Oath, Debt, Grace
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Ritual
Time: 1 hour
Range: Touch
Duration: Until fulfilled, broken, released, or dispelled by a superior effect
Cost: 8 CP
Bind one willing creature to one significant oath. Examples include:
protect this sect until the invasion ends;
never reveal the scripture;
return the stolen relic;
do not harm the heir;
serve until the debt is repaid;
carry this message to the ancestor hall before the new moon.
If the creature knowingly breaks the oath, the creature suffers all of the following:
takes 8d10 Psychic damage;
gains the maximum number of Debt Imprints you can place on it;
cannot regain CP until the next dawn;
you know the oath was broken;
the oath mark becomes visible to Karma, Divination, and Spirit Awakening until cleansed.
If the creature fulfills the oath at meaningful cost, it gains one persistent Grace Imprint from you. This Imprint lasts until spent, until the creature finishes seven long rests, or until the GM rules the grace has been honored.
A Great Oath cannot compel agreement. The creature must enter willingly.
Great Oath counts against Karmic Load.

tianxia.talent.karma.minor_oath:
#### Minor Oath
Tags: Oath, Debt, Grace
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Ritual
Time: 10 minutes
Range: Touch
Duration: 7 days or until fulfilled
Cost: 2 CP
Bind one willing creature to one clearly stated promise. Examples include:
do not reveal this location;
protect this person;
return this object;
do not attack until attacked;
deliver this message unopened;
repay this favor before the next moonrise.
If the creature knowingly breaks the oath, the oath ends and the creature suffers all of the following:
it gains the maximum number of Debt Imprints you can place on it;
it takes 2d8 Psychic damage;
you know the oath was broken;
the creature cannot benefit from your Grace Imprints until it finishes a long rest.
If the creature fulfills the oath at meaningful cost, you may place one Grace Imprint on it without using your Reaction.
Minor Oath counts against Karmic Load.

tianxia.talent.life.adrenaline_surge:
#### Adrenaline Surge - Breath, Response
When you use a Life sphere ability on an ally other than yourself, you may spend 1 CP to shock their living pattern into motion.
The ally may immediately use its Reaction to do one of the following:
make one weapon attack;
move up to its Speed;
make a Dexterity check to escape bonds, a grapple, or another physical restraint;
draw, pick up, or ready a weapon or shield;
stand up from Prone.
Surges are resolved in initiative order if multiple creatures surge at once.

tianxia.talent.life.meridian_unbinding:
#### Meridian Unbinding - Purification
Your Purify the Pulse can restore motion.
Augment - 1 CP: Purify the Pulse may remove one of the following:
Petrified;
Restrained;
one effect reducing the target’s Speed below its normal value;
one effect preventing the target from standing;
one effect preventing the target from using Reactions due to bodily restraint.
This does not remove mundane restraints unless your treatment gives the target a chance to escape them.

tianxia.talent.life.mind_cooling_pulse:
#### Mind-Cooling Pulse - Purification, Spirit
Your Life cultivation can calm the body’s panic and wake the spirit’s command over the flesh.
Augment - 1 CP: Purify the Pulse may remove one effect causing one of the following conditions:
Charmed;
Frightened;
Stunned;
Unconscious.
Spirit Awakening cultivators often learn this talent as a soul-stabilizing method.

tianxia.talent.life.physician_s_step:
#### Physician’s Step - Purification, Response
Your restorative touch restores enough coordination for movement.
When you use Purify the Pulse on a target, the target may immediately use its Reaction to do one of the following:
stand from Prone;
make a Strength (Athletics) check to escape a grapple, with Advantage;
make a Dexterity (Acrobatics) check to escape a grapple, with Advantage.

tianxia.talent.life.soul_in_the_body_tre:
#### Soul-in-the-Body Treatment - Purification, Spirit
You can treat injuries where the body and spirit have begun to disagree.
When you use Purify the Pulse on a target, you may spend 2 additional CP to affect one of the following:
possession;
forced soul displacement;
an effect preventing the soul from controlling the body;
an effect trapping the target’s awareness outside its body;
a Spirit Awakening effect causing Stunned, Unconscious, Frightened, or Charmed.
The target immediately makes a new saving throw against the effect with Advantage.
If the effect does not normally allow a saving throw, make a Cultivation Check against the effect’s save DC. On a success, the effect is suppressed for 1 minute.
This talent does not destroy the possessing entity or spiritual prison unless another feature says otherwise.

tianxia.talent.monkey_style.seventy_two_:
#### Seventy-Two Earthly Transformations
“Why remain one thing when the world contains so many useful shapes?”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Great Sage Equal to Heaven, hidden transformation scripture
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 hour
Cost: 10 Stamina or 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Chain Role: Transformation, Engine
Transform into one ordinary or supernatural beast form you have studied.
Choose one form template.
Tiny Scout: Tiny size, Speed 30 feet, Climb 30 feet, Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth).
Swift Beast: Speed 60 feet, Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics).
Climbing Beast: Climb Speed 50 feet, Advantage on Strength (Athletics).
Aquatic Beast: Swim Speed 60 feet and can breathe underwater.
Flying Beast: Fly Speed 50 feet. You do not gain Hover unless the studied form has Hover and the GM permits it.
Powerful Beast: Large size, Advantage on Strength checks, natural weapon 1d12.
Armored Beast: +3 AC, Speed reduced by 10 feet.
Burrowing Beast: Burrow Speed 30 feet through ordinary soil, sand, loose earth, or similar material.
You retain:
HP;
Stamina or CP;
mental ability scores;
cultivation talents;
personality;
Path features.
You gain only the listed template benefits.
You do not copy:
full monster stat blocks;
Legendary actions;
Lair actions;
Innate Spellcasting;
entire creature abilities;
unique boss traits;
Secret Inheritances.
Your transformation remains visibly unusual under close spiritual inspection.
While transformed, any template movement that changes elevation, slips through a hostile space, climbs, flies, swims, burrows, or uses beast agility may create a Monkey Link once per turn.

tianxia.talent.music.bell_that_reveals_f:
#### Bell That Reveals False Notes - Dissonance, Utility
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
For the duration, you and allies inside gain Advantage on checks to notice:
disguised voices;
false commands;
illusory sounds;
supernatural music;
hidden speakers;
possession speaking through a host;
concealed listeners;
emotional manipulation carried by sound.
Once during the duration, when a creature inside the aura fails such a check, you may allow it to reroll.

tianxia.talent.music.choir_of_the_split_:
#### Choir of the Split Spirit - Echo, Soul-Sound
Prerequisite: Echo Performer
When you create an Echo Performer, choose one improvement:
create two Echo Performers instead of one;
increase its AC to 16 and HP to your Proficiency Bonus;
it can maintain the visible origin of one Chord you sustain;
when you use Resonant Note through it, add your Proficiency Bonus to one damage roll;
it can deliver Harmonizing Breath to one willing creature within 5 feet of it when you use that talent.
You still maintain only one performance.

tianxia.talent.music.echo_performer:
#### Echo Performer - Echo
Action Type: Action
Range: 30 feet
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
Create an echoing duplicate, instrument-shadow, bell-image, drum-silhouette, voice afterimage, or similar projection.
The Echo Performer:
has AC 14;
has 1 HP;
has Speed 30 feet;
produces your voice or music;
can be the origin point of one Music effect you create;
can take the Help action for one creature that can perceive it;
can deliver Resonant Note from its position when you use that action;
disappears when damaged.
The Echo Performer does not create an additional performance and is not an independent creature.

tianxia.talent.music.echoing_step:
#### Echoing Step - Phrase, Cadence
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Until the end of the current turn
Cost: 1 CP or 1 Stamina
Your movement follows a cultivated rhythm.
Until the end of your turn:
ignore nonmagical difficult terrain;
do not provoke Opportunity Attacks from one creature that can perceive your Measure;
move through spaces occupied by willing allies;
leave a faint audible, spiritual, or visual echo.

tianxia.talent.music.festival_of_ten_tho:
#### Festival of Ten Thousand Listeners - Chord, Utility
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 10 minutes
Area: One village, sect courtyard, army camp, city district, valley, or similar area up to 1 mile across
Duration: 1 hour
Cost: 8 CP
Your performance reaches a vast but socially coherent area.
Choose one effect:
carry a message clearly to willing listeners;
calm a panicked population;
coordinate allied troops at a basic level;
grant Advantage on one morale-related saving throw;
suppress ordinary fear caused by rumor, panic, or confusion;
mark the beginning of a ritual, festival, funeral, wedding, duel, or sect ceremony.
Festival of Ten Thousand Listeners does not mind-control unwilling listeners and does not replace War logistics.

tianxia.talent.music.song_carried_across:
#### Song Carried Across Mountains - Chord, Utility
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 10 minutes
Duration: 1 hour
Cost: 10 CP
Your performance reaches a vast area.
Choose one:
a city district;
a battlefield;
a sect compound;
a valley;
a marching army;
an area approximately 1 mile across.
Choose one effect:
calm a panicked population;
carry a message clearly to every willing listener;
coordinate allied troops;
grant Advantage on one morale-related saving throw;
suppress ordinary fear;
mark the beginning of a ritual, festival, or sect ceremony;
allow willing listeners to sing or drum one simple response back to you.
Song Carried Across Mountains does not mind-control unwilling listeners.

tianxia.talent.music.song_of:
### Secret Music Inheritance - Song of the Forgotten Name
“The note was so pure that, for one breath, the world forgot what the enemy was called.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Symphony of Heaven and Earth, hidden musical inheritance
Action Type: Action
Range: 90 feet
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature that can hear or spiritually perceive you.
The target makes a Wisdom or Charisma saving throw, chosen by the GM according to the connection being targeted.
Failed Save: Choose one narrow identity-linked connection.
Examples include:
recognition by one group;
ability to issue commands to one bonded creature;
benefit from one named title or authority;
access to one named transformation;
use of one named technique;
control of one summoned creature;
one specific oath-linked benefit;
one musical, spiritual, or voice-based identity mark.
The chosen connection is suppressed for 1 hour.
Successful Save: The connection is suppressed until the start of your next turn.
Song of the Forgotten Name does not erase the target’s entire identity, memories, ancestry, cultivation base, character sheet, or existence. It suppresses one named connection that can be meaningfully sung out of tune.

tianxia.talent.music.unbroken_rhythm:
#### Unbroken Rhythm - Cadence
Prerequisite: Battle Cadence
While using Battle Cadence:
gain Advantage on saving throws against being knocked Prone;
reduce forced movement affecting you by 10 feet;
Opportunity Attacks against you are made with Disadvantage;
once per turn when you miss with a weapon attack, move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.

tianxia.talent.poison.antidote_art:
#### Antidote Art
You can use Appraise the Venom as practical treatment.
When you use Appraise the Venom on a creature, poison, food, drink, wound, or object, you may spend 1 CP and choose one:
end the Poisoned condition caused by an ordinary poison;
grant the target an immediate repeat saving throw against one Toxin Effect;
remove one Dose Mark from the target;
neutralize one ordinary poison dose on an object, weapon, food, or drink;
grant Advantage on the target’s next saving throw against poison before its next short rest.
If you have an Antidote Profile for the poison, the target also gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

tianxia.talent.poison.miasma_form:
#### Miasma Form
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
You become partly toxic vapor, poison mist, spirit spores, or corrosive breath.
For the duration, gain:
Fly Speed 30 feet and Hover;
Resistance to nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage;
Resistance to Poison and Acid damage;
Advantage on checks made to escape Grappled or Restrained;
ability to move through occupied spaces as difficult terrain;
ability to pass through openings as narrow as 1 inch.
You cannot pass through sealed barriers or solid objects.
When you move through a hostile creature’s space for the first time on a turn, it makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: The creature becomes Poisoned until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: No effect.

tianxia.talent.poison.perfect_antidote:
#### Perfect Antidote
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: 1 hour ritual
Range: Touch
Cost: 6 CP
You create one dose of perfected antidote for a poison you have an Antidote Profile for.
When consumed or administered, the antidote does all of the following:
ends Poisoned;
ends one Toxin Effect;
removes all Dose Marks from one creator;
removes all Toxin Burden from one creator;
grants Resistance to Poison and Acid damage for 8 hours;
grants Advantage on saving throws against poison for 8 hours;
suppresses one Legendary poison for 1 hour;
grants one treatment attempt against a Serious Ingrained Toxin with Advantage.
A dose remains potent for 30 days.
You may maintain a number of perfected antidote doses equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
Perfect Antidote does not automatically cure a Secret poison, but it allows a Cultivation Check against that poison if treatment would otherwise be impossible.

tianxia.talent.poison.perfected_counterd:
#### Perfected Counterdose
When you create an Antidote Profile, you may spend 3 CP to create a counterdose.
A counterdose lasts until you finish a long rest. You may maintain a number of counterdoses equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
A creature can consume or receive a counterdose as an Action. Choose one benefit:
end Poisoned;
end one Toxin Effect;
remove all Dose Marks from one creator;
remove 1 Toxin Burden;
grant Resistance to Poison and Acid damage for 1 hour;
grant Advantage on saving throws against one known poison for 8 hours.
A counterdose is tied to one Antidote Profile. It does not cure unrelated poisons.

tianxia.talent.poison.poison_sense:
#### Poison Sense
Your Appraise the Venom becomes a passive sense.
You sense obvious poison and toxic contamination within 30 feet.
You know whether:
food or drink is poisoned;
a visible creature is Poisoned;
a visible wound carries venom;
nearby air contains hazardous spores, gas, or toxic vapor;
an object has been coated with poison;
a corpse shows signs of toxic death.
Poison Sense does not reveal exact formulas, secret toxins, hidden creatures, invisible poison, or alchemical recipes.
At Core Formation Realm, the range increases to 60 feet.

tianxia.talent.poison.treating_serious_i:
#### Treating Serious Ingrained Toxin
A Serious Ingrained Toxin is meant to be dangerous but answerable.
Treatment may include:
Core Formation or higher Life purification;
a dedicated Alchemy antidote project;
a Poison cultivator using Appraise the Venom and Antidote Art with an Antidote Profile;
rare detoxifying materials worth at least 500 gp per treatment attempt;
a sect infirmary project;
a forged technique designed to purge cultivation poison;
a successful adventure to retrieve the proper antidote.
A treatment attempt normally requires 1 hour and a Cultivation Check, Medicine check, Alchemy check, or appropriate sphere check against your Cultivation Save DC.
Success: Reduce the stage by 1. If this would reduce the poison below Stage 1, the poison ends.
Failure: The poison remains. The GM may impose a complication if the treatment was reckless.
Serious Ingrained Toxin should not permanently scatter a cultivation base unless the target fails repeatedly, the table wants that story, and the GM treats it as a major campaign event.

tianxia.talent.poison.valley_of_poisonou:
#### Valley of Poisonous Immortals
Action Type: Strategic Project
Timing Detail: 30-day strategic project
Cost: 10 CP committed at the beginning of the project, plus 25,000 gp in rare toxins, plants, beast materials, mineral reagents, and alchemical equipment
You create a permanent toxic cultivation site.
Choose three benefits:
produce rare poison ingredients worth 500 gp each month;
support Poison and Alchemy projects;
protect an area against ordinary vermin and hostile beasts;
create concealed toxic defenses;
grant +2 to checks made to identify, refine, resist, or treat poison in the site;
provide a safe training environment for poison cultivators;
allow antidote preparation in half the ordinary time;
improve Flower, Blood, Disease, or Alchemy poison-related techniques;
create a secure toxin archive;
cultivate medicinal organisms useful for antidotes.
You may maintain a number of Valleys equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
A Valley of Poisonous Immortals is socially dangerous. Orthodox sects may require licenses, inspections, quarantine formations, and antidote reserves.

tianxia.talent.poison.venom_sovereign_in:
#### Venom-Sovereign Incarnation
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minuteConcentration: Not required
Cost: 10 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You transform into a perfected toxic incarnation.
For the duration, gain:
Fly Speed 40 feet and Hover;
Immunity to Poison damage;
Resistance to Acid and Necrotic damage;
Immunity to Poisoned;
Deliver the Dose deals 6d10 Poison or Acid damage instead of its normal damage;
your Poison talents ignore ordinary Resistance to Poison and Acid damage.

tianxia.talent.poison.virulent_presence:
#### Virulent Presence
While Venom-Sovereign Incarnation is active, when an enemy starts its turn within 20 feet of you, it makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one:
the enemy takes 4d8 Poison or Acid damage;
the enemy becomes Poisoned until the start of its next turn;
the enemy cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
healing the enemy receives is halved until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: The enemy takes half of 4d8 Poison or Acid damage, or suffers no effect if you chose a non-damaging option.
A creature is affected only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.pressure_points.the_point:
### The Point Between Heartbeats
“The immortal prepared ten thousand answers. The master touched the silence before the first one began.”
Prerequisite: Sovereign Nine-Gate Hand, CL 17+, hidden meridian scripture or personal enlightenment
Action Type: Action
Range: 90 feet
Cost: Expend Martial Focus and 6 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature you can perceive. A single impossible point appears in its body, spirit, technique, shadow, or fate-like rhythm for one breath.
The target makes a Constitution saving throw. If the target lacks ordinary anatomy but has a readable spiritual, mechanical, elemental, or conceptual structure, it makes a Wisdom saving throw instead.
#### Failed Save
The target is sealed until the end of its next turn.
While sealed this way:
it is Incapacitated;
its Speed is 0;
it cannot speak clearly or provide Verbal components;
it loses Concentration;
ongoing non-Secret body-enhancing, movement-enhancing, and technique-channeling effects on it are suppressed;
it cannot take Reactions, Bonus Actions, Legendary Actions, or similar extra actions;
the next attack roll made against it before the seal ends has Advantage and deals an extra 6d10 Force or Psychic damage on a hit.
#### Successful Save
The target is partially sealed until the start of your next turn.
While partially sealed this way:
it cannot take Reactions;
its Speed is halved;
it has Disadvantage on Concentration saving throws;
the next attack roll made against it before the partial seal ends has Advantage.
#### Limits
The Point Between Heartbeats cannot permanently disable a creature, erase a Path, remove a Realm, destroy a soul, suppress a Secret Inheritance automatically, or rewrite destiny.
A creature of superior Realm, divine office, or narrative-scale authority may convert the failed-save result into the successful-save result by winning an opposed Cultivation Check, at the GM’s discretion.

tianxia.talent.protection.adaptation:
#### Adaptation - Aegis
Prerequisite: Energy Resistance and one future environmental-protection Aegis, CL 10+
Cost: +4 CP
When applying the required environmental-protection Aegis, improve it.
The bearer becomes immune to:
extreme heat;
extreme cold;
toxic air;
drowning;
vacuum exposure. The bearer gains Resistance to:
Acid;
Cold;
Fire;
Lightning;
Radiant;
Thunder. Additional Resistances may be added if you know future talents that explicitly provide them.
Source gap: Adaptation remains provisional because the supplied source did not include the referenced environmental-protection talents.

tianxia.talent.protection.anti_magic_aur:
#### Anti-Magic Aura - Ward
Prerequisite: Spell Ward, CL 12+
Action Type: Action
Range: Self only
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
Create a Spell Ward centered on yourself.
No Cultivation Check is required.
Inside the Ward:
ordinary supernatural effects are suppressed;
ordinary magic items cease functioning;
summoned creatures temporarily disappear;
new supernatural effects fail automatically. Anti-Magic Aura does not automatically suppress:
Domains;
Secret Inheritances;
Formation cores;
Realm-defining transformations;
artifacts;
effects explicitly written to resist anti-magic suppression. Those require a contested Cultivation Check or a separate ruling.

tianxia.talent.protection.energy_resista:
#### Energy Resistance - Aegis, Ward Choose one damage type:
Acid;
Cold;
Fire;
Lightning;
Radiant;
Thunder.
##### Aegis The bearer gains Resistance to the chosen damage type.
##### Ward
Creatures inside gain Resistance to the chosen damage type while they remain inside.

tianxia.talent.protection.exclusion:
#### Exclusion - Ward
Choose one common material, element, or physical property when creating the Ward.
Examples include:
stone;
metal;
water;
acid;
fire;
light;
poisonous material;
living material. A creature made of or carrying the excluded substance must make a Strength check against your Cultivation Save DC to cross the Ward’s edge.
Failed Check: The creature cannot cross while carrying or embodying the excluded substance.
Successful Check: The creature crosses normally.
A creature may drop carried excluded material before attempting to cross.
An attack crossing into the Ward while composed primarily of the excluded substance has Disadvantage.
Exclusion does not remove material already inside.

tianxia.talent.protection.impartiality:
#### Impartiality - Aegis, Ward Protected creatures are treated as having no alignment for magical effects.
This does not disguise alignment. It creates an absence.
The Aegis or Ward also conceals the creature type of:
Celestials;
Fiends;
Fey;
Undead. A creature still remains its actual creature type for effects that do not rely on detection.

tianxia.talent.protection.obscurity:
#### Obscurity - Aegis, Ward
Protected creatures appear unremarkable and unimportant.
A creature attempting to notice a protected creature makes an Intelligence saving throw before making any Wisdom (Perception) check.
Failed Save: It fails to notice the protected creature.
Successful Save: It may perceive the creature normally until the protected creature leaves its sight or successfully Hides.
A creature automatically succeeds if it:
is already in combat with the protected creature;
is specifically searching for that creature;
has been clearly told the creature is present;
possesses a talent that explicitly bypasses Obscurity.

tianxia.talent.protection.repel_spirit_k:
#### Repel Spirit-Kin - Ward
Choose one or more creature families appropriate to the setting:
Celestials;
Fiends;
Fey;
Undead. A chosen creature attempting to cross the Ward’s edge makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: It cannot cross.
Successful Save: It may cross and becomes immune to your Repel Spirit-Kin Ward until the next dawn.
A creature already inside when the Ward appears is unaffected.

tianxia.talent.protection.sanctuary_with:
#### Sanctuary Without Borders - Ward
Prerequisite: Peacebound or Impedance, CL 12+
Action Type: Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
Choose one Ward you create.
When a willing creature enters the Ward for the first time on a turn or starts its turn inside, it may immediately end one of the following:
Frightened;
Grappled;
Restrained;
one ordinary forced-movement effect;
one ordinary ongoing damage effect caused by a talent. A creature may benefit once per activation.
Sanctuary Without Borders does not end curses, Domains, Secret effects, or permanent injuries.

tianxia.talent.protection.slippery:
#### Slippery - Aegis
Protect the bearer from physical restraint and manipulation.
The bearer gains Advantage on:
saving throws against being Restrained;
saving throws against forced movement;
checks made to avoid being shoved;
checks made to escape a Grapple;
checks made to squeeze through a tight space;
checks made to escape bonds.

tianxia.talent.protection.unplottable:
#### Unplottable - Aegis
Prerequisite: Obscurity, CL 15+
Cost: +3 CP
When applying Obscurity Aegis, make the bearer undetectable through ordinary divination.
Attempts to gather information directly about the bearer automatically fail.
This includes ordinary:
scrying;
supernatural tracking;
effects that reveal Invisible;
alignment detection;
creature-type detection. Area scans still function normally, but the bearer does not appear inside them.
Unplottable does not automatically defeat:
Secret divination inheritances;
artifacts;
Domains;
direct observation;
effects explicitly written to overcome it.

tianxia.talent.puppetry.borrowed_body_pe:
### Borrowed Body Performance - Thread, Substitute
Prerequisite: Voice Through the Doll, CL 12+
As an Action, choose one active puppet vessel.
Until the start of your next turn, perceive through the vessel’s hearing and sight if it has appropriate carved senses, gemstone eyes, spirit mirrors, or similar features.
During that time:
you are Blinded and Deafened to your own body’s surroundings;
you may speak through the vessel;
you may take the Help, Search, Study, or Utilize action through the vessel;
you may make one Puppet Strike through the vessel as a Bonus Action if you have not already used Puppet Strike this turn.

tianxia.talent.puppetry.red_thread_comma:
### Red Thread Command Seat - Vessel, Thread
Prerequisite: CL 12+
You may sit, stand, or meditate inside a specially prepared command rig, puppet chair, palanquin, coffin-cart, or suspended thread frame.
While using the command seat:
you cannot move except by directing the seat or being carried;
your control range increases by 120 feet;
you may maintain one additional active puppet vessel;
if an enemy damages the command seat, you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against DC 10 or half the damage taken, whichever is higher, or lose Concentration on one Puppetry effect.
The command seat is an object with AC 15 and Hit Points equal to 10 + five times your CL unless built better by Blacksmith, Metal, or crafting.

tianxia.talent.puppetry.red_thread_world:
### Red Thread World-Puppet Array - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: Puppet Theater Domain, CL 15+
When you create Puppet Theater Domain, you may anchor it to visible threads, hanging banners, stage ropes, chains, roots, wires, or Formation lines in the area.
For the duration:
the Domain area increases to a 60-foot Emanation;
hostile creatures treat the area within 5 feet of your puppet vessels as Difficult Terrain;
once per round, when a hostile creature fails a saving throw against one of your Puppetry talents, move one puppet vessel up to its Speed without spending an Action;
allied creatures inside gain Advantage on saving throws against being Grappled or Restrained.
If all anchors are destroyed or severed, the Domain ends.

tianxia.talent.radiance.consecrated_lant:
##### Consecrated Lantern - Revelation
When you create Glow, you may make it a Consecrated Lantern.
A Consecrated Lantern lasts 8 hours instead of 1 hour.
While a creature carries or wears it, the creature gains Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) or Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to notice:
fresh spiritual residue;
signs of possession;
hidden writing;
concealed bloodstains;
undead traces;
corruption marks;
an object or creature already bearing your Dawnmark.
You may maintain a number of Consecrated Lanterns equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

tianxia.talent.radiance.court_of_unshado:
##### Court of Unshadowed Dawn - Domain
“Every shadow in the court understood that it was only waiting for permission to confess.”
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius Emanation originating from you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 7 CP
Use Limit: Once per short rest
Create a Domain of judgment-bearing dawn.
Inside the Domain, you and allies you designate gain the following benefits:
Resistance to Necrotic damage;
Advantage on saving throws against Charmed, Frightened, possession, and corruption;
ordinary Darkness and Dim Light do not impose penalties on sight;
ordinary Blinded effects caused by light or darkness are suppressed at the start of the ally’s turn;
once per round when an ally succeeds on a saving throw against Charmed, Frightened, possession, or corruption, that ally gains Temporary HP equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
Enemies inside the Domain suffer the following effects:
ordinary Invisible provides no benefit;
ordinary visual concealment cannot be used to Hide from creatures inside the Domain;
disguises and illusions visibly strain;
Unclean creatures cannot regain HP while inside the Domain;
when a hostile creature starts its turn inside, it makes a Constitution or Wisdom saving throw, your choice when you create the Domain.
Failed Save: Choose one:
the creature is Blinded until the start of its next turn;
the creature cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
the creature takes 2d8 Radiant damage;
the creature cannot regain HP or gain Temporary HP until the start of its next turn;
suppress one ordinary corruption-derived temporary benefit on the creature until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: The creature cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.
A sightless creature automatically succeeds against the Blinded option but remains subject to the non-visual effects.

tianxia.talent.radiance.crown_of_the_unb:
##### Crown of the Unblinking Sun
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 10 CP
A crown of unwavering dawn appears above you.
For the duration:
you cannot be Blinded;
you gain Truesight out to 30 feet, but only for perceiving illusions, disguises, possession signs, magical darkness, and spiritual corruption;
your Radiance talents affect incorporeal Unclean creatures normally;
when an Unclean creature fails a save against your Radiance talent, it also cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
once per turn, when you apply Dawnmark, you may extend it to one additional hostile creature within 10 feet of the original target.
The Truesight granted by this talent does not reveal every secret door, ethereal creature, or planar boundary unrelated to Radiance’s purifying scope.

tianxia.talent.radiance.dawnmark_scriptu:
##### Dawnmark Scripture - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Your Dawnmark becomes a stable spiritual brand rather than a momentary gleam.
Gain the following benefits:
your Dawnmark lasts until the end of your next turn;
your Dawnmark sheds Bright Light in its space and Dim Light for 5 feet;
when a creature bearing your Dawnmark starts its turn, you may choose to make the mark flare; if you do, the creature cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
once per turn when you damage an Unclean creature bearing your Dawnmark, add 1d8 Radiant damage;
you may use Mark talents on a Dawnmarked target within 60 feet even if you cannot currently see the target, provided you know its direction and there is a legal route for the technique.
Dawnmark Scripture does not reveal exact position through Total Cover or bypass sealed barriers.

tianxia.talent.radiance.expose_false_for:
##### Expose False Form - Mark, Revelation
When you apply Dawnmark to a creature, you may pay 1 CP.
Until the Dawnmark ends:
the target cannot benefit from ordinary Invisible;
the target has Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks relying on visual concealment;
ordinary disguises and illusions covering the target visibly shimmer;
attacks against the target ignore ordinary visual concealment if the attacker can see the Dawnmark.
Expose False Form does not reveal exact position through Total Cover or automatically defeat superior illusion or transformation techniques.

tianxia.talent.radiance.first_dawn_befor:
##### First Dawn Before Falsehood
“Before the first mask, before the first grave refused rest, before the first shadow learned to lie, there was morning.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Heavenly Radiance, hidden primordial-dawn inheritance
Action Type: Action
Area: 90-foot-radius Emanation originating from you
Duration: 1 minute Concentration: Required
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
You manifest the memory of the world’s first dawn.
Inside the area, the following effects are suppressed unless created by a Legendary or Secret technique, artifact, major Formation, divine source, or Realm-defining phenomenon:
ordinary Invisible;
ordinary illusions and disguises;
ordinary Darkness and non-Legendary magical Darkness;
ordinary fear auras;
ordinary charm-based glamour;
possession concealment;
visible corruption-derived temporary benefits;
hidden writing and concealed spiritual residue;
shadow travel that relies on ordinary or non-Legendary shadows.
A Legendary or Secret concealment, corruption, possession, or darkness effect may resist with an opposed Cultivation Check.
When you create the Emanation, hostile creatures of your choice inside make Wisdom saving throws. Unclean creatures have Disadvantage.
Failed Save: Choose three different consequences for that creature:
take 8d10 Radiant damage;
become Blinded until the end of your next turn;
cannot take Reactions until the end of your next turn;
cannot regain HP or gain Temporary HP until the end of your next turn;
suppress one corruption-derived temporary benefit until the end of your next turn;
end one ordinary invisibility, disguise, or illusion covering it;
force a possessing entity to reveal itself and lose the benefit of concealment until the end of your next turn;
apply Dawnmark for the full duration of the inheritance.
Successful Save: Choose one consequence other than the full-duration Dawnmark.
Allies of your choice inside the Emanation immediately gain the following benefits:
may repeat one saving throw against Charmed, Frightened, possession, corruption, Poisoned, or a curse;
gain Temporary HP equal to 3 × your Proficiency Bonus;
may see ordinary Invisible and ordinary illusion-covered creatures revealed by the inheritance;
cannot be Blinded by ordinary light or darkness while inside the Emanation.
First Dawn Before Falsehood cannot automatically:
destroy a god;
erase an entire bloodline curse;
break a campaign-defining oath;
reveal every secret in a city;
identify every spy without evidence;
override a Secret Inheritance without a contest;
purify a willing villain who has made corruption part of their Dao;
turn Radiance into unrestricted Divination.
When the inheritance ends, choose one Dawnmark created by it. That Dawnmark lasts until the end of your next turn.

tianxia.talent.radiance.heaven_reading_d:
##### Heaven-Reading Dawnbeam - Revelation
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Range: 120 feet
Cost: 5 CP
Choose one creature, object, corpse, doorway, seal, or obvious magical effect you can see.
A pillar of radiance falls across the target.
Make a Cultivation Check against the target’s Save DC, the creator’s Save DC, or a DC set by the GM.
Success: Learn up to two of the following:
whether it is Unclean;
whether it is possessed or serving as a possession anchor;
whether it bears a curse or spiritual contamination;
whether it is disguised or under an illusion;
whether it recently harmed a creature through necrotic, radiant, fear, charm, or possession pressure;
whether it is maintaining a concealment effect;
whether one obvious corruption-derived benefit is active.
Failure: Learn one obvious surface truth and apply Dawnmark until the start of your next turn if the target is a creature.
This talent does not reveal a target’s full statistics, future actions, secret name, or complete history.

tianxia.talent.radiance.revealing_light:
##### Revealing Light - Revelation, Aura
Action Type: Action
Area: 20-foot-radius Emanation originating from you
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 2 CP
You surround yourself with searching dawnlight.
Inside the aura:
ordinary darkness is suppressed;
ordinary Invisible provides no benefit against creatures that can see the target;
creatures have Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks relying on visual concealment;
ordinary disguises, false faces, and obvious illusions become visibly strained;
hidden writing, concealed doors, fresh blood, lingering spiritual residue, and signs of corruption are easier to detect;
a creature bearing your Dawnmark cannot benefit from ordinary visual concealment.
Revealing Light does not automatically answer questions, reveal exact squares through Total Cover, or defeat Legendary or Secret concealment.

tianxia.talent.radiance.searing_halo:
##### Searing Halo - Aura
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 2 CP
A sharp halo forms behind your head, weapon, palm, or back.
For the duration:
you shed Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for another 20 feet;
once per turn when Radiance Strike hits, deal +1d8 Radiant damage;
a creature that hits you with a melee attack while within 5 feet takes Radiant damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus;
you gain Advantage on saving throws against being Frightened by Unclean creatures.

tianxia.talent.radiance.unhidden_stain_s:
##### Unhidden Stain Sight - Revelation
Prerequisite: CL 5+
While you are in Bright Light, your Glow, a Consecrated Boundary, or your Revealing Light, you may use a Bonus Action to inspect one creature or object you can see within 60 feet.
Make a Wisdom (Insight), Intelligence (Investigation), or Cultivation Check against the target’s passive Deception, passive Stealth, or an appropriate DC set by the GM.
Success: Learn whether the target bears one of the following obvious spiritual conditions:
possession;
undeath;
active corruption;
a curse currently affecting behavior;
a disguise or illusion covering its true form;
a recent contact with an Unclean force.
This does not identify the exact source, full stat block, future intention, or hidden name of the effect.

tianxia.talent.radiance.world_of_reveale:
##### World of Revealed Morning
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Action
Range: 120 feet
Area: 60-foot-radius sphere
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 12 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Fill the area with overwhelming revealed morning.
Inside the area, allies you designate gain:
Resistance to Necrotic and Radiant damage;
Advantage on checks made to detect hidden creatures, possession, curses, and spiritual contamination;
Advantage on saving throws against Charmed, Frightened, possession, and corruption;
immunity to ordinary Blinded effects caused by light or darkness;
the ability to ignore ordinary Darkness and ordinary visual concealment.
Hostile creatures inside suffer:
ordinary Invisible fails;
ordinary illusions and disguises visibly shimmer;
ordinary Darkness disappears;
corruption marks, undead residue, possession anchors, and fresh spiritual stains become visible;
Unclean creatures cannot regain HP and cannot gain Temporary HP.
When a hostile creature enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn inside, it makes a Constitution saving throw.
Failed Save: Take 4d8 Radiant damage and become Blinded until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Take half damage and cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn.
A creature takes this damage only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.retribution.read_the_tell:
### Read the Tell - Unique Retribution Talent
Prerequisite: CL 5+
When you prepare Counterstrike, choose one creature you can see within 60 feet.
Until the start of your next turn, gain Advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks made to recognize that creature’s immediate intent, feints, combat habits, or emotional commitment.
The GM may reveal one broad category the creature appears prepared to attempt, such as:
attack;
move;
flee;
cast or activate a supernatural effect;
defend;
speak or issue a command;
wait for another creature.
Read the Tell does not reveal an exact ability, guarantee that the creature follows through, or bypass deception automatically.

tianxia.talent.scoundrel.the_dao_of_sham:
#### THE DAO OF SHAMELESS SURVIVAL - ESCAPE
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You would drop to 0 HP, fail a saving throw, gain Grappled or Restrained, or become the target of an attack
Cost: Expend Martial Focus
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Choose one:
drop to 1 HP instead of 0 HP;
turn the failed saving throw into a success;
move up to 60 feet into a legal space you can perceive before the triggering attack resolves;
redirect one legal single-target attack to another creature within 10 feet of you;
end one ordinary Grappled, Restrained, Prone, or disarmed effect affecting you;
reveal one previously prepared mundane object that solves the immediate physical problem.
A Legendary or Secret effect may resist with an opposed Cultivation Check.
The Dao of Shameless Survival cannot rewrite a previous turn, negate an entire area effect automatically, create an artifact, or pass through a sealed Barrier without a legal route.

tianxia.talent.sect_stewardship.found_a_:
### Found a Branch Hall - Lineage, Steward, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
You can plant a sect presence without mistaking a building for a lineage.
With GM approval, appropriate authority, 1 year of work, and major resources, you may found or reorganize a branch hall, village protectorate, outer academy, medicine station, scripture school, pilgrimage lodge, field office, or resource outpost.
Choose the branch’s first purpose:
teaching;
medicine;
farming administration;
gathering permissions;
archive preservation;
mission staging;
guest diplomacy;
disaster relief;
trade oversight;
outer disciple training.
While present in the branch and acting according to its purpose, your Merit Die increases by one step, to a maximum of d10.
The branch is a strategic asset. It can be attacked, corrupted, starved, praised, taxed, abandoned, or inherited.

tianxia.talent.sect_stewardship.hall_app:
### Hall Apprenticeship - Steward, Pavilion
Prerequisite: CL 5+.
Choose one hall where you have trained: Medicine Hall, Scripture Pavilion, Mission Hall, Storehouse, Kitchen, Spirit Field Office, Forge Office, Formation Maintenance Office, Beast Yard, Guest Hall, or another GM-approved department.
When you work in that hall for at least 1 hour, you may spend one Merit Die and choose one benefit:
gain Advantage on one non-combat check using that hall’s tools or records;
reduce the time for one ordinary hall task by half;
identify the proper superior, clerk, or specialist for a problem;
secure supervised access to common equipment;
learn one ordinary rule, fee, or requirement for using the hall.
You may take this talent multiple times, choosing a different hall each time.

tianxia.talent.sect_stewardship.inner_ar:
### Inner Archive Index - Pavilion, Ledger
Prerequisite: CL 10+.
You do not know every scripture, but you know how they are shelved.
After spending at least 1 hour in a library, Scripture Pavilion, clan archive, mission record vault, or comparable collection, spend one Merit Die and make a Sect Check.
On a success, find one of the following if it exists and is not forbidden to your current access:
a clue to a technique’s teacher or location;
a safe public summary of a restricted topic;
an old map or mission report;
a recipe title and required permission level;
a precedent in sect law;
a list of known hazards for a region;
a lineage note connecting two people, halls, or events.
On a success by 5 or more, you also learn what permission, Standing, mission, sponsor, or price would be needed to reach the next layer of information.
This talent finds indexes and references. It does not grant secret manuals by itself.

tianxia.talent.sect_stewardship.open_the:
### Open the Grand Archive - Pavilion, Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+.
Once per campaign arc, or once per year of downtime with GM approval, you may spend one Merit Die to petition for access to a Grand Archive, ancestral catalogue, restricted scripture index, founding record, sealed court transcript, or comparable high institution record.
Make a Sect Check.
On a success, you do not gain a secret technique directly. Instead, choose one:
learn the true name of a lost scripture;
learn the required trial for a Secret Inheritance;
discover which elder or branch controls a forbidden record;
identify a historical lie in the sect’s public story;
find the map to a lost branch hall, medicine garden, battlefield, tomb, or oath site;
learn why a technique was banned, sealed, or restricted.
On a failure, you learn what price, sponsor, trial, rank, or political concession would be needed to try again.

tianxia.talent.shadow.shadow_signal:
### Shadow Signal
Action Type: Action
Range: 1 mile
Duration: 10 minutes
Cost: 1 CP
Project a simple silhouette onto a visible surface.
Examples include:
a warning symbol;
an arrow;
a written message;
a moving figure;
a map-like outline;
a concealed mark visible only from one angle.

tianxia.talent.shield.projected_shield_f:
#### PROJECTED SHIELD FACE - REALM EVOLUTION
Prerequisite: CL 5+
While wielding a Shield, your Active Defense and Face talents may manifest visible or nearly invisible Shield-Qi.
A projected Shield Face may appear as:
a translucent shield several times larger than the physical Shield;
overlapping scales of compressed Qi;
a rotating mirror-bright disc;
an ancestral shield emblem;
a circular ripple that catches the incoming attack;
a scripture-specific spiritual rampart.
Gain the following benefits:
Active Defense and your Deflect talents may affect magical attack rolls, ghost strikes, incorporeal attacks, and Cultivation Attack rolls normally.
When using Cover Ally, increase its range to 15 feet. You still require a clear legal route from your Shield to the ally and must be able to present the projected face toward the incoming attack.
When using Flexible Cover, the Shield Face becomes a 15-foot-wide, 10-foot-high plane centered on the chosen edge of your space.
A projected Shield Face remains attached to you, moves with you, and protects creatures behind it when an attack or effect physically crosses its surface.
Projected Shield Face does not:
become a free-standing Barrier;
block movement;
grant general telekinesis;
pass through Total Cover or a sealed Barrier;
protect against teleportation, gaze effects, possession, or effects that do not cross its surface;
allow a mundane Shield to answer a narrative-scale calamity without an appropriate higher-Realm talent.

tianxia.talent.shield.the_world_has_only:
#### THE WORLD HAS ONLY ONE FRONT
“Heaven sent its judgment from every direction. The old shield-bearer raised one hand and taught Heaven where the front was.”
Prerequisite: Sovereign Shield-Soul Incarnation, CL 17+, hidden shield scripture or equivalent narrative inheritance
Action Type: Reaction
Trigger: You perceive an attack, area effect, siege strike, breath weapon, physically traveling cultivation technique, or narrative-scale calamity entering a battlefield within 300 feet
Cost: Expend Martial Focus; your wielded Shield becomes spiritually exhausted when the technique ends
Use Limit: Once per week
Manifest one colossal Shield Face along a visible legal line within range.
The face may be up to:
300 feet wide and 150 feet high
Choose one defended side.
Until the end of your next turn, the Shield Face is a Barrier and the battlefield recognizes it as the single meaningful front of the conflict.
Choose Hold or Turn when manifesting the face.
##### HOLD
The Shield Face stops the triggering effect at its surface.
Creatures and objects on the defended side gain Total Cover against the triggering effect when the effect must cross the face to reach them.
The face may hold against:
siege fire;
a dragon’s breath;
a flood front;
an avalanche;
a collapsing fortress wall;
a descending celestial weapon;
a massed projectile storm;
a physically traveling Nascent Soul technique;
another comparable calamity.
A superior Secret, Legendary, or narrative-scale effect may force an opposed Cultivation Check.
##### TURN
Attempt to turn the triggering effect aside or return it.
Make a Cultivation Check against the creator’s Cultivation Save DC or an appropriate narrative-scale DC.
Successful Check: Choose one legal new direction, destination, or origin-facing return route. Resolve the remaining physically traveling portion of the effect along that route.
Failed Check: The face still holds long enough for creatures on the defended side to move up to their Speed as a Reaction without provoking Opportunity Attacks. The triggering effect then resolves with creatures behind the face gaining Resistance to its damage and Advantage on saving throws against its additional effects.
##### LIMITS
The World Has Only One Front does not automatically stop or turn:
teleportation;
planar travel;
Ethereal travel;
possession;
gaze effects;
mind-affecting effects that do not cross the face;
effects originating behind the face;
a curse already inside a creature;
an entire Domain merely because the face intersects it;
a cosmic office, destiny, or permanent law of reality;
a superior inheritance without an appropriate opposed check or narrative resolution.
When the technique ends, your Shield becomes spiritually exhausted.
Until repaired through one Long Rest, suitable maintenance, and any additional narrative requirement imposed by the GM:
it grants no Shield Bonus;
it cannot be used for Shield talents;
an artifact Shield may require a specific refining material, oath, trial, or master artisan.

tianxia.talent.sniper.sniper_s_nest_scri:
#### Sniper’s Nest Scripture - Line, Utility
Prerequisite: CL 5+
During 1 minute of preparation, you prepare a firing position: rooftop, tree fork, cliff ledge, ruined window, wagon bed, formation notch, dune crest, battlefield corpse pile, or similar site.
Until you leave that position for more than 1 round, you gain the following benefits while there:
you can use Shift Position even if you move up to 10 feet within the prepared position;
you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice movement inside your weapon’s normal range;
your first Snipe Shot from the position after rolling Initiative has an Aimed Line;
Half Cover from the position counts as Three-Quarters Cover against ranged attacks from creatures you can perceive.
You can maintain one Sniper’s Nest at a time unless a project, formation, item, or higher-Realm talent expands this.

tianxia.talent.space.expand_the_room:
#### Expand the Room
Tag: Pocket Art.
Action Type: Action
Range: 30 feet.
Duration: 10 minutes.
Cost: 3 CP.
Choose a chamber, corridor, courtyard, vehicle interior, tent, cave mouth, or other bounded space no larger than a 30-foot cube.
For the duration, its interior counts as up to twice as large for ordinary movement and occupancy, while its exterior size remains unchanged.
This can:
allow more creatures to fit comfortably;
create room for a ritual or duel;
let a narrow passage hold more defenders;
make a cramped room less restrictive.
This cannot:
crush creatures when it ends;
create infinite space;
bypass a dimensional lock;
produce valuable material;
safely nest another pocket space without GM permission.

tianxia.talent.space.pocket_sanctuary:
#### Pocket Sanctuary
Tag: Pocket Art.
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 1 hour.
Duration: 8 hours.
Cost: 8 CP.
Create a small extradimensional chamber with one visible entrance.
The chamber:
holds up to 10 Medium creatures;
contains breathable air;
is approximately 20 feet across;
has one entrance;
cannot move after creation;
cannot be created inside another extradimensional space;
cannot be used to trap unwilling creatures unless they enter or are forced through the entrance by another legal effect.
The entrance has AC 15 and Hit Points equal to 10 times your CL. It is immune to Poison and Psychic damage.
Destroying the entrance ejects all occupants harmlessly into the nearest available spaces.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.ancestr:
### Ancestral Ear
When you use Read the Spirit Nature, you can also hear the emotional tone of the spirit's presence.
You learn whether the spirit is dominated by one of the following:
- grief;
- hunger;
- duty;
- rage;
- fear;
- loyalty;
- curiosity;
- shame;
- pride;
- joy;
- confusion;
- sacred obligation;
- predatory instinct.
If the spirit is an ancestor, family guardian, oath spirit, or old companion spirit, you have Advantage on the first social check you make toward respectful communication.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.avatar_:
### Avatar Hosting
A willing spirit may descend into you as an avatar.
Action Type: Action
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
Choose one willing Major Spirit Bond that is hosted in you or touching you.
For the duration, you and the spirit act as one avatar.
You gain:
- one major physical or spiritual transformation based on the spirit's Nature;
- one active Nature Expression without needing to separately command the spirit;
- Advantage on saving throws against fear, possession, and forced separation;
- resistance to one damage type tied to the spirit's Nature;
- the ability to originate body-bound or aura-bound Nature Expressions from yourself.
At the start of each of your turns, if your intended action violates the spirit's Nature or Taboo, make a contested key ability check against the spirit.
If you fail, choose one:
- your action is altered by the spirit's Nature;
- Bond Strain increases by 1;
- the avatar ends.
Avatar Hosting does not allow a Body Refiner to freely project unrelated qi. The avatar may externalize the spirit's Nature only where the talent or spirit expression permits.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.court_o:
### Court of Small Spirits
You can coordinate many lesser spirits without making each one a full companion.
Your Minor Spirit Agreements can act together as a court.
During a short rest or 10-minute ritual, you may ask your court for one collective service:
- survey a small location;
- carry rumors across a district;
- identify a spiritual taboo in the area;
- create a harmless distraction;
- help maintain a shrine;
- watch a sleeping camp;
- find a spirit trail;
- deliver a simple message to a nearby spirit;
- gather minor offerings.
Once per long rest, the court may also grant Advantage on one Read the Spirit Nature check.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.covenan:
### Covenant Spirit
You may form a Covenant Bond with one willing spirit as your Major Spirit Bond.
The spirit gains:
- one Spirit Nature;
- one Need / Offering;
- one Taboo;
- one simple Nature Expression;
- one manifestation form;
- one role such as scout, guardian, singer, ambusher, guide, ritual assistant, shrine attendant, omen-bearer, or domain anchor.
This talent is the normal entry point for ethical spirit relationships.
This talent does not automatically make the spirit a full Chapter 13 bonded companion. By default, the spirit acts through its Nature Expression, bond role, manifestations, and noncombat presence.
If the spirit has separately been gained as a full combat-capable companion through an Insight, roleplaying reward, inheritance, GM approval, or another feature, use Chapter 13 for its companion statistics and combat action economy. Then add this spirit's Nature, Need, Taboo, and Nature Expressions from this sphere.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.deep_ho:
### Deep Hosting
A hosted spirit can dwell closer to your cultivation base.
Choose one hosted spirit. It may occupy one deep vessel:
- dantian;
- heart blood;
- spine;
- bones;
- inner palace;
- shadow root;
- dream core;
- soul wound;
- weapon soul;
- ancestral mark.
While deeply hosted, the spirit grants one stronger body-bound expression chosen from its Nature.
Examples:
- a blood spirit lets your wounds feed a counterattack;
- a flower spirit roots through your blood and drinks hostile qi on contact;
- a storm spirit accelerates your movement for one round;
- an ancestor spirit steadies you against fear;
- a weapon spirit lets you call the weapon back to hand;
- a corpse-lamp spirit lets you see ghosts in dim light.
Deep Hosting is powerful but risky. Whenever Bond Strain reaches 3, the hosted spirit may contest influence over the host.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.dual_na:
### Dual Nature Expression
Choose one Major Spirit Bond.
The spirit may treat a second Nature Sphere as active for purposes of Spirit Nature Expressions.
If the spirit already had two Nature Spheres, choose one additional Nature Tag and design one expression that blends two of its Natures.
Example blends:
- Flower + Blood = blood-drinking vines;
- Death + Music = funeral song that weakens ghosts;
- Weather + Spear = storm-lance spirit thrust;
- Dreams + Shadow = nightmare silhouette scout;
- Poison + Ink = toxic seal-script;
- Radiance + Guardian = shrine-lantern ward.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.exorcis:
### Exorcist's Mercy
You can remove a spirit without destroying it.
As an Action, target one creature, object, or location hosting a spirit within 30 feet.
Make a Cultivation Check against the spirit's Cultivation Save DC or the binder's DC.
On a success, choose one:
- suppress the Hosting Bond for 1 minute;
- force the spirit to manifest adjacent to the host;
- give the host Advantage on its next saving throw against possession;
- reduce the spirit's control over the host for 1 scene;
- remove one layer of a Binding Seal if the spirit wants to leave.
This talent does not work on a willing stable Covenant Bond unless the host also wants separation.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.great_s:
### Great Spirit Covenant
You may form a Covenant Bond with a Great Spirit, ancient spirit, local god, major ancestor, spirit sovereign's fragment, or similarly powerful entity.
The Great Spirit does not become a normal pet or companion.
Instead, choose one covenant benefit:
- you may call a lesser avatar as a Major Spirit Bond;
- you gain one powerful but limited Nature Expression;
- you gain access to a Shrine Anchor or sacred territory;
- you may ask one major question per long rest;
- you gain protection from lesser spirits of the same court;
- you can call on a spirit court during downtime;
- you may forge techniques from the Great Spirit's Nature.
A Great Spirit Covenant always includes at least one serious Oath and one serious Taboo.
Breaking the covenant may have campaign-level consequences.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.heaven_:
### Heaven-Sealing Binding
Forbidden
You can bind a powerful spirit into a long-term seal.
This requires:
- a defeated, willing, trapped, or ritually contained spirit;
- 1 hour of uninterrupted ritual work;
- a prepared vessel, shrine, formation, body, or object;
- an appropriate offering or coercive anchor;
- 7 CP;
- GM approval.
The spirit makes a saving throw with Advantage unless it is willing, already bound by its true Name, or weakened by a suitable story condition.
On a failure, the spirit is sealed into the vessel.
A Heaven-Sealing Binding may last indefinitely, but it is never casual. It creates enemies, spiritual debt, haunting pressure, social consequences, or future escape risks.
This talent exists because cultivation stories include wicked binders and sealed spirits. It is not assumed to be righteous.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.host_th:
### Host the Small God
You may create a Hosting Bond with a willing minor spirit or a spirit with which you have a Covenant Bond.
Choose one vessel:
- your body;
- a weapon;
- a piece of armor;
- a talisman;
- a mask;
- a tattoo;
- a scar;
- your shadow;
- an inner shrine;
- an animal companion;
- another willing creature.
While hosted, the spirit can communicate with the host and may provide one of the following benefits, chosen when the bond is formed:
- Advantage on one narrow type of check tied to its Nature once per short rest;
- resistance to one minor environmental discomfort tied to its Nature;
- the ability to perceive spirits of a similar Nature within 30 feet;
- a cosmetic or narrative manifestation;
- one body-bound simple Nature Expression.
A hosted spirit may still manifest outside the vessel if another talent allows it.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.hosted_:
### Hosted Battle Aspect
A hosted spirit can lend you a visible battle aspect.
As a Bonus Action, spend 1 CP and choose one hosted spirit.
For 1 minute, you gain one body-bound benefit based on the spirit's Nature:
- claws, horns, fangs, wings, roots, spectral arms, a tail, burning eyes, bark skin, blood markings, or similar cosmetic manifestation;
- Advantage on one type of check tied to the spirit's Nature;
- one minor movement mode appropriate to the Nature, such as climbing from a spider spirit or swimming from a river spirit;
- one natural weapon or weapon modification using the spirit's damage type or style;
- one self-only or touch-only Nature Expression.
If you use this aspect in a way the spirit hates, increase Bond Strain by 1.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.indepen:
### Independent Counsel
Your bonded spirit may advise you without consuming your action economy.
Once per short rest, when you make an ability check involving the spirit's Nature, you may add your Proficiency Bonus to the roll. If you already add Proficiency, add half your Proficiency Bonus instead.
Examples:
- a river spirit advising about currents;
- a sword spirit judging a blade;
- a corpse-lamp spirit identifying funerary rites;
- a fox spirit detecting social trickery;
- a dryad identifying jungle spirits;
- an ancestor warning about noble protocol.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.manifes:
### Manifest Spirit Domain
Your bonded spirit can temporarily impose a small domain shaped by its Nature.
Action Type: Action
Range: 60 feet, or the spirit's space
Area: 20-foot-radius field
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 3 CP
The field reflects the spirit's Nature.
Examples:
- a flower dryad creates red blooms, pollen, grasping roots, and qi-drinking petals;
- an ancestor-general creates a command tent of banners and ghostly soldiers;
- a river spirit creates flowing mist, slick stone, and murmuring current;
- a fox spirit creates deceptive lanterns and false paths;
- a sword spirit creates ringing sword-pressure;
- a plague spirit creates fever wind and crawling omens.
Choose one mechanical effect appropriate to the spirit's Nature:
- difficult terrain for enemies;
- light obscurement;
- allies gain Advantage on one narrow check;
- enemies have Disadvantage on one narrow check;
- a minor damage pulse once per round;
- a minor healing or temporary hit point pulse once per round;
- suppression of one spirit type;
- enhanced manifestation for the spirit;
- improved range for one Nature Expression.
The GM may require the effect to be built from the spirit's Nature Sphere talents.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.minor_s:
### Minor Spirit Agreements
You may maintain additional Minor Spirit Agreements equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
A Minor Spirit Agreement can provide one of the following noncombat benefits once per long rest each:
- a rumor from a place the spirit watches;
- a warning about an approaching creature type tied to its Nature;
- safe passage through a small territory;
- a minor omen;
- help finding a corpse, shrine, plant, object, or trail tied to its Nature;
- a small environmental favor;
- a harmless manifestation;
- a ritual assistant for one scene.
Minor Spirit Agreements cannot use combat actions, impose conditions, or create major sphere effects unless upgraded.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.ninefol:
### Ninefold Spirit Court
You can coordinate a court of spirits around your cultivation.
You may maintain up to three Major Spirit Bonds and a number of Minor Spirit Agreements equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus.
Once per long rest, as a 10-minute rite, you may call the court to perform one major noncombat service:
- protect a sect hall for a night;
- scout a valley through local spirits;
- guide refugees through haunted territory;
- identify the ruler of a spirit ecosystem;
- negotiate with a local god's attendants;
- gather spirit rumors across a city;
- suppress minor hauntings;
- prepare a battlefield shrine;
- carry an omen to an ally.
The service cannot replace a major adventure, defeat a major enemy, or solve a central problem without risk or cost.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.pact_br:
### Pact-Brother Battle Rhythm
When you and a Covenant spirit attack or act in harmony, the bond accelerates.
Once per round, when you damage a creature that your spirit damaged since the start of your last turn, or when your spirit damages a creature you damaged since the start of your last turn, choose one:
- reduce Bond Strain by 1 if the attack served the spirit's Nature;
- grant the next attack against that creature Advantage;
- move yourself or the spirit up to 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks;
- allow the spirit to Help you as a Reaction.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.shrine_:
### Shrine Anchor
You may anchor a bonded spirit to a prepared location.
Creating a Shrine Anchor takes 1 hour and appropriate offerings.
While within 1 mile of its Shrine Anchor, the spirit gains one of the following benefits:
- Advantage on checks to resist banishment or forced binding;
- one additional use of a limited Nature Expression per long rest;
- reduced Bond Strain after a long rest;
- increased manifestation duration;
- the ability to perceive intruders near the shrine.
A spirit can have only one Shrine Anchor from you at a time.
Destroying or desecrating the shrine increases Bond Strain by 2 and may wound the spirit.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.spirit_:
### Spirit Body
Your bonded spirit can create a more durable body.
Choose one Major Spirit Bond.
When it manifests, it gains one of the following benefits:
- additional Hit Points equal to twice your Cultivation Level;
- resistance to one damage type tied to its Nature;
- a fly, swim, climb, burrow, hover, or incorporeal movement mode appropriate to its Nature;
- the ability to interact with physical objects normally;
- the ability to squeeze through spaces as small as 1 inch if appropriate;
- immunity to one mundane environmental hazard tied to its Nature.
The spirit's body still remains vulnerable to effects that target spirits, souls, bindings, or its vessel.

### Spirit Court Command
When you use your Action to command a Major Spirit Bond, you may also command one Minor Spirit Agreement to perform a harmless or minor task.
If the Minor Spirit Agreement's task directly supports the Major Spirit's Nature Expression, the Major Spirit gains a small benefit chosen by the GM, such as:
- +1 to a check;
- 5 feet more range;
- a visible omen;
- Advantage on a noncombat part of the expression;
- a clearer manifestation;
- reduced collateral damage;
- a slight increase in duration.

### Spirit Domain: Court Between Breaths
You create a temporary domain where spirits can safely manifest and bargains become visible.
Action Type: Action
Range: Self
Area: 60-foot-radius aura
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Cost: 5 CP
For the duration:
- spirits in the area become visible unless hidden by a stronger effect;
- your bonded spirits can manifest without using an Action the first time they appear;
- hostile spirits have Disadvantage on checks to possess, hide inside, or flee through the area;
- Covenant spirits gain Advantage on saving throws against banishment;
- Binding Seals in the area visibly reveal their chains, terms, wounds, or pressure;
- you may communicate with any spirit in the area through Spirit Speech.
Once during the duration, you may command one bonded spirit to use a Spirit Nature Expression without spending your Bonus Action. You must still pay any CP cost.

### Spirit-Ridden Weapon
You may host a willing spirit in a weapon, shield, armor piece, implement, talisman, chain, mask, or other carried item.
While the spirit is hosted in the item, you may use Manifest the Spirit Nature through that item.
The expression must be item-bound unless the spirit manifests separately.
Examples:
- a sword spirit lending cutting pressure;
- a flower spirit blooming along a spear haft;
- a blood spirit drinking through a dagger;
- a storm spirit roaring from a war drum;
- an ancestor spirit guarding a shield;
- a fox spirit whispering through a mask.
Body Refiners often use this talent to keep spirit power legal as held-weapon or item-bound expression.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.true_na:
### True Name Mercy
You can use a true or partial Name to release instead of enslave.
When you know a spirit's true or partial Name and the spirit is bound, cursed, lost, maddened, or trapped, you may perform a 1-hour rite to call the spirit back to itself.
Make a Cultivation Check against the DC of the binding, curse, corruption, madness, or prison.
On a success, choose one:
- reduce the spirit's Bond Strain to 0;
- remove one coercive command;
- break one lesser Binding Seal;
- restore one lost memory;
- end one hostile possession;
- allow the spirit to pass on peacefully;
- transform a Binding Seal into a Covenant Bond if the spirit agrees.
This talent is one of the main orthodox answers to immoral spirit binding.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.unjust_:
### Unjust Chain Reversal
When you successfully use Break the Cruel Seal against a Binding Seal, you may turn the seal's pressure against the binder.
The binder makes a Wisdom saving throw.
On a failure, the binder suffers one of the following until the start of your next turn:
- cannot command the bound spirit;
- takes Psychic damage equal to your key ability modifier + Proficiency Bonus;
- has Disadvantage on the next check to maintain a spirit bond;
- loses access to one Binding Seal benefit;
- becomes visible to the spirit if hidden.

tianxia.talent.spirit_companions.world_r:
### World-Root Shrine
You create a permanent or semi-permanent sacred anchor for a spirit.
This requires downtime, materials, offerings, and GM approval.
A World-Root Shrine may anchor one Great Spirit Covenant, one spirit court, or one Major Spirit Bond of great importance.
While the shrine stands:
- the spirit is difficult to banish permanently;
- followers or allies may make offerings;
- local spirits recognize the covenant;
- the spirit's domain influence grows;
- the spirit may provide limited aid even when not traveling with you;
- enemies may attack the shrine to weaken the bond.
A World-Root Shrine is a story object, not just a buff.

tianxia.talent.stars.astral_survey:
#### Astral Survey
Tags: Survey, Anchor, Astral
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 10 minutes
Duration: Concentration, up to 10 minutes
Cost: 5 CP
Project awareness toward one active Star Anchor within 10 miles on the same plane. You perceive the area within 60 feet of that anchor as a dim starlit image.
You perceive:
major terrain;
bright light and darkness;
visible creatures;
visible structures;
celestial disturbances;
active portals or major spatial distortions.
Astral Survey does not automatically reveal invisible creatures, hidden rooms, secret techniques, thoughts, exact statistics, or things protected by stronger concealment.

tianxia.talent.stars.celestial_observato:
#### Celestial Observatory
Tags: Anchor, Survey, Strategic
Action Type: Strategic Project
Timing Detail: Project
Time: 30 days
Cost: 15 CP and 25,000 gp in crystal, star-metal, jade, mirrors, lenses, astronomical instruments, and observatory construction
Create a permanent celestial observatory. Choose three benefits:
Star Anchors last indefinitely within 10 miles of the observatory;
Stars talents cost 1 fewer CP once per turn nearby, minimum 1;
Divination, Space, Formations, and Stars projects gain +2 on relevant checks made through the observatory;
celestial disturbances become easier to notice;
long-distance navigation improves dramatically for designated sect members;
Constellation Road may connect permanent anchors maintained by the observatory;
one observatory chamber reveals supernatural distortion in the night sky;
Star Maps created inside update automatically;
warning constellations appear when major threats approach the observatory’s territory;
students studying Stars gain +2 on one relevant training check.
You may maintain a number of Celestial Observatories equal to your Proficiency Bonus unless the campaign treats them as sect infrastructure instead of personal projects.

tianxia.talent.stars.constellation_that_:
### Secret Inheritance - Constellation That Names the Unreachable
“Distance became an excuse. The stars had already written the path.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Star-Sovereign Incarnation, hidden primordial-constellation inheritance
Action Type: Action
Range: Special
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CPConcentration: Required
Use Limit: Once per week
Choose one creature, object, or location you can perceive through one of the following:
direct sight;
active Star Anchor;
Astral Survey;
Divination effect;
strong spiritual connection;
reliable celestial map;
a Star Anchor Network tied to the target’s region.
The target must remain on the same plane and within 10 miles unless a campaign-level observatory, star road, or Forged Technique expands this range.
A primordial constellation forms around the target.
#### Creature
An unwilling creature makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: For the duration:
the creature bears your Stellar Mark;
it cannot benefit from ordinary Invisible;
it cannot teleport;
it cannot Hide from you through ordinary concealment;
your Stars attacks may target it as though it were within normal range if no Total Cover, sealed chamber, dimensional barrier, or stronger Secret concealment blocks the line;
at the start of each of its turns, it takes 4d10 Radiant and 4d10 Force damage;
it repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.
Successful Initial Save: Until the start of your next turn, the creature bears your Stellar Mark, cannot teleport, and cannot benefit from ordinary Invisible against you.
#### Object or Location
You know its exact direction and approximate distance. You may create one temporary Star Anchor at that location if physically possible and if no stronger ward prevents it. The temporary anchor lasts until the Secret ends.
#### Limits
Constellation That Names the Unreachable does not:
bypass planar boundaries;
bypass Dimensional Locks;
bypass Total Cover automatically;
strike through entire mountains without a suitable Forged Technique;
reveal a target whose existence is protected by a stronger Secret concealment effect;
replace exploration, investigation, or travel entirely;
override GM-placed campaign mysteries without the correct narrative key.

tianxia.talent.stars.star_map:
#### Star Map
Tags: Survey, Anchor
Action Type: Ritual Procedure
Timing Detail: Ritual
Time: 10 minutes
Duration: 24 hours
Cost: 1 CP
Create a moving star map of one area you can observe, remember clearly, or study through a reliable map. The map may record:
major roads;
settlements;
mountain ridges;
rivers;
known Star Anchors;
known portals;
known dangerous regions;
approximate direction of celestial disturbances;
the direction of sunrise, sunset, and major visible constellations.
The map updates ordinary celestial orientation automatically.
Star Map does not reveal hidden locations, secret doors, unseen enemies, concealed portals, or unknown terrain beyond your knowledge.

tianxia.talent.stars.star_sovereign_inca:
#### Star-Sovereign Incarnation
Tags: Realm Evolution, Astral, Mark, Movement
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 15 CPConcentration: Not required
Use Limit: Once per long rest
You transform into a perfected stellar incarnation. Gain:
Fly Speed 80 feet and Hover;
+3 AC;
resistance to Radiant, Force, Cold, and Psychic damage;
Starbolt deals 6d10 Radiant, Force, or Cold damage;
Starpath Step range becomes 60 feet;
you may use Starpath Step once per turn without spending CP;
you know the direction of every creature bearing your Stellar Mark within 10 miles.
Sovereign Constellation. When an enemy starts its turn within 20 feet of you, it makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one effect:
it takes 4d8 Radiant, Force, or Cold damage;
apply Stellar Mark until the start of its next turn;
it cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
pull it 10 feet;
its Speed becomes 0 until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Apply Stellar Mark until the start of its next turn.
A creature is affected by Sovereign Constellation only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.stars.starpath_step:
#### Starpath Step
Tags: Line, Movement
Action Type: Bonus Action
Range: 20 feet
Cost: 1 CP
Move along a brief line of starlight to an unoccupied space you can see. This movement:
does not provoke Opportunity Attacks;
ignores nonmagical difficult terrain;
may carry you vertically up to 10 feet;
does not pass through solid barriers;
is rapid celestial movement, not teleportation.
Aligned Benefit: Increase the range by 10 feet.

tianxia.talent.stars.stars_domain:
#### Stars Domain - Court of the Celestial Compass
Tags: Domain, Mark, Ward, Realm Evolution
Action Type: Action
Area: 30-foot-radius aura centered on you
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 7 CPConcentration: Required
Constellations appear across the battlefield. Every direction is assigned a star.
You and Allies. You and allies you designate in the area gain:
+1 AC;
Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks;
the ability to ignore ordinary darkness penalties;
immunity to becoming lost or disoriented by ordinary means;
Advantage on saving throws against involuntary teleportation and forced planar movement;
once per turn, after hitting a creature bearing your Stellar Mark, the attacker may move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.
Enemies. Enemies in the area:
cannot benefit from ordinary Invisible against you;
have Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks;
treat terrain as difficult terrain while moving away from you or one of your Star Anchors;
are subject to the Compass Pulse.
Compass Pulse. When an enemy starts its turn inside the Domain, it makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: Choose one effect:
apply Stellar Mark until the start of its next turn;
it cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
it takes 2d8 Radiant, Force, or Cold damage;
pull it 10 feet toward one Star Anchor or point you choose;
reduce its Speed by 10 feet until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: Apply Stellar Mark until the start of its next turn.
A creature is affected by Compass Pulse only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.stars.world_beneath_the_c:
#### World Beneath the Constellations
Tags: Domain, Anchor, Astral
Action Type: Action
Range: 120 feet
Area: 60-foot-radius sphere
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 12 CPConcentration: Required
Use Limit: Once per long rest
A complete artificial night sky appears overhead.
Allies. You and allies you designate inside gain:
+2 AC;
Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks;
the ability to ignore ordinary darkness;
Advantage on saving throws against involuntary teleportation and forced planar movement;
once per turn, after hitting a marked enemy, the attacker may move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.
Enemies. Enemies inside:
cannot benefit from ordinary Invisible against you;
have Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks;
treat terrain as difficult terrain;
cannot teleport unless they succeed on a Charisma saving throw;
are struck by falling starlight.
When an enemy enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn inside, it makes a Charisma saving throw.
Failed Save: It takes 4d8 Radiant or Force damage and bears your Stellar Mark until the start of its next turn.
Successful Save: It takes half damage.
A creature takes this damage only once per turn.

tianxia.talent.talismans.formula_library:
#### Formula Library
Prerequisite: CL 10+
You maintain a personal formula library.
During a long rest, choose one formula family represented in your library. Until your next long rest, you gain one of the following benefits for formulae from that family:
reduce crafting DC by 1;
reduce CP spent during crafting by 1, minimum 0;
increase prepared talisman limit by 1 for that family only;
gain Advantage on Read the Script checks involving that family.

tianxia.talent.talismans.grand_sealing_a:
#### Grand Sealing Array - Array, Seal
Prerequisite: CL 10+, Formations sphere or a cooperating Formation cultivator
Your talismans can reinforce Formation projects and sect-grade site seals.
When contributing talismans to a Formation project, choose one benefit:
reduce construction time by 10 percent;
add +2 to one activation, concealment, repair, or stabilization check;
permit one triggered talisman effect when a Node, Gate, or Array Eye is attacked;
provide a written key that lets chosen creatures pass a Gate or ward;
create a failure warning visible to the formation keeper.
This does not let Talismans replace the Formations sphere’s project rules.

tianxia.talent.talismans.heavenly_seal:
#### Heavenly Seal - Seal
Prerequisite: CL 15+
You can create strategic seals protecting major locations or containing dangerous entities.
A Heavenly Seal may protect or bind:
vaults;
tombs;
compounds;
sect gates;
city districts;
spiritual veins;
sleeping monsters;
demons;
ghosts;
sealed inheritances;
forbidden scriptures.
A Heavenly Seal requires:
at least 30 days;
at least 10,000 gp in materials;
anchors;
maintenance procedures;
a defined weakness;
a written activation condition;
GM approval.
A Heavenly Seal is a project, not a normal combat action.

tianxia.talent.talismans.living_scriptur:
#### Living Scripture Servitor - Spirit
Prerequisite: CL 15+, Talisman Spirit
Your Talisman Spirit improves:
hit points become 10 x your Proficiency Bonus;
duration becomes 10 minutes;
it can carry up to three prepared talismans;
it can activate one carried talisman when you use a Bonus Action to command it;
you may communicate with it telepathically within 1 mile.
If the spirit carries a Secret talisman, it becomes visible to any creature with supernatural senses.

tianxia.talent.talismans.permanent_talis:
#### Permanent Talisman - Medium
Prerequisite: CL 10+, Reusable Talisman
You may create permanent jade, bone, or metal talismans storing Common, Uncommon, or Rare formulae.
Requirements:
30 days;
5,000 gp or more in materials;
10 CP spent during final stabilization;
one formula you know;
GM approval for campaign availability.
A permanent talisman has one charge and regains one charge at dawn, after cultivation, or under a formula-specific condition.
You may maintain a number of permanent talismans equal to your Proficiency Bonus.

tianxia.talent.talismans.talisman_affini:
#### Talisman Affinity
Choose one formula family.
When you craft a talisman from that family, choose one benefit:
+1 to its stored Save DC;
+1 to its stored Attack Modifier;
add your Proficiency Bonus to one healing roll;
reduce material cost by 20 percent;
reduce crafting time by 20 percent.
You may learn this talent multiple times, choosing a different formula family each time.

tianxia.talent.talismans.talisman_array:
#### Talisman Array - Array
Prerequisite: CL 5+
Setup
Time: 1 minute
Cost: 3 CP plus the talismans used
Area: 15-foot-radius circle
Place up to your Proficiency Bonus compatible talismans inside the area.
Choose one array mode.
Reinforced Effect: Use multiple talismans from the same family. When one activates, consume the supporting talismans to choose one benefit per supporting talisman:
+1 damage die;
+1 healing die;
radius +5 feet;
duration +1 round;
stored Save DC +1, maximum +2;
range +30 feet;
one target has Disadvantage on the first saving throw against the effect.
Layered Array: Use up to three compatible talismans from different families. When the array triggers, resolve each effect once in an order chosen when the array is built.
A Talisman Array is not a full Formation. It can be disabled by destroying or removing key talismans.

tianxia.talent.talismans.talisman_god_bo:
#### Talisman God Body - Realm Evolution
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Your intent can serve as brush and ink.
You gain the following benefits:
Advantage on Talisman Crafting Checks;
immunity to ordinary Common, Uncommon, and Rare talisman backlash from your own talismans;
automatic identification of Common, Uncommon, and Rare talismans you can clearly inspect;
you may use Emergency Stroke without brush or ink, writing with visible Qi;
PB times per long rest, you may use Emergency Stroke for a Common talisman without spending CP.
This does not remove material requirements for stable crafted talismans, jade slips, permanent talismans, or Secret formulae.

tianxia.talent.talismans.talisman_master:
#### Talisman Master’s Ink
You can brew spiritual ink during a short or long rest if you have appropriate materials.
While using your own spiritual ink:
gain Advantage on checks to identify inks, damaged inscriptions, forged seals, and cracked talismans;
reduce the material cost of Common talismans by 25 percent;
once per long rest, reroll a Talisman Crafting Check for a Common talisman.

tianxia.talent.talismans.talisman_spirit:
#### Talisman Spirit - Spirit
Prerequisite: CL 10+
Action Type: Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 6 CP
Target: one prepared talisman you crafted
You animate a talisman into a small talisman spirit.
The talisman spirit has:
AC 15;
hit points equal to 5 x your Proficiency Bonus;
Fly Speed 30 feet, hover;
immunity to Poisoned and Prone;
ability to carry one prepared talisman;
ability to activate the carried talisman using your action economy if you command it;
ability to take the Help action;
ability to retrieve unattended talismans.
It acts immediately after your turn. If reduced to 0 hit points, it is destroyed and the animated talisman is consumed.

tianxia.talent.verdant_growth.verdant_in:
### Verdant Incarnation: Body Becomes the Ancient Tree
Prerequisite: CL 15+
Action Type: Bonus Action
Duration: 1 minute
Cost: 6 CP
Use Limit: Once per long rest
Your body becomes a living scripture of bark, leaf, root, flower, and seed.
For the duration:
your reach with non-Projected Verdant Growth talents increases by 10 feet;
you count as a Living Medium for all your Verdant Growth talents;
you may create one Living Claim on your body at the start of each of your turns without spending an action;
you gain Resistance to Poison damage and Advantage on saving throws against Poisoned;
when a creature hits you with a melee attack, place 1 Growth Mark on it;
when you spend Growth Marks on Root, Bind, Shelter, Bloom, or Thorn, treat the number of marks spent as one higher, maximum +1 per response.
While this incarnation is active, Fire damage you take prevents you from gaining the free Living Claim at the start of your next turn.

tianxia.talent.warleader.breath_support:
### Breath Support - Shout
When you use a Shout, choose one of the following shapes:
normal 15-foot Emanation;
20-foot Cone;
30-foot Line that is 5 feet wide.
At CL 11+, increase the Cone to 30 feet and the Line to 60 feet.

tianxia.talent.warleader.call_attention:
### Call Attention - Shout
Use this Shout to draw hostile attention.
Until the start of your next turn:
affected allies gain Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks;
you automatically fail Dexterity (Stealth) checks;
the first enemy that targets an affected ally other than you with an attack roll does so with Disadvantage if it can see or hear you.

tianxia.talent.warleader.general_s_soul_:
### General’s Soul-Standard
Prerequisite: CL 15+
When you are reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright, you may expend Martial Focus and spend all Momentum Marks.
You remain conscious until the end of your next turn.
During this time:
you cannot gain Hit Points except from a feature that restores you from 0 Hit Points;
you may Set the Standard without spending a Bonus Action;
you may use one Command Response without spending Momentum;
if you are still at 0 Hit Points at the end of your next turn, you fall Unconscious normally.
Use General’s Soul-Standard once per long rest.

tianxia.talent.warleader.imperial_mandat:
### Imperial Mandate of the Living Line
Prerequisite: Court of Moving Banners, CL 15+
While Court of Moving Banners is active:
Commanded allies are immune to Frightened while they can see or hear you;
once per round, when a Commanded ally fails a saving throw, use a Command Response without spending Momentum;
when you use Step on My Count, the ally moves 10 feet instead of 5 feet;
when you use Strike on My Count, add twice your Proficiency Bonus to the damage instead of your Proficiency Bonus.

tianxia.talent.weapons.court_of_ten_thou:
### Court of Ten Thousand Weapons
Action Type: Bonus Action
Cost: Expend Martial Focus and 5 CP or Stamina, depending on Path expression
Duration: Concentration, up to 1 minute
Area: 20-foot aura centered on you
You establish a weapon court where every tool has a correct answer.
While the court lasts:
- you may apply one minor Weapon Method per turn without using your once-per-turn Weapon Method limit;
- you may draw or stow one additional weapon each turn;
- enemies in the aura have Disadvantage on checks made to disarm you;
- when an enemy in the aura misses you with a melee attack, you may move 5 feet or change weapon grip;
- once per round, when you reduce a creature's speed, prevent a reaction, or break a guard with a Weapon Method, you may regain Martial Focus.
This court is martial discipline, not external qi projection unless the character's Path expression makes it qi-shaped.

tianxia.talent.yang.the_completed_action:
### Secret Inheritance - The Completed Action Beneath Heaven
“You began. Heaven will not permit you to remain unfinished.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Yang Domain, secret solar scripture or forbidden furnace inheritance
Action Type: Reaction
Range: 120 feet
Cost: 18 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
Saving Throw: Constitution if the source is unwilling
Trigger: A creature, object, Barrier, Formation, Domain, spell, sphere talent, forged technique, monster action, cultivation ability, or supernatural event you can perceive begins to produce a consequence.
You declare that the consequence must complete itself beneath Heaven.
If the source is willing or the triggering event is your own effect, choose one consequence of the event. That consequence becomes complete:
one damage roll is maximized for one target;
one healing or Temporary Hit Point effect is maximized for one target;
one teleportation, movement, or forced movement effect reaches its intended legal destination despite lower-Realm reduction;
one condition-removal effect removes the condition from one target despite lower-Realm suppression;
one Barrier, Domain, Formation, summoned creature, or created object appears with full normal Hit Points and duration despite lower-Realm weakening;
one revealing effect pierces lower-Realm darkness, concealment, or illusion for one target;
one spoken command, oath, kiai, mantra, or declaration reaches all intended legal listeners within range despite lower-Realm silence or muffling.
If the source is unwilling, the source makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the event completes with forbidden surplus. Choose one consequence:
the source takes 12d10 Fire, Radiant, or Force damage after the event resolves;
the source cannot benefit from being Hidden, Invisible, or magically concealed until the end of your next turn;
the source cannot use the same named spell, talent, monster action, forged technique, or cultivation ability again until the end of its next turn;
a created Barrier, Domain, Formation effect, summon, or object appears overbright and unstable, losing half its Hit Points or duration after its first turn or first activation;
one resource the source spent becomes visible as spiritual expenditure, allowing you to learn whether it used CP, a spell slot, charges, a limited use, or an external patron.
On a successful save, the event completes normally, but the source gains a Rising Mark that lasts for 1 minute, and you may immediately spend that mark without counting against your once-per-round limit.
The Completed Action Beneath Heaven cannot force a plot-level miracle, override superior Realm law by default, compel a god, restore a destroyed soul, or guarantee a whole scene outcome. Against artifacts, divine interventions, Realm-defining Domains, Secret Inheritances, and superior cultivation-scale effects, the GM may reduce the failed-save result to partial completion or dangerous overcompletion rather than full effect.
This inheritance is forbidden because it proves that incompletion is not safety.

tianxia.talent.yin.the_unfinished_action:
### Secret Inheritance - The Unfinished Action Beneath Heaven
“You may begin. Heaven is not required to let you finish.”
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Yin Domain, hidden Yin scripture or forbidden lunar inheritance
Action Type: Reaction
Range: 120 feet
Cost: 18 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
Saving Throw: Wisdom
Trigger: A creature, object, Barrier, Formation, Domain, spell, sphere talent, forged technique, monster action, cultivation ability, or supernatural event you can perceive begins to produce a consequence.
You declare that the action has begun to return to stillness before it fully enters the world. The source of the triggering event makes a Wisdom saving throw. If the source is not a creature, use the creator’s Cultivation Save DC, spell save DC, Formation DC, item DC, or an appropriate GM-assigned DC.
On a failed save, choose one consequence of the event. That consequence becomes incomplete:
damage from the event is reduced to 0 for one target;
healing from the event is reduced to 0 for one target;
teleportation or planar travel from the event fails for one target;
a condition the event would end does not end for one target;
a condition the event would impose lasts only until the start of the affected creature’s next turn;
a Barrier, Domain, or Formation created by the event appears with half its normal Hit Points, radius, or duration;
a summoned or created creature appears with half its normal Hit Points and cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn;
a resource recovery effect restores nothing to one target;
a declaration, oath, command, or spoken technique reaches only creatures within 10 feet of the speaker.
On a successful save, the event completes, but its source gains a Waning Mark that lasts for 1 minute, and you may immediately spend that mark without counting against your once-per-round limit.
The Unfinished Action Beneath Heaven cannot erase a whole scene, undo past events, negate an entire Secret Inheritance, or cancel a higher-Realm mandate by default. Against artifacts, divine interventions, Realm-defining Domains, superior cultivation-scale effects, and plot-level calamities, the GM may reduce the failed-save result to a partial weakening instead of full incompletion.
This inheritance is forbidden because it proves that completion is not guaranteed.

tianxia.tradition.spirit.echo_scribe.fea:
### CL18 — Chronicle of the Living Soul

You open a living record in which the next moments become editable before they harden into history.

**Action**  
**Cost:** 10 Resonance  
**Duration:** The scene

Manifest a **Living Chronicle** containing pages, floating script, carved tablets, or remembered verses. Choose up to your Proficiency Bonus creatures you can perceive. Each becomes a **Recorded Soul** for the duration.

When a Recorded Soul experiences one of the following events, you may record it as a **Living Entry** without using an action:

- succeeds or fails an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw;
- fails a death saving throw;
- is reduced to 0 Hit Points;
- becomes Charmed, Frightened, possessed, spiritually transformed, or identity-wounded;
- loses Concentration;
- has a Soul Anchor, Cultivation Asset, spiritual bond, or companion bond suppressed;
- willingly makes a defining vow, confession, sacrifice, or betrayal.

You can maintain a number of Living Entries equal to your Proficiency Bonus. Recording beyond the maximum erases the oldest Living Entry.

#### Rewrite the Margin

Once on each of your turns, you may spend 4 Resonance and consume one relevant Living Entry to rewrite the recorded event into one lesser result:

- erase one failed death saving throw;
- reduce damage that reduced the creature to 0 Hit Points by `2 × Spirit Awakening CL`, potentially leaving it above 0;
- suppress one Charmed, Frightened, possession, ordinary transformation, or identity-wound expression until the end of the creature’s next turn;
- restore Concentration if the creature has not begun another Concentration effect and the original effect’s duration has not expired;
- allow the creature to reroll the recorded Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw with Advantage;
- convert a recorded betrayal, confession, or vow into undeniable spiritual evidence without changing whether it occurred.

Against an ordinary lower-Source-CL effect, the rewrite applies as printed. Against equal or higher, Rare, Forbidden, Secret, divine, artifact, tribulation, Foundation, Method, bloodline, true-name, reincarnation, or campaign-scale authority, make a Cultivation Check. On failure, the Entry is not consumed, but the rewrite does not occur and you learn one required recovery or counterprocedure.

#### Chronicle Asset

You may externalize the Chronicle as a Medium Cultivation Asset in an adjacent space:

- **AC:** your Cultivation Save DC
- **Hit Points:** `8 × Proficiency Bonus`
- **Saving Throws:** uses your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throw bonuses
- **Resistances:** Psychic damage
- **Source CL:** your effective Spirit Awakening CL

While externalized, you may originate Echo Scribe features from it. If destroyed, every unused Living Entry is lost and the activation ends. If kept internal, it cannot be targeted separately but every use of Rewrite the Margin costs 1 additional Resonance.

Chronicle of the Living Soul edits recent spiritual consequence, not settled history. It cannot undo an event after the scene meaningfully changes, resurrect someone whose death is no longer current, restore resources spent before the recorded event, duplicate consumed items, reverse a breakthrough, erase consent, or rewrite the campaign’s past.

---

tianxia.tradition.spirit.knot_weaver.fea:
### CL6 — Tie the Moment

**Reaction**  
**Trigger:** A Resonance Marked creature within 60 feet involved in an Observed Tie makes an attack roll, saving throw, or ability check, or willingly moves 10 feet or more  
**Cost:** 3 Resonance or 1 Knot Tension

Declare the tug before the outcome is finalized. Choose one:

- subtract `1d6` from the triggering attack roll or saving throw;
- reduce the triggering movement by 10 feet;
- deny Advantage granted by the other side of the Observed Tie on the triggering roll;
- if the triggering creature moved away from the other side, pull it 5 feet back after its movement resolves;
- if it targeted the other side with a hostile effect, impose one ordinary Spiritual Pressure effect after the effect resolves.

Tie the Moment cannot reverse an already resolved event, create an attack target that was illegal at declaration, or force a creature to spend an additional limited resource.

#### Counter-Tug

An equal- or higher-Source-CL target may spend its Reaction to make a Charisma saving throw. On success, reduce the numerical adjustment by half or ignore the forced movement. This does not refund your cost.

### CL3 — The Last Inch

You gain Spirit-Touch Unarmed Strike and Handspan Subject.

#### Handspan Reach

Your Spirit-Touch Unarmed Strikes have 10-foot reach against your Handspan Subject. This reach is spiritual contact:

- it requires line of effect;
- it cannot pass through total cover or a sealed boundary;
- it cannot deliver a Grapple, Shove, item, poison, bodily secretion, or touch-range feature unless that feature expressly permits spiritual delivery;
- it does not threaten every space within 10 feet for opportunity attacks; you can make an opportunity attack at that reach only against your Handspan Subject.

#### Last-Inch Step

**Reaction**  
**Trigger:** Your Handspan Subject within 15 feet enters your reach, leaves your reach, or attempts to pass through your space  
**Limit:** Once per round

Move 5 feet to a legal space without provoking opportunity attacks from the subject. Then choose one:

- remain adjacent to it if a legal space exists;
- increase your distance from it by 5 feet;
- exchange which side of it you occupy without entering its space;
- impose Heavy Soul or Stilled Intent as Spiritual Pressure until the start of its next turn if it bears your Resonance Mark.

Last-Inch Step cannot escape an existing Grapple or Restrained effect and cannot cross a barrier.

#### Contact Reveals Disturbance

When a Spirit-Touch Unarmed Strike damages your Handspan Subject, you learn whether it is currently affected by ordinary possession, a curse, a Heart Demon, spiritual contamination, an external controlling link, or a disguised spirit-body relation. This reveals only the category, not the source or cure.

tianxia.tradition.spirit.soulstring_danc:
### CL14 — Dance of Borrowed Limbs

**Action**  
**Range:** 60 feet  
**Cost:** 6 Resonance  
**Concentration:** Required, up to 1 minute  
**Requirement:** The target bears at least two Choreography Strings

The target makes a Wisdom saving throw.

**Failed Save:** Consume one String. At the start of each of the target’s turns, choose one command:

- lose 10 feet of Speed;
- drop one held object that is not soul-bound or inseparably attached;
- move up to 10 feet along a legal path;
- fall Prone;
- make one weapon attack at Disadvantage against a legal target you choose within reach;
- spend its Reaction making a harmless involuntary gesture, step, or guard motion;
- speak or remain silent for one brief phrase, provided this does not compel protected information or a lie the creature cannot formulate.

The target repeats the save at the end of each turn, ending the feature on a success. Each successful save removes one remaining Choreography String.

**Successful Initial Save:** The feature does not take hold. The target suffers one ordinary Spiritual Pressure effect, and you do not consume a String.

#### Control Boundary

Dance of Borrowed Limbs cannot force direct self-destruction, activate Legendary, Secret, divine, artifact, tribulation, or limited-use powers, spend the target’s cultivation resources, alter its memories, or compel it to reveal unknown or protected information.

A substantially lower-Source-CL ordinary creature can be forced to repeat harmless choreography without further saves after three failed saves during the same activation, but hostile attacks, self-endangerment, and major actions always preserve the saving throw procedure.

### CL6 — Stolen Rhythm

**Bonus Action**  
**Range:** 60 feet  
**Cost:** 3 Resonance  
**Requirement:** The target bears at least one Choreography String

The target makes a Wisdom saving throw.

**Failed Save:** Consume one String and choose two effects until the start of your next turn:

- Speed reduced by 10 feet;
- cannot take Reactions;
- Disadvantage on the next weapon attack;
- cannot benefit from Advantage created by an ally’s Help;
- must spend 5 additional feet of movement to stand from Prone or change elevation;
- cannot take the same movement mode twice during the turn, such as teleporting twice or flying after walking.

**Successful Save:** Do not consume the String. Choose one effect from the list.

#### Catch the Beat

If the target fails while bearing three Strings, you may instead consume all three to make its Speed 0 until the start of your next turn. It can still teleport or be moved by another source unless that source also fails a Source CL contest against you.

tianxia.tradition.spirit.well_of_hours.f:
### CL6 — Borrowed Second

You pull a small act from the next breath and spend it now.

**Bonus Action**  
**Cost:** 3 Resonance  
**Limit:** Once per turn

Choose one option:

- move up to half your Speed without provoking opportunity attacks;
- stand from Prone and move up to 10 feet;
- draw, stow, pick up, hand off, open, close, or manipulate one ordinary object;
- use Spiritual Sense or Soul Gaze;
- take the Disengage or Search action;
- make one attack with a weapon you are already proficient with against a creature bearing your Resonance Mark and within the weapon’s normal reach or range;
- use Mind Spike against a creature bearing your Resonance Mark, reducing its damage by one die, to a minimum of one die.

The ordinary options create 1 Time Debt. The weapon-attack and Mind Spike options create 2 Time Debt.

Borrowed Second cannot:

- activate a Domain;
- activate a CL10-or-higher Subpath feature;
- activate Soul Vessel, Soul Splitting, or another feature that creates a separately acting Asset;
- activate a full multi-packet Forged Technique;
- activate an item power limited to once per scene or less often;
- activate another feature whose primary effect is to grant an additional Action, Bonus Action, Reaction, or turn;
- be used during a turn granted by another extra-turn effect.

#### Pay the Second Back

At the start of your turn, before moving, taking an Action or Bonus Action, or using a Reaction, you may choose to pay the current.

Until the start of your next turn:

- your Speed becomes 0;
- you cannot take Reactions;
- you cannot voluntarily move, teleport, spiritually step, conceptually translate, or activate a Source Rule whose primary effect moves you;
- you cannot use Borrowed Second.

Then remove 2 Time Debt. Involuntary movement does not cancel this payment and does not restore your ability to move voluntarily.

This declaration occurs before the turn’s actions and cannot be made after you have already benefited from movement, a Reaction, or another Well of Hours feature during that turn.

---

### CL14 — Refuse the Moment

You place one consequence beside the present and demand that it wait.

**Reaction**  
**Trigger:** You or a creature you can perceive within 30 feet would take damage, gain a condition from a failed saving throw, be forcibly moved, become Grappled or Restrained, become Unconscious, or be reduced to 0 Hit Points by a non-damage effect  
**Cost:** 6 Resonance  
**Time Debt:** 2  
**Delay:** Until the end of the protected creature’s next turn

Defer one discrete consequence of the triggering event. Valid examples include:

- all damage from one attack, technique packet, hazard pulse, or fall;
- one condition, command, possession impulse, or other discrete effect caused by the failed save;
- one instance of forced movement;
- one Grappled or Restrained condition;
- becoming Unconscious;
- being set or reduced to 0 Hit Points by an effect that does not deal damage.

Record the consequence using the Deferred Consequence procedures. The deferred consequence arrives at the end of the protected creature’s next turn unless it has been answered before then.

You can maintain only one Deferred Consequence from Well of Hours at a time. Creating another releases the first immediately before the new consequence is deferred.

#### Authority Limits

Refuse the Moment automatically delays an ordinary, Open, Restricted, or equal-Source-CL consequence when all other requirements are met.

A Rare, Forbidden, Secret, divine, artifact, heavenly-law, Foundation-breaking, Method-breaking, permanent, soul-consuming, or explicitly outside-time consequence requires a Cultivation Check against the originating Source Rule.

On a failed contest:

- the consequence is not delayed;
- the Resonance is spent;
- you gain only 1 Time Debt instead of 2.

Refuse the Moment cannot:

- restore a creature already dead before the trigger;
- undo a completed severance, destroyed Asset, broken Foundation, or consumed soul;
- reverse an event whose Source Rule resolves outside time;
- restore an action, resource, charge, item, or opportunity already spent.

#### Soul Splitting — Hold This Breath

When an ally within 30 feet of your soul fragment takes damage, the fragment can use its Subpath Fragment action and spend 2 Resonance from you to defer up to `2d8 + Wisdom modifier` of that damage until the end of that ally’s turn.

This does not use your Reaction, but it creates 1 Time Debt and still counts against the limit of one Deferred Consequence from Well of Hours. If you are already at maximum Time Debt, the Hour Comes Due normally at the start of your next turn.

---
